 vomiting","Fever","Pain worsened by movement or cough"],"physicalSigns":["Right lower quadrant tenderness","Localized guarding","Pain with movement or cough","Possible fever and tachycardia","Variable findings in pregnancy, older adults, and children"],"redFlags":["Generalized peritonitis","Hemodynamic instability or sepsis","Rigid abdomen","Rapidly worsening pain or systemic illness","Pregnancy/immunosuppression with concerning symptoms"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Ectopic pregnancy","distinguishingFeatures":"Possible pregnancy, pelvic pain, vaginal bleeding, or instability."},{"condition":"Ovarian torsion","distinguishingFeatures":"Acute unilateral pelvic pain with supportive adnexal imaging."},{"condition":"Renal/ureteric colic","distinguishingFeatures":"Colicky flank-to-groin pain and possible hematuria."},{"condition":"Gastroenteritis/mesenteric adenitis","distinguishingFeatures":"Diarrhea or diffuse symptoms may predominate; serial examination helps distinguish."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial focused abdominal examination","modalityTarget":"Serial focused abdominal examination — Appendicitis or peritoneal irritation","targetCondition":"Appendicitis or peritoneal irritation","expectedFinding":"Persistent or evolving focal tenderness, guarding, or movement pain.","clinicalRationale":"Clinical course and serial findings support diagnosis."},{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"Ultrasound or CT selected by age, pregnancy, and local protocol","modalityTarget":"Ultrasound or CT selected by age, pregnancy, and local protocol — Appendicitis","targetCondition":"Appendicitis","expectedFinding":"Imaging consistent with inflamed appendix or complication.","clinicalRationale":"Clarifies uncertain presentations and identifies complications."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Urinalysis","modalityTarget":"Urinalysis — Urinary infection or calculus","targetCondition":"Urinary infection or calculus","expectedFinding":"No findings sufficient to explain symptoms when urinary disease is unlikely.","clinicalRationale":"Assesses common mimics but does not independently exclude appendicitis."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Pregnancy test when relevant","modalityTarget":"Pregnancy test when relevant — Pregnancy-related abdominal pain","targetCondition":"Pregnancy-related abdominal pain","expectedFinding":"Negative when pregnancy is excluded.","clinicalRationale":"Informs differential, imaging, and gynecologic urgency."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Arrange prompt surgical assessment, analgesia and fluid support according to clinical need.","Discuss operative care or selected nonoperative care with the surgical team; document selection criteria and recurrence risk."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"efbb5ffe-dff2-4cd7-8a28-e7cedeb03067","title":"Appendicitis Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Emergency Department Care, Nonsurgical Treatment","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/773895-treatment","locator":"Emergency Department Care; Nonsurgical Treatment","primary_source":true},{"id":"1919c9db-1113-438a-8a27-9a074856e244","title":"WSES Jerusalem guidelines: acute appendicitis","i