nforms differential, imaging, and gynecologic urgency.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"efbb5ffe-dff2-4cd7-8a28-e7cedeb03067","title":"Appendicitis Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Emergency Department Care, Nonsurgical Treatment","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/773895-treatment","locator":"Emergency Department Care; Nonsurgical Treatment","primary_source":true},{"id":"1919c9db-1113-438a-8a27-9a074856e244","title":"WSES Jerusalem guidelines: acute appendicitis","issuer":"Other","edition":"2020","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7386163/","locator":"Recommendations 1.1, 1.10, 3.1 and 7.1","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult assessment and surgical referral only; reconcile the 2025 WSES guideline before approving a definitive antibiotic or operative protocol. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Arrange prompt surgical assessment, analgesia and fluid support according to clinical need.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Discuss operative care or selected nonoperative care with the surgical team; document selection criteria and recurrence risk.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"efbb5ffe-dff2-4cd7-8a28-e7cedeb03067","title":"Appendicitis Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Emergency Department Care, Nonsurgical Treatment","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/773895-treatment","locator":"Emergency Department Care; Nonsurgical Treatment","primary_source":true},{"id":"1919c9db-1113-438a-8a27-9a074856e244","title":"WSES Jerusalem guidelines: acute appendicitis","issuer":"Other","edition":"2020","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7386163/","locator":"Recommendations 1.1, 1.10, 3.1 and 7.1","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult assessment and surgical referral only; reconcile the 2025 WSES guideline before approving a definitive antibiotic or operative protocol. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain that symptoms can evolve and reassessment may be needed.","Review warning symptoms requiring immediate return."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Follow fasting instructions while surgery is considered.","Resume oral intake per treating-team advice."],"mdtReferrals":["General surgery","Obstetrics and gynecology if relevant","Radiology for uncertain or complex cases"],"dischargeCriteria":["Serious surgical and pregnancy-related causes assessed","Stable observations and manageable symptoms","Follow-up or observation plan documented","Immediate return precautions understood"],"followUpPlan":"If discharged, arrange follow-up by working diagnosis and advise immediate return for worsening or persistent symptoms."}}},{"guideline_id":"83aa7315-9778-4b3a-93a8-edcac20d7c58","original_version_ids":["65f56724-d1f6-4afb-802a-e9cc952df2c2","ef384c63-715a-4154-89a5-349fce37618e"],"source_title":"Small-Bowel Obstruction Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Surgical Care","source_url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/774140-treatment","issuer":"Other","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"83aa7315-9778-4b3a-93a8-edcac20d7c58","title":"Acute Bowel Obstruction","specialty":"Acute Care Surgery / Emergency Medicine","authority":"Other","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Small-bowel obstruction only; do not generalise adhesive-obstruction observation thresholds to all bowel obstruction.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","Small-bowel obstruction only; do not generalise adhesive-obstruction observation thresholds to all bowel obstruction.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"limited-comparison","originalVersionIds":["65f56724-d1f6-4afb-802a-e9cc952df2c2","ef384c63-715a-4154-89a5-349fce37618e"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"A mechanical blockage or dysmotility causes proximal dilation and fluid sequestration. A closed-loop obstruction can compromise venous and arterial supply, leading to ischaemia, necrosis, and perforation. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["A mechanical blockage or dysmotility causes proximal dilation and fluid sequestration. A closed-loop obstruction can compromise venous and arterial supply, leading to ischaemia, necrosis, and perforation.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Acute Bowel Obstruction, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Continuous severe pain or peritonism","Shock, fever with toxicity, or metabolic acidosis","Strangulated hernia","Free air or suspected bowel ischaemia"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Ileus","distinguishingFeatures":"Diffuse bowel dilation without a mechanical transition; consider medicines and recent illness/surgery."},{"condition":"Gastroenteritis","distinguishingFeatures":"Diarrhoea and absence of progressive distension may support an alternative."},{"condition":"Mesenteric ischaemia or perforation","distinguishingFeatures":"Pain out of proportion or peritonism requires emergency action."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"CBC, electrolytes, renal function and lactate when ischaemia is suspected; pregnancy test where relevant.","modalityTarget":"CBC, electrolytes, renal function and lactate when ischaemia is suspected; pregnancy test where relevant. — Acute Bowel Obstruction","targetCondition":"Acute Bowel Obstruction","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Abdominal imaging selected with surgical input to define level, transition, closed loop, ischaemia, or perforation.","modalityTarget":"Abdominal imaging selected with surgical input to define level, transition, closed loop, ischaemia, or perforation. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Bowel Obstruction","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Bowel Obstruction","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Acute Bowel Obstruction","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Acute Bowel Obstruction","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Obtain early surgical review and assess for peritonitis, strangulation or ischaemia.","Use bowel rest, intravenous fluid and electrolyte correction and indicated decompression; deterioration requires urgent reassessment for surgery."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"777f11ff-c482-411e-809f-022500cfb067","title":"Small-Bowel Obstruction Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Surgical Care","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/774140-treatment","locator":"Approach Considerations; Surgical Care","primary_source":true},{"id":"51328a5d-b61c-490a-824d-bed228dbfcfd","title":"WSES Bologna guidelines: adhesive small bowel obstruction","issuer":"Other","edition":"2017 update, published 2018","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6006983/","locator":"Diagnosis; CT scans; Non-operative management","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Small-bowel obstruction only; do not generalise adhesive-obstruction observation thresholds to all bowel obstruction. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"CBC, electrolytes, renal function and lactate when ischaemia is suspected; pregnancy test where relevant.","clinical_question":"Acute Bowel Obstruction","expected_finding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Abdominal imaging selected with surgical input to define level, transition, closed loop, ischaemia, or perforation.","clinical_question":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Bowel Obstruction","expected_finding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","clinical_question":"Important alternative to Acute Bowel Obstruction","expected_finding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","clinical_question":"Progression or evolving complication","expected_finding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"777f11ff-c482-411e-809f-022500cfb067","title":"Small-Bowel Obstruction Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Surgical Care","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/774140-treatment","locator":"Approach Considerations; Surgical Care","primary_source":true},{"id":"51328a5d-b61c-490a-824d-bed228dbfcfd","title":"WSES Bologna guidelines: adhesive small bowel obstruction","issuer":"Other","edition":"2017 update, published 2018","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6006983/","locator":"Diagnosis; CT scans; Non-operative management","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Small-bowel obstruction only; do not generalise adhesive-obstruction observation thresholds to all bowel obstruction. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Obtain early surgical review and assess for peritonitis, strangulation or ischaemia.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use bowel rest, intravenous fluid and electrolyte correction and indicated decompression; deterioration requires urgent reassessment for surgery.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"777f11ff-c482-411e-809f-022500cfb067","title":"Small-Bowel Obstruction Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Surgical Care","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/774140-treatment","locator":"Approach Considerations; Surgical Care","primary_source":true},{"id":"51328a5d-b61c-490a-824d-bed228dbfcfd","title":"WSES Bologna guidelines: adhesive small bowel obstruction","issuer":"Other","edition":"2017 update, published 2018","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6006983/","locator":"Diagnosis; CT scans; Non-operative management","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Small-bowel obstruction only; do not generalise adhesive-obstruction observation thresholds to all bowel obstruction. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain acute bowel obstruction in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Acute Care Surgery / Emergency Medicine","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"c2c404f2-5f47-4e4d-9ce7-fb32a9c1e103","original_version_ids":["e9897fcf-3ca4-49bd-a6fa-4a1b0ce6721c","448029d6-ef84-4ff0-81ab-30f6a47af751"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng185/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"c2c404f2-5f47-4e4d-9ce7-fb32a9c1e103","title":"Acute Coronary Syndrome","specialty":"Emergency Medicine and Cardiology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult ACS; NICE and US ACS prescribing branches must remain separate. Full antithrombotic, renal and bleeding-risk reconciliation remains pending.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Adult ACS; NICE and US ACS prescribing branches must remain separate. Full antithrombotic, renal and bleeding-risk reconciliation remains pending.","US loading doses and anticoagulant options must not be labelled a universal NICE regimen; bleeding, reperfusion, renal and pretreatment branches are required."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"limited-comparison","originalVersionIds":["e9897fcf-3ca4-49bd-a6fa-4a1b0ce6721c","448029d6-ef84-4ff0-81ab-30f6a47af751"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Acute reduction in coronary blood flow, commonly from plaque disruption and thrombosis, causes myocardial ischemia and may cause infarction.","keyMechanisms":["Atherosclerotic plaque disruption","Platelet activation and coronary thrombosis","Myocardial oxygen supply-demand imbalance","Myocardial necrosis if ischemia persists"]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Chest pressure, tightness, heaviness, or pain","Discomfort to arm, jaw, back, neck, or upper abdomen","Shortness of breath","Nausea, vomiting, or sweating","Fatigue, lightheadedness, or syncope"],"physicalSigns":["Diaphoresis or pallor","Tachycardia, bradycardia, or arrhythmia","Hypotension or hypertension","Signs of acute heart failure","Examination may be normal"],"redFlags":["Persistent or recurrent ischemic pain","High-risk ECG changes","Hemodynamic instability","Pulmonary edema or cardiogenic shock","Cardiac arrest or malignant arrhythmia"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Aortic dissection","distinguishingFeatures":"Abrupt severe pain, pulse/BP asymmetry, neurologic deficit, or aortic regurgitation."},{"condition":"Pulmonary embolism","distinguishingFeatures":"Pleuritic pain, unexplained hypoxemia/tachycardia, and VTE risk."},{"condition":"Pericarditis","distinguishingFeatures":"Often positional or pleuritic pain with characteristic ECG changes."},{"condition":"Gastroesophageal or musculoskeletal pain","distinguishingFeatures":"Meal-related, positional, or reproducible features do not alone exclude ACS."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"12-lead ECG repeated when symptoms persist/evolve","modalityTarget":"12-lead ECG repeated when symptoms persist/evolve — ACS","targetCondition":"ACS","expectedFinding":"Possible ST elevation, ischemic ST depression, T-wave inversion, or dynamic changes.","clinicalRationale":"Rapid interpretation guides reperfusion and risk management."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial high-sensitivity troponin using local pathway","modalityTarget":"Serial high-sensitivity troponin using local pathway — Acute myocardial injury","targetCondition":"Acute myocardial injury","expectedFinding":"Rise/fall with a value above assay threshold in clinical context.","clinicalRationale":"Supports diagnosis and risk assessment with symptoms and ECG."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Serial ECG and troponin pathway","modalityTarget":"Serial ECG and troponin pathway — Acute MI","targetCondition":"Acute MI","expectedFinding":"No evolving ischemic ECG or significant troponin change by validated pathway.","clinicalRationale":"A single normal ECG or early troponin does not exclude ACS."},{"tier":"firstLineImaging","testName":"Chest radiograph when indicated","modalityTarget":"Chest radiograph when indicated — Alternative thoracic cause or complication","targetCondition":"Alternative thoracic cause or complication","expectedFinding":"No evident pneumothorax, major edema, or other thoracic cause.","clinicalRationale":"Assesses selected mimics but does not rule out ACS."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Give a single 300 mg aspirin loading dose when indicated and not contraindicated under the NICE ACS pathway.","Activate reperfusion assessment for STEMI; use a bleeding-risk and coronary-strategy-specific antithrombotic plan for NSTEMI rather than a universal P2Y12 or heparin regimen."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8480c808-16c0-4d9c-8fb3-1d9c5547909f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng185/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1 STEMI; 1.2 NSTEMI and unstable angina","primary_source":true},{"id":"2ea5fc8d-8db7-4946-8f71-0bce734f789f","title":"Acute Coronary Syndrome Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Pharmacologic Anti-ischemic Therapy, Pharmacologic Antithrombotic Therapy","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public Medscape page retrieved 11 October 2026; limited secondary comparison","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1910735-treatment","locator":"Treatment and Management; detailed prescribing not reconciled","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult ACS; NICE and US ACS prescribing branches must remain separate. Full antithrombotic, renal and bleeding-risk reconciliation remains pending. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"12-lead ECG repeated when symptoms persist/evolve","clinical_question":"ACS","expected_finding":"Possible ST elevation, ischemic ST depression, T-wave inversion, or dynamic changes.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Rapid interpretation guides reperfusion and risk management.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Serial high-sensitivity troponin using local pathway","clinical_question":"Acute myocardial injury","expected_finding":"Rise/fall with a value above assay threshold in clinical context.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports diagnosis and risk assessment with symptoms and ECG.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Serial ECG and troponin pathway","clinical_question":"Acute MI","expected_finding":"No evolving ischemic ECG or significant troponin change by validated pathway.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: A single normal ECG or early troponin does not exclude ACS.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Chest radiograph when indicated","clinical_question":"Alternative thoracic cause or complication","expected_finding":"No evident pneumothorax, major edema, or other thoracic cause.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Assesses selected mimics but does not rule out ACS.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8480c808-16c0-4d9c-8fb3-1d9c5547909f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng185/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1 STEMI; 1.2 NSTEMI and unstable angina","primary_source":true},{"id":"2ea5fc8d-8db7-4946-8f71-0bce734f789f","title":"Acute Coronary Syndrome Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Pharmacologic Anti-ischemic Therapy, Pharmacologic Antithrombotic Therapy","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public Medscape page retrieved 11 October 2026; limited secondary comparison","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1910735-treatment","locator":"Treatment and Management; detailed prescribing not reconciled","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult ACS; NICE and US ACS prescribing branches must remain separate. Full antithrombotic, renal and bleeding-risk reconciliation remains pending. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Give a single 300 mg aspirin loading dose when indicated and not contraindicated under the NICE ACS pathway.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Activate reperfusion assessment for STEMI; use a bleeding-risk and coronary-strategy-specific antithrombotic plan for NSTEMI rather than a universal P2Y12 or heparin regimen.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8480c808-16c0-4d9c-8fb3-1d9c5547909f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng185/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1 STEMI; 1.2 NSTEMI and unstable angina","primary_source":true},{"id":"2ea5fc8d-8db7-4946-8f71-0bce734f789f","title":"Acute Coronary Syndrome Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Pharmacologic Anti-ischemic Therapy, Pharmacologic Antithrombotic Therapy","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public Medscape page retrieved 11 October 2026; limited secondary comparison","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1910735-treatment","locator":"Treatment and Management; detailed prescribing not reconciled","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult ACS; NICE and US ACS prescribing branches must remain separate. Full antithrombotic, renal and bleeding-risk reconciliation remains pending. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain that possible ACS needs urgent assessment even if discomfort improves.","Seek emergency help immediately if symptoms recur."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Address tobacco, diet, activity, and cardiovascular risks after stabilization.","Support adherence to secondary prevention."],"mdtReferrals":["Cardiology","Cardiac rehabilitation when appropriate","Pharmacy and primary care for medication and risk-factor follow-up"],"dischargeCriteria":["Assessed by validated ACS pathway","No ongoing instability or unresolved high-risk features","Medication and follow-up plans documented","Emergency return precautions understood"],"followUpPlan":"For confirmed ACS, arrange cardiology follow-up and cardiac rehabilitation as appropriate."}}},{"guideline_id":"a14c7e92-5b31-4d68-9f20-6c83e1b7a405","original_version_ids":["ae7d60a4-0942-42d0-9172-b1ab43144112","92351adb-82fc-45c6-b074-05da4f68995e"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng185/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a14c7e92-5b31-4d68-9f20-6c83e1b7a405","title":"Acute Coronary Syndrome Assessment and Escalation Pathway","specialty":"Emergency Medicine and Cardiology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult ACS escalation; inherited investigation text is not newly verified.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Adult ACS escalation; inherited investigation text is not newly verified."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"limited-comparison","originalVersionIds":["ae7d60a4-0942-42d0-9172-b1ab43144112","92351adb-82fc-45c6-b074-05da4f68995e"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Acute myocardial ischaemia usually results from reduced coronary blood flow and may progress to infarction, arrhythmia, or haemodynamic compromise.","keyMechanisms":["Atherosclerotic plaque disruption with platelet activation and thrombosis","Reduced myocardial oxygen supply relative to demand","Progressive myocardial injury"]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Chest pressure, tightness, heaviness, or discomfort","Discomfort radiating to arm, shoulder, jaw, back, or upper abdomen","Dyspnoea, nausea, sweating, or unusual fatigue","Atypical or minimal symptoms, especially in older adults and people with diabetes"],"physicalSigns":["Pallor, diaphoresis, or respiratory distress","Tachycardia, bradycardia, hypotension, or irregular pulse","Possible heart-failure signs such as crackles or raised jugular venous pressure"],"redFlags":["Persistent or recurrent suspected cardiac chest discomfort","Acute ischaemic ECG pattern","Syncope, shock, pulmonary oedema, or life-threatening arrhythmia","Cardiac arrest or new neurological deficit"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Aortic dissection","distinguishingFeatures":"Abrupt severe chest or back pain, pulse or blood-pressure asymmetry, or new aortic regurgitation."},{"condition":"Pulmonary embolism","distinguishingFeatures":"Acute dyspnoea, pleuritic pain, hypoxaemia, or venous thromboembolism risk factors."},{"condition":"Acute pericarditis","distinguishingFeatures":"Often pleuritic or positional pain with compatible ECG findings."},{"condition":"Gastro-oesophageal or musculoskeletal pain","distinguishingFeatures":"May be meal-related, reflux-associated, movement-related, or reproducible; these features alone do not exclude ACS."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"12-lead electrocardiogram","modalityTarget":"12-lead electrocardiogram — Acute myocardial ischaemia or infarction","targetCondition":"Acute myocardial ischaemia or infarction","expectedFinding":"ST elevation or depression, dynamic T-wave change, or another acute ischaemic pattern","clinicalRationale":"Identify immediately actionable ischaemia and guide escalation."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial high-sensitivity cardiac troponin","modalityTarget":"Serial high-sensitivity cardiac troponin — Acute myocardial injury","targetCondition":"Acute myocardial injury","expectedFinding":"Rise or fall with at least one value above the assay-specific 99th percentile, interpreted with symptoms and ECG","clinicalRationale":"Detect myocardial injury using symptom timing and the local assay pathway."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Bedside echocardiography when indicated","modalityTarget":"Bedside echocardiography when indicated — Regional ventricular dysfunction or mechanical complication","targetCondition":"Regional ventricular dysfunction or mechanical complication","expectedFinding":"New regional wall-motion abnormality or cardiac dysfunction","clinicalRationale":"Assess instability or complications when clinically indicated."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Serial 12-lead electrocardiograms","modalityTarget":"Serial 12-lead electrocardiograms — Evolving acute myocardial ischaemia","targetCondition":"Evolving acute myocardial ischaemia","expectedFinding":"No dynamic ischaemic changes during assessment","clinicalRationale":"Repeat ECG when symptoms persist or recur; one normal ECG does not exclude ACS."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial high-sensitivity cardiac troponin using a validated local pathway","modalityTarget":"Serial high-sensitivity cardiac troponin using a validated local pathway — Acute myocardial infarction","targetCondition":"Acute myocardial infarction","expectedFinding":"Values and change below pathway rule-out thresholds with appropriate timing","clinicalRationale":"Support rule-out only when the complete validated pathway and clinical assessment permit."},{"tier":"firstLineImaging","testName":"Chest radiograph when indicated","modalityTarget":"Chest radiograph when indicated — Selected alternative acute thoracic causes","targetCondition":"Selected alternative acute thoracic causes","expectedFinding":"No finding supporting an alternative such as pulmonary oedema or pneumothorax","clinicalRationale":"Assess relevant alternatives; a normal result does not rule out ACS."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Activate the specialist reperfusion pathway for STEMI without waiting for a routine serial-troponin rule-out schedule.","For NSTEMI, assess bleeding risk and suitability and timing of coronary angiography before selecting antithrombotic treatment."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8480c808-16c0-4d9c-8fb3-1d9c5547909f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; 