n":"Regional ventricular dysfunction or mechanical complication","expected_finding":"New regional wall-motion abnormality or cardiac dysfunction","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Assess instability or complications when clinically indicated.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Serial 12-lead electrocardiograms","clinical_question":"Evolving acute myocardial ischaemia","expected_finding":"No dynamic ischaemic changes during assessment","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Repeat ECG when symptoms persist or recur; one normal ECG does not exclude ACS.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Serial high-sensitivity cardiac troponin using a validated local pathway","clinical_question":"Acute myocardial infarction","expected_finding":"Values and change below pathway rule-out thresholds with appropriate timing","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Support rule-out only when the complete validated pathway and clinical assessment permit.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Chest radiograph when indicated","clinical_question":"Selected alternative acute thoracic causes","expected_finding":"No finding supporting an alternative such as pulmonary oedema or pneumothorax","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Assess relevant alternatives; a normal result does not rule out ACS.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8480c808-16c0-4d9c-8fb3-1d9c5547909f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng185/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1 STEMI; 1.2 NSTEMI and unstable angina","primary_source":true},{"id":"2ea5fc8d-8db7-4946-8f71-0bce734f789f","title":"Acute Coronary Syndrome Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Pharmacologic Anti-ischemic Therapy, Pharmacologic Antithrombotic Therapy","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public Medscape page retrieved 11 October 2026; limited secondary comparison","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1910735-treatment","locator":"Treatment and Management; detailed prescribing not reconciled","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult ACS escalation; inherited investigation text is not newly verified. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Activate the specialist reperfusion pathway for STEMI without waiting for a routine serial-troponin rule-out schedule.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"For NSTEMI, assess bleeding risk and suitability and timing of coronary angiography before selecting antithrombotic treatment.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8480c808-16c0-4d9c-8fb3-1d9c5547909f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng185/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1 STEMI; 1.2 NSTEMI and unstable angina","primary_source":true},{"id":"2ea5fc8d-8db7-4946-8f71-0bce734f789f","title":"Acute Coronary Syndrome Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Pharmacologic Anti-ischemic Therapy, Pharmacologic Antithrombotic Therapy","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public Medscape page retrieved 11 October 2026; limited secondary comparison","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1910735-treatment","locator":"Treatment and Management; detailed prescribing not reconciled","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult ACS escalation; inherited investigation text is not newly verified. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain urgent ECGs, blood tests, monitoring, and possible transfer.","Discuss warning symptoms requiring emergency reassessment.","For confirmed ACS, explain follow-up and prescribed risk-reduction plan."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer individualised tobacco-cessation support, heart-healthy eating, physical activity, and cardiovascular risk reduction after acute assessment."],"mdtReferrals":["Emergency medicine","Cardiology","Critical care when indicated","Cardiac rehabilitation","Primary care"],"dischargeCriteria":["Time-critical causes have been assessed using an appropriate pathway.","Patient is clinically stable and disposition is documented.","Follow-up instructions and return precautions are communicated."],"followUpPlan":"Arrange follow-up for the final diagnosis; confirmed ACS requires a documented cardiology and cardiac-rehabilitation plan."}}},{"guideline_id":"05481a2b-c95c-440a-a4d0-0c520e8129a4","original_version_ids":["8e1ce559-b51a-406d-956b-7ddeae659366","3fb25cea-0d20-4ce5-9b01-e1b89f721cf0","e169da07-64c5-4ec2-88b8-4bb13413d757"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng115/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"05481a2b-c95c-440a-a4d0-0c520e8129a4","title":"Acute Exacerbation of COPD","specialty":"Respiratory Medicine / Emergency Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"NICE adult exacerbation branch. The inherited 40 mg steroid regimen is a different guideline approach and is not the NICE regimen. Antibiotic eligibility is not restricted to an ONLY cardinal-symptom rule.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","NICE adult exacerbation branch. The inherited 40 mg steroid regimen is a different guideline approach and is not the NICE regimen. Antibiotic eligibility is not restricted to an ONLY cardinal-symptom rule.","The version has no exact source URL.","Prednisolone 40 mg is not NICE NG115's 30 mg regimen. The restrictive ONLY antibiotic rule does not match NG114's individualised assessment.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["8e1ce559-b51a-406d-956b-7ddeae659366","3fb25cea-0d20-4ce5-9b01-e1b89f721cf0","e169da07-64c5-4ec2-88b8-4bb13413d757"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Airway inflammation and mucus increase expiratory flow limitation and dynamic hyperinflation; infection or pollutants can worsen ventilation-perfusion mismatch. Severe episodes may cause hypercapnia, fatigue, and respiratory muscle failure. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Airway inflammation and mucus increase expiratory flow limitation and dynamic hyperinflation","infection or pollutants can worsen ventilation-perfusion mismatch. Severe episodes may cause hypercapnia, fatigue, and respiratory muscle failure."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Acute Exacerbation of COPD, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Severe hypoxaemia or rising carbon dioxide with acidosis","Exhaustion, confusion, or silent chest","Haemodynamic instability","Sudden pleuritic pain or unilateral reduced breath sounds"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Pneumonia","distinguishingFeatures":"Fever, focal findings, or infiltrate may indicate concurrent infection."},{"condition":"Acute heart failure","distinguishingFeatures":"Congestion may coexist and change fluid or respiratory decisions."},{"condition":"Pulmonary embolism or pneumothorax","distinguishingFeatures":"Consider when onset, pain, hypoxaemia, or examination is disproportionate."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Oxygenation and blood gas when severe or hypercapnia is suspected; chest imaging and ECG as indicated.","modalityTarget":"Oxygenation and blood gas when severe or hypercapnia is suspected; chest imaging and ECG as indicated. — Acute Exacerbation of COPD","targetCondition":"Acute Exacerbation of COPD","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Review infection markers, renal function, medicines, and alternative causes; spirometry is generally not a stabilisation test.","modalityTarget":"Review infection markers, renal function, medicines, and alternative causes; spirometry is generally not a stabilisation test. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Exacerbation of COPD","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Exacerbation of COPD","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Acute Exacerbation of COPD","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Acute Exacerbation of COPD","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Under NICE NG115, the oral prednisolone course is 30 mg once daily for 5 days; assess contraindications and local prescribing requirements.","Use NG114 to consider antibiotics from sputum change, severity, admission history, cultures and resistance risk; reassess blood gases and provide NIV for persistent hypercapnic ventilatory failure despite optimal treatment."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b0ae3287-fdfd-4c81-8036-70e9b76b5884","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng115/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.3.16; 1.3.21; non-invasive ventilation","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NICE adult exacerbation branch. The inherited 40 mg steroid regimen is a different guideline approach and is not the NICE regimen. Antibiotic eligibility is not restricted to an ONLY cardinal-symptom rule. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Oxygenation and blood gas when severe or hypercapnia is suspected; chest imaging and ECG as indicated.","clinical_question":"Acute Exacerbation of COPD","expected_finding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Review infection markers, renal function, medicines, and alternative causes; spirometry is generally not a stabilisation test.","clinical_question":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Exacerbation of COPD","expected_finding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","clinical_question":"Important alternative to Acute Exacerbation of COPD","expected_finding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","clinical_question":"Progression or evolving complication","expected_finding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b0ae3287-fdfd-4c81-8036-70e9b76b5884","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng115/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.3.16; 1.3.21; non-invasive ventilation","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NICE adult exacerbation branch. The inherited 40 mg steroid regimen is a different guideline approach and is not the NICE regimen. Antibiotic eligibility is not restricted to an ONLY cardinal-symptom rule. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Under NICE NG115, the oral prednisolone course is 30 mg once daily for 5 days; assess contraindications and local prescribing requirements.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use NG114 to consider antibiotics from sputum change, severity, admission history, cultures and resistance risk; reassess blood gases and provide NIV for persistent hypercapnic ventilatory failure despite optimal treatment.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b0ae3287-fdfd-4c81-8036-70e9b76b5884","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.