plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"c2c404f2-5f47-4e4d-9ce7-fb32a9c1e105","original_version_ids":["04968dd7-475c-4576-863f-df8145ba1d60"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng128/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"c2c404f2-5f47-4e4d-9ce7-fb32a9c1e105","title":"Acute Ischemic Stroke","specialty":"Emergency Medicine and Neurology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult stroke; thrombolysis exclusions, post-thrombolysis antiplatelet timing and thrombectomy selection require stroke-team confirmation.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Adult stroke; thrombolysis exclusions, post-thrombolysis antiplatelet timing and thrombectomy selection require stroke-team confirmation."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["04968dd7-475c-4576-863f-df8145ba1d60"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Acute arterial occlusion reduces cerebral perfusion, causing focal neurologic dysfunction and potentially irreversible infarction.","keyMechanisms":["Thrombotic occlusion or embolism","Reduced cerebral blood flow","Ischemic penumbra around infarcted tissue","Potential large-vessel occlusion"]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Sudden unilateral face/arm/leg weakness or numbness","Sudden speech or language difficulty","Sudden visual loss or diplopia","Sudden imbalance or incoordination","Sudden focal deficit"],"physicalSigns":["Facial asymmetry","Unilateral weakness or sensory loss","Aphasia or dysarthria","Visual field deficit or gaze deviation","Ataxia or neglect"],"redFlags":["New disabling focal neurologic deficit","Reduced consciousness or airway compromise","Severe sudden headache or vomiting","Seizure at onset or worsening deficit","Unknown last-known-well time"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Intracranial hemorrhage","distinguishingFeatures":"May present similarly; urgent imaging is required before reperfusion decisions."},{"condition":"Hypoglycemia","distinguishingFeatures":"Can mimic focal deficit and should be checked immediately."},{"condition":"Seizure with postictal deficit","distinguishingFeatures":"Seizure or postictal state may be present, but stroke can also provoke seizure."},{"condition":"Migraine with aura","distinguishingFeatures":"May cause evolving positive symptoms; new deficits require urgent stroke assessment."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"Urgent noncontrast CT and vascular imaging when indicated","modalityTarget":"Urgent noncontrast CT and vascular imaging when indicated — Ischemic stroke/large-vessel occlusion","targetCondition":"Ischemic stroke/large-vessel occlusion","expectedFinding":"CT may initially be normal or show ischemic change; vascular imaging may identify occlusion.","clinicalRationale":"Excludes hemorrhage and supports reperfusion/thrombectomy decisions."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Bedside capillary glucose","modalityTarget":"Bedside capillary glucose — Hypoglycemia mimic or comorbidity","targetCondition":"Hypoglycemia mimic or comorbidity","expectedFinding":"Possible glucose abnormality.","clinicalRationale":"Rapidly identifies a treatable mimic."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Brain imaging before reperfusion","modalityTarget":"Brain imaging before reperfusion — Intracranial hemorrhage","targetCondition":"Intracranial hemorrhage","expectedFinding":"No acute hemorrhage on appropriate initial imaging.","clinicalRationale":"Hemorrhage must be assessed before ischemic reperfusion."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"ECG and cardiac monitoring","modalityTarget":"ECG and cardiac monitoring — Arrhythmia contributing to symptoms","targetCondition":"Arrhythmia contributing to symptoms","expectedFinding":"No acute arrhythmia; normal result does not exclude embolic source.","clinicalRationale":"Detects concurrent rhythm problems without delaying imaging."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Record last-known-well time and obtain urgent brain imaging; assess eligible patients for thrombolysis and thrombectomy.","Exclude intracranial haemorrhage before aspirin; do not apply the aspirin pathway without checking whether thrombolysis or another contraindication changes timing."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9f1d79e8-b471-4ab7-8cfe-54a3b9c6a8c8","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng128/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.3; 1.4","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult stroke; thrombolysis exclusions, post-thrombolysis antiplatelet timing and thrombectomy selection require stroke-team confirmation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Urgent noncontrast CT and vascular imaging when indicated","clinical_question":"Ischemic stroke/large-vessel occlusion","expected_finding":"CT may initially be normal or show ischemic change; vascular imaging may identify occlusion.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Excludes hemorrhage and supports reperfusion/thrombectomy decisions.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Bedside capillary glucose","clinical_question":"Hypoglycemia mimic or comorbidity","expected_finding":"Possible glucose abnormality.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Rapidly identifies a treatable mimic.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Brain imaging before reperfusion","clinical_question":"Intracranial hemorrhage","expected_finding":"No acute hemorrhage on appropriate initial imaging.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Hemorrhage must be assessed before ischemic reperfusion.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"ECG and cardiac monitoring","clinical_question":"Arrhythmia contributing to symptoms","expected_finding":"No acute arrhythmia; normal result does not exclude embolic source.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects concurrent rhythm problems without delaying imaging.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9f1d79e8-b471-4ab7-8cfe-54a3b9c6a8c8","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng128/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.3; 1.4","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult stroke; thrombolysis exclusions, post-thrombolysis antiplatelet timing and thrombectomy selection require stroke-team confirmation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Record last-known-well time and obtain urgent brain imaging; assess eligible patients for thrombolysis and thrombectomy.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Exclude intracranial haemorrhage before aspirin; do not apply the aspirin pathway without checking whether thrombolysis or another contraindication changes timing.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9f1d79e8-b471-4ab7-8cfe-54a3b9c6a8c8","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng128/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.3; 1.4","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult stroke; thrombolysis exclusions, post-thrombolysis antiplatelet timing and thrombectomy selection require stroke-team confirmation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain stroke symptoms require immediate emergency assessment even if they improve.","Discuss rehabilitation and recurrent-stroke warning signs after stabilization."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Assess tobacco, diet, activity, and vascular risks during recovery.","Follow swallowing and diet recommendations before oral intake."],"mdtReferrals":["Stroke neurology","Neurosurgery/interventional neuroradiology when indicated","Speech therapy, physiotherapy, occupational therapy","Cardiology and rehabilitation as appropriate"],"dischargeCriteria":["Stroke-team assessment and safe disposition completed","Neurologic status and investigations documented","Swallowing, mobility, and support assessed","Prevention, rehabilitation, and follow-up documented"],"followUpPlan":"Arrange stroke-service follow-up, rehabilitation, and etiologic evaluation; communicate prevention plans to primary care."}}},{"guideline_id":"cb0f8932-f4c5-4a6a-9d44-d320713a366b","original_version_ids":["e3ea9b5d-58ed-4873-be9b-97ca4d5ed4cd","21ec7e73-9c50-4d74-b9df-605b63a5a747"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng148/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"cb0f8932-f4c5-4a6a-9d44-d320713a366b","title":"Acute Kidney Injury","specialty":"Nephrology / Emergency Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"AKI assessment and escalation, not a dialysis prescription.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","AKI assessment and escalation, not a dialysis prescription.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["e3ea9b5d-58ed-4873-be9b-97ca4d5ed4cd","21ec7e73-9c50-4d74-b9df-605b63a5a747"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Reduced renal perfusion, parenchymal injury, or urinary obstruction can lower filtration; these mechanisms may coexist. Sepsis, medicines, glomerular disease, and fluid depletion can lead to electrolyte, acid-base, and volume complications. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Reduced renal perfusion, parenchymal injury, or urinary obstruction can lower filtration","these mechanisms may coexist. Sepsis, medicines, glomerular disease, and fluid depletion can lead to electrolyte, acid-base, and volume complications."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Acute Kidney Injury, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Anuria or rapidly rising creatinine","Refractory hyperkalaemia or acidosis","Pulmonary oedema or uraemic complication","Sepsis or suspected bilateral obstruction"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Chronic kidney disease progression","distinguishingFeatures":"Prior results and duration establish chronicity."},{"condition":"Urinary obstruction","distinguishingFeatures":"Retention symptoms and imaging identify a reversible cause."},{"condition":"Glomerular/interstitial disease or rhabdomyolysis","distinguishingFeatures":"Urine sediment, systemic signs, medicines, and muscle injury guide testing."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Trend creatinine against baseline, urine output, electrolytes, acid-base status, urine dip/microscopy and medication exposures.","modalityTarget":"Trend creatinine against baseline, urine output, electrolytes, acid-base status, urine dip/microscopy and medication exposures. — Acute Kidney Injury","targetCondition":"Acute Kidney Injury","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Renal imaging if obstruction is possible; use serology or additional imaging only when cause suggests it.","modalityTarget":"Renal imaging if obstruction is possible; use serology or additional imaging only when cause suggests it. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Kidney Injury","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Kidney Injury","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Acute Kidney Injury","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Acute Kidney Injury","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Compare creatinine with baseline, track urine output and review hypovolaemia, obstruction and nephrotoxic exposure.","Request urgent ultrasound when cause is unknown or obstruction is suspected; seek immediate specialist advice for refractory electrolyte, acid-base, uraemic or fluid complications."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":