1-06d78ec6c66b","25836b62-783e-4a3b-8a33-a14fe3e8443e"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Premature activation of pancreatic enzymes causes local inflammation and can trigger systemic inflammatory response. Oedema may progress to necrosis, fluid collections, or organ failure; gallstones, alcohol, metabolic causes, and medicines require consideration. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Premature activation of pancreatic enzymes causes local inflammation and can trigger systemic inflammatory response. Oedema may progress to necrosis, fluid collections, or organ failure","gallstones, alcohol, metabolic causes, and medicines require consideration."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Acute Pancreatitis, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Shock or persistent organ dysfunction","Hypoxaemia or acute kidney injury","Cholangitis or obstructive jaundice","Peritonism or pain out of proportion"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Biliary colic/cholecystitis","distinguishingFeatures":"May cause similar pain but lacks the full pancreatitis pattern."},{"condition":"Peptic ulcer/perforation","distinguishingFeatures":"Peritonism or free air changes management."},{"condition"