0a17b97"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng225/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"b2e88f9f-f504-436b-b521-b20ae8767b15","title":"Acute Poisoning and Overdose","specialty":"Emergency Medicine / Toxicology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"NG225 covers self-harm assessment, not antidote selection, toxic doses or general poisoning treatment. Agent-specific toxicology evidence remains required.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","NG225 covers self-harm assessment, not antidote selection, toxic doses or general poisoning treatment. Agent-specific toxicology evidence remains required.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["3aeb2822-c4b2-4467-a154-2fa8de32b4e7","661435bc-553c-46dc-80a2-8359a0a17b97"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Toxicity depends on the substance, dose, formulation, time, co-ingestants, and host physiology. Absorption and metabolism may cause delayed injury, and initially reassuring observations do not exclude later deterioration. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Toxicity depends on the substance, dose, formulation, time, co-ingestants, and host physiology. Absorption and metabolism may cause delayed injury, and initially reassuring observations do not exclude later deterioration.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Acute Poisoning and Overdose, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Airway compromise or respiratory depression","Seizure, dysrhythmia, shock, or severe acidosis","Hyperthermia or rapidly changing consciousness","High-risk caustic/cardiotoxic exposure or delayed-release ingestion"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Stroke/sepsis/metabolic encephalopathy","distinguishingFeatures":"May mimic intoxication and require parallel evaluation."},{"condition":"Trauma after collapse","distinguishingFeatures":"Look for occult injury."},{"condition":"Withdrawal","distinguishingFeatures":"Timing and substance history distinguish toxicity from withdrawal."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Bedside glucose, ECG, vital-sign trends, and targeted laboratory tests based on exposure and toxidrome.","modalityTarget":"Bedside glucose, ECG, vital-sign trends, and targeted laboratory tests based on exposure and toxidrome. — Acute Poisoning and Overdose","targetCondition":"Acute Poisoning and Overdose","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Contact regional poison centre or toxicologist; broad screening should not replace focused assessment.","modalityTarget":"Contact regional poison centre or toxicologist; broad screening should not replace focused assessment. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Poisoning and Overdose","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Poisoning and Overdose","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Acute Poisoning and Overdose","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Acute Poisoning and Overdose","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["For intentional overdose, arrange psychosocial assessment alongside physical care.","Obtain agent-specific poison-centre or toxicology advice; do not use this NICE self-harm source as an antidote or decontamination protocol."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"48402ff7-e689-44be-8db9-d786f735c0a2","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng225/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Initial aftercare; psychosocial assessment","primary_source":true},{"id":"9fcbd16b-3164-48b3-8ef4-79568e8801d7","title":"Resuscitation Council UK 2025 Special Circumstances Guidelines","issuer":"Other","edition":"2025 Resuscitation Guidelines","url":"https://www.resus.org.uk/professional-library/2025-resuscitation-guidelines/special-circumstances-guidelines","locator":"Toxins section","primary_source":false}],"sel