d and not verified in this audit: The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","clinical_question":"Progression or evolving complication","expected_finding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"48402ff7-e689-44be-8db9-d786f735c0a2","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng225/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Initial aftercare; psychosocial assessment","primary_source":true},{"id":"9fcbd16b-3164-48b3-8ef4-79568e8801d7","title":"Resuscitation Council UK 2025 Special Circumstances Guidelines","issuer":"Other","edition":"2025 Resuscitation Guidelines","url":"https://www.resus.org.uk/professional-library/2025-resuscitation-guidelines/special-circumstances-guidelines","locator":"Toxins section","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NG225 covers self-harm assessment, not antidote selection, toxic doses or general poisoning treatment. Agent-specific toxicology evidence remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"For intentional overdose, arrange psychosocial assessment alongside physical care.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Obtain agent-specific poison-centre or toxicology advice; do not use this NICE self-harm source as an antidote or decontamination protocol.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"48402ff7-e689-44be-8db9-d786f735c0a2","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng225/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Initial aftercare; psychosocial assessment","primary_source":true},{"id":"9fcbd16b-3164-48b3-8ef4-79568e8801d7","title":"Resuscitation Council UK 2025 Special Circumstances Guidelines","issuer":"Other","edition":"2025 Resuscitation Guidelines","url":"https://www.resus.org.uk/professional-library/2025-resuscitation-guidelines/special-circumstances-guidelines","locator":"Toxins section","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NG225 covers self-harm assessment, not antidote selection, toxic doses or general poisoning treatment. Agent-specific toxicology evidence remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain acute poisoning and overdose in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Emergency Medicine / Toxicology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"c2c404f2-5f47-4e4d-9ce7-fb32a9c1e101","original_version_ids":["3056cc7b-03fc-4590-89c6-d8ebeb6c0836"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"c2c404f2-5f47-4e4d-9ce7-fb32a9c1e101","title":"Acute Severe Asthma Exacerbation","specialty":"Emergency Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"NG245 excludes acute attacks and severe asthma management. An acute BTS/SIGN or equivalent locally reviewed emergency pathway remains required.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","NG245 excludes acute attacks; it is suitable only for chronic management and follow-up comparison.","NG245 excludes acute attacks and severe asthma management. An acute BTS/SIGN or equivalent locally reviewed emergency pathway remains required."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["3056cc7b-03fc-4590-89c6-d8ebeb6c0836"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Airway inflammation, bronchoconstriction, and mucus cause acute variable airflow obstruction.","keyMechanisms":["Bronchial smooth-muscle constriction","Mucosal edema and inflammation","Mucus plugging","Air trapping and ventilation-perfusion mismatch"]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Worsening dyspnea","Wheeze","Cough","Chest tightness","Reduced ability to speak or perform usual activity"],"physicalSigns":["Tachypnea","Prolonged expiration","Wheeze or reduced air entry","Accessory muscle use","Reduced oxygen saturation"],"redFlags":["Silent chest","Exhaustion or altered consciousness","Cyanosis or severe hypoxemia","Poor respiratory effort","Hypotension or possible anaphylaxis"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Anaphylaxis","distinguishingFeatures":"Respiratory symptoms with urticaria, angioedema, hypotension, or likely allergen exposure."},{"condition":"COPD exacerbation","distinguishingFeatures":"Chronic airflow symptoms with relevant smoking or exposure history."},{"condition":"Pneumonia","distinguishingFeatures":"Fever, focal chest findings, or compatible infiltrate."},{"condition":"Pulmonary embolism","distinguishingFeatures":"Sudden dyspnea or pleuritic pain with thromboembolic risk."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Peak expiratory flow or FEV1 when safe","modalityTarget":"Peak expiratory flow or FEV1 when safe — Airflow obstruction","targetCondition":"Airflow obstruction","expectedFinding":"Reduced expiratory flow compared with predicted or personal best.","clinicalRationale":"Objective severity measure and response assessment; do not delay treatment."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Pulse oximetry","modalityTarget":"Pulse oximetry — Hypoxemia","targetCondition":"Hypoxemia","expectedFinding":"Reduced oxygen saturation when hypoxemic.","clinicalRationale":"Guides oxygen and monitoring."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"firstLineImaging","testName":"Chest radiograph when complications or alternative diagnosis suspected","modalityTarget":"Chest radiograph when complications or alternative diagnosis suspected — Pneumothorax or focal pneumonia","targetCondition":"Pneumothorax or focal pneumonia","expectedFinding":"No alternative acute thoracic abnormality in uncomplicated asthma.","clinicalRationale":"Imaging is selective and not routinely required."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"12-lead ECG when cardiac symptoms or risks are present","modalityTarget":"12-lead ECG when cardiac symptoms or risks are present — Acute cardiac cause of dyspnea","targetCondition":"Acute cardiac cause of dyspnea","expectedFinding":"No acute ischemic or significant rhythm abnormality when not causal.","clinicalRationale":"Assesses important mimics or complications."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Escalate severe or life-threatening attacks through the emergency respiratory pathway; NG245 must not be cited as the acute rescue-treatment source.","After recovery, check controller treatment, inhaler technique and the written action plan using the chronic-management recommendations."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Scope; chronic management and supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NG245 excludes acute attacks and severe asthma management. An acute BTS/SIGN or equivalent locally reviewed emergency pathway remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Peak expiratory flow or FEV1 when safe","clinical_question":"Airflow obstruction","expected_finding":"Reduced expiratory flow compared with predicted or personal best.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Objective severity measure and response assessment; do not delay treatment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Pulse oximetry","clinical_question":"Hypoxemia","expected_finding":"Reduced oxygen saturation when hypoxemic.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Guides oxygen and monitoring.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Chest radiograph when complications or alternative diagnosis suspected","clinical_question":"Pneumothorax or focal pneumonia","expected_finding":"No alternative acute thoracic abnormality in uncomplicated asthma.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Imaging is selective and not routinely required.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"12-lead ECG when cardiac symptoms or risks are present","clinical_question":"Acute cardiac cause of dyspnea","expected_finding":"No acute ischemic or significant rhythm abnormality when not causal.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Assesses important mimics or complications.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Scope; chronic management and supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NG245 excludes acute attacks and severe asthma management. An acute BTS/SIGN or equivalent locally reviewed emergency pathway remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Escalate severe or life-threatening attacks through the emergency respiratory pathway; NG245 must not be cited as the acute rescue-treatment source.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"After recovery, check controller treatment, inhaler technique and the written action plan using the chronic-management recommendations.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Scope; chronic management and supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NG245 excludes acute attacks and severe asthma management. An acute BTS/SIGN or equivalent locally reviewed emergency pathway remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Review warning signs, written action plan, and inhaler technique."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Discuss individualized trigger reduction and smoke avoidance.","Encourage prescribed controller adherence."],"mdtReferrals":["Respiratory/asthma service for severe or recurrent disease","Allergy service when relevant","Critical care for life-threatening exacerbation"],"dischargeCriteria":["Sustained improvement","Stable oxygenation and effort per local criteria","Patient understands regimen and return precautions","Follow-up documented"],"followUpPlan":"Arrange prompt primary-care or asthma-service review; earlier review if symptoms persist or recur."}}},{"guideline_id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","original_version_ids":["9a2e4fd2-7700-4781-aaca-6a8d90f2846e","a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","title":"Acute Severe Asthma Exacerbation (Adult)","specialty":"Emergency Medicine and Respiratory Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2018-01-01","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"NG245 is a chronic-management comparator only; it cannot verify emergency bronchodilator, steroid or magnesium doses.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","NG245 excludes acute attacks; it is suitable only for chronic management and follow-up comparison.","NG245 is a chronic-management comparator only; it cannot verify emergency bronchodilator, steroid or magnesium doses."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["9a2e4fd2-7700-4781-aaca-6a8d90f2846e","a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"An acute exacerbation is a sustained worsening of airflow obstruction caused by bronchial smooth-muscle constriction, airway-wall oedema and mucus plugging on a background of variable airway inflammation. Severe obstruction raises the work of breathing, produces ventilation-perfusion mismatch and may progress from hypocapnia to carbon-dioxide retention as respiratory muscles fatigue.","keyMechanisms":["Trigger-driven airway inflammation and bronchial hyper-responsiveness narrow conducting airways.","Mucosal oedema and tenacious secretions amplify expiratory flow limitation and dynamic hyperinflation.","Ventilation-perfusion mismatch causes hypoxaemia; a normalising or rising carbon dioxide level in a distressed patient can indicate fatigue.","Prolonged expiration and air trapping increase intrathoracic pressure and the work of breathing."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Rapidly worsening breathlessness","Wheeze or chest tightness","Cough, often after a viral, allergen or irritant exposure","Reduced response to the patient's usual reliever medicine"],"physicalSigns":["Tachypnoea with prolonged expiration","Diffuse expiratory wheeze or, in near-fatal obstruction, a quiet chest","Accessory-muscle use and inability to complete sentences","Tachycardia with reduced peak expiratory flow compared with predicted or personal best"],"redFlags":["Exhaustion, confusion, drowsiness, cyanosis, hypotension or a silent chest","Inability to speak, worsening hypoxaemia or poor respiratory effort despite initial treatment","Normal or rising arterial carbon dioxide in a patient with severe respiratory distress","Previous near-fatal asthma, intensive-care admission or mechanical ventilation"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Anaphylaxis","distinguishingFeatures":"Abrupt multisystem illness with urticaria, angioedema, hypotension or gastrointestinal symptoms after a likely exposure."},{"condition":"Acute pulmonary oedema","distinguishingFeatures":"Orthopnoea, inspiratory crackles, raised jugular venous pressure or radiographic congestion rather than predominantly expiratory obstruction."},{"condition":"Pulmonary embolism","distinguishingFeatures":"Pleuritic pain, haemoptysis, venous-thromboembolism risk factors or unexplained hypoxaemia with limited wheeze."},{"condition":"Pneumothorax","distinguishingFeatures":"Sudden unilateral pleuritic pain, asymmetric breath sounds and hyper-resonance; tension physiology adds hypotension and tracheal deviation."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Peak expiratory flow","modalityTarget":"Peak expiratory flow — Severity of airflow obstruction","targetCondition":"Severity of airflow obstruction","expectedFinding":"Marked reduction from predicted or documented personal best, with serial improvement after treatment supporting reversible obstruction.","clinicalRationale":"Provides an objective trend when the patient can perform the manoeuvre safely."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Continuous pulse oximetry","modalityTarget":"Continuous pulse oximetry — Hypoxaemia","targetCondition":"Hypoxaemia","expectedFinding":"Reduced oxygen saturation or a need for supplemental oxygen to maintain the locally defined target.","clinicalRationale":"Detects gas-exchange impairment and guides titrated oxygen while avoiding delay to treatment."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Arterial or venous blood gas when severe or deteriorating","modalityTarget":"Arterial or venous blood gas when severe or deteriorating — Respiratory failure and metabolic disturbance","targetCondition":"Respiratory failure and metabolic disturbance","expectedFinding":"Hypoxaemia; carbon-dioxide retention or acidaemia in life-threatening disease.","clinicalRationale":"A rising carbon dioxide level can signal fatigue and the need for critical-care escalation."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"firstLineImaging","testName":"Chest radiograph when clinically indicated","modalityTarget":"Chest radiograph when clinically indicated — Pneumothorax, pneumonia or pulmonary oedema","targetCondition":"Pneumothorax, pneumonia or pulmonary oedema","expectedFinding":"No focal alternative pathology in uncomplicated asthma; an abnormality redirects management.","clinicalRationale":"Imaging is selective rather than routine and should not delay immediate bronchodilator treatment."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"12-lead electrocardiogram","modalityTarget":"12-lead electrocardiogram — Acute coronary syndrome or significant arrhythmia","targetCondition":"Acute coronary syndrome or significant arrhythmia","expectedFinding":"Absence of acute ischaemic change or a clinically important rhythm disturbance.","clinicalRationale":"Useful for older patients, chest pain, marked tachycardia or relevant cardiovascular comorbidity."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Use the locally reviewed acute-asthma emergency pathway for rescue treatment and escalation.","Before discharge, arrange controller review, inhaler-technique assessment and an individual written action plan; verify the acute prescribing source separately."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Scope; chronic management and supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NG245 is a chronic-management comparator only; it cannot verify emergency bronchodilator, steroid or magnesium doses. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Peak expiratory flow","clinical_question":"Severity of airflow obstruction","expected_finding":"Marked reduction from predicted or documented personal best, with serial improvement after treatment supporting reversible obstruction.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides an objective trend when the patient can perform the manoeuvre safely.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Continuous pulse oximetry","clinical_question":"Hypoxaemia","expected_finding":"Reduced oxygen saturation or a need for supplemental oxygen to maintain the locally defined target.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects gas-exchange impairment and guides titrated oxygen while avoiding delay to treatment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Arterial or venous blood gas when severe or deteriorating","clinical_question":"Respiratory failure and metabolic disturbance","expected_finding":"Hypoxaemia; carbon-dioxide retention or acidaemia in life-threatening disease.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: A rising carbon dioxide level can signal fatigue and the need for critical-care escalation.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Chest radiograph when clinically indicated","clinical_question":"Pneumothorax, pneumonia or pulmonary oedema","expected_finding":"No focal alternative pathology in uncomplicated asthma; an abnormality redirects management.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Imaging is selective rather than routine and should not delay immediate bronchodilator treatment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"12-lead electrocardiogram","clinical_question":"Acute coronary syndrome or significant arrhythmia","expected_finding":"Absence of acute ischaemic change or a clinically important rhythm disturbance.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Useful for older patients, chest pain, marked tachycardia or relevant cardiovascular comorbidity.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Scope; chronic management and supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NG245 is a chronic-management comparator only; it cannot verify emergency bronchodilator, steroid or magnesium doses. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Use the locally reviewed acute-asthma emergency pathway for rescue treatment and escalation.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Before discharge, arrange controller review, inhaler-technique assessment and an individual written action plan; verify the acute prescribing source separately.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Scope; chronic management and supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NG245 is a chronic-management comparator only; it cannot verify emergency bronchodilator, steroid or magnesium doses. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain reliever versus controller medicines and the danger of relying on frequent reliever use.","Demonstrate inhaler and spacer technique and confirm understanding using teach-back.","Provide a written action plan that states deterioration thresholds and where to obtain urgent care."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Identify and reduce exposure to tobacco smoke, vaping, occupational irritants and known allergens.","Support influenza vaccination and other indicated immunisation under the Saudi schedule.","Encourage gradual return to activity once symptoms and peak flow recover."],"mdtReferrals":["Respiratory specialist for life-threatening, recurrent severe or diagnostically uncertain asthma","Asthma educator or respiratory pharmacist for technique and adherence review","Critical care when deterioration, exhaustion or ventilatory support is anticipated"],"dischargeCriteria":["Symptoms and work of breathing have improved and remain stable after observation.","Oxygenation is stable without unplanned escalation and objective airflow is improving.","Medicines, inhaler technique, written action plan, follow-up and return precautions are confirmed."],"followUpPlan":"Arrange prompt primary-care or respiratory review after discharge, with earlier assessment for recurrent symptoms; review the trigger, control, adherence, inhaler technique and need to step up long-term therapy."}}},{"guideline_id":"6fccc942-c6f3-4ef7-94cf-26fd23edfd27","original_version_ids":["5f870750-7401-4d72-bd07-1469e822e769","e28fb868-6c3d-488d-9f60-f989847037af"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg141/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"6fccc942-c6f3-4ef7-94cf-26fd23edfd27","title":"Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","specialty":"Gastroenterology / Emergency Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult acute UGIB; distinguish variceal from non-variceal treatment.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","Adult acute UGIB; distinguish variceal from non-variceal treatment.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["5f870750-7401-4d72-bd07-1469e822e769","e28fb868-6c3d-488d-9f60-f989847037af"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Bleeding proximal to the ligament of Treitz can arise from ulceration, varices, erosions, malignancy, or vascular lesions. Blood loss may progress rapidly; liver disease and antithrombotic medicines change the risk and management pathway. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Bleeding proximal to the ligament of Treitz can arise from ulceration, varices, erosions, malignancy, or vascular lesions. Blood loss may progress rapidly","liver disease and antithrombotic medicines change the risk and management pathway."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Shock or ongoing brisk haematemesis","Syncope with instability or altered mental state","Suspected variceal bleeding","Airway compromise or major comorbidity"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Lower GI source","distinguishingFeatures":"Brisk upper bleeding can present with red blood; source needs evaluation."},{"condition":"Swallowed nasal/oral blood","distinguishingFeatures":"Examine for an alternative source when history suggests it."},{"condition":"Aortoenteric fistula","distinguishingFeatures":"Prior aortic graft with GI bleeding is a time-critical emergency."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"CBC, renal profile, coagulation, liver tests, ECG when appropriate, and type/crossmatch.","modalityTarget":"CBC, renal profile, coagulation, liver tests, ECG when appropriate, and type/crossmatch. — Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","targetCondition":"Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Endoscopy timing and risk stratification follow current local protocol after stabilisation.","modalityTarget":"Endoscopy timing and risk stratification follow current local protocol after stabilisation. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Calculate the Blatchford score initially and arrange endoscopy immediately after resuscitation for unstable severe bleeding, or within 24 hours for other patients.","Do not routinely give acid suppression before endoscopy for suspected non-variceal bleeding under this NICE pathway; use a separate variceal pathway when suspected."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8e361751-c78c-4290-8237-65e0085d4439","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg141/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.3; 1.4; 1.5","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult acute UGIB; distinguish variceal from non-variceal treatment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"CBC, renal profile, coagulation, liver tests, ECG when appropriate, and type/crossmatch.","clinical_question":"Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","expected_finding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Endoscopy timing and risk stratification follow current local protocol after stabilisation.","clinical_question":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","expected_finding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","clinical_question":"Important alternative to Acute Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding","expected_finding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","clinical_question":"Progression or evolving complication","expected_finding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8e361751-c78c-4290-8237-65e0085d4439","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg141/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.3; 1.4; 1.5","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult acute UGIB; distinguish variceal from non-variceal treatment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Calculate the Blatchford score initially and arrange endoscopy immediately after resuscitation for unstable severe bleeding, or within 24 hours for other patients.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Do not routinely give acid suppression before endoscopy for suspected non-variceal bleeding under this NICE pathway; use a separate variceal pathway when suspected.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"8e361751-c78c-4290-8237-65e0085d4439","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg141/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.3; 1.4; 1.5","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult acute UGIB; distinguish variceal from non-variceal treatment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain acute upper gastrointestinal bleeding in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Gastroenterology / Emergency Medicine","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"c36e9014-7d53-4a82-b641-8e05a3c9d627","original_version_ids":["126c1f4a-c6af-425f-af52-4d86f6e92223","f8a3c6b1-f12a-4123-a95c-63e43c1121a2"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng136/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"c36e9014-7d53-4a82-b641-8e05a3c9d627","title":"Adult Essential Hypertension Screening and Confirmation","specialty":"Primary Care and Family Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"NICE diagnosis thresholds; local Saudi risk tools and treatment implementation require review.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Diagnostic referral or uptake guidance is not sufficient evidence for a Saudi population screening or vaccination schedule.","NICE diagnosis thresholds; local Saudi risk tools and treatment implementation require review."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["126c1f4a-c6af-425f-af52-4d86f6e92223","f8a3c6b1-f12a-4123-a95c-63e43c1121a2"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Essential hypertension is persistently elevated arterial blood pressure without an identified secondary cause. It is often asymptomatic and increases cardiovascular, cerebrovascular, and kidney risk.","keyMechanisms":["Interactions among genetic, renal, vascular, neurohormonal, and environmental factors","Increased systemic vascular resistance and altered sodium-volume regulation","Cumulative pressure-related vascular and target-organ injury"]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Usually asymptomatic","Occasional non-specific headache or dizziness, which cannot establish diagnosis"],"physicalSigns":["Elevated pressure on correctly performed measurement","Possible target-organ disease in established hypertension","Possible clinical clues to a secondary cause"],"redFlags":["Severe elevation with chest pain, dyspnoea, neurological deficit, confusion, visual loss, or acute kidney injury","Pregnancy with elevated pressure or pre-eclampsia symptoms","Abrupt onset, resistant readings, or suspected secondary cause"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"White-coat hypertension","distinguishingFeatures":"Clinic readings elevated but validated out-of-office average not persistently elevated."},{"condition":"Masked hypertension","distinguishingFeatures":"Clinic readings may be below threshold while home or ambulatory readings are elevated."},{"condition":"Secondary hypertension","distinguishingFeatures":"Young onset, abrupt worsening, resistance, relevant medicines, renal or endocrine clues."},{"condition":"Transient elevation","distinguishingFeatures":"Pain, anxiety, acute illness, stimulants, or measurement error; repeat under standardised conditions."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Repeated standardised clinic blood-pressure measurement","modalityTarget":"Repeated standardised clinic blood-pressure measurement — Persistently elevated blood pressure","targetCondition":"Persistently elevated blood pressure","expectedFinding":"Repeated readings meeting locally adopted threshold using validated device and correct cuff","clinicalRationale":"Reduce misclassification from poor technique or transient elevation."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Home or ambulatory blood-pressure monitoring","modalityTarget":"Home or ambulatory blood-pressure monitoring — Sustained hypertension","targetCondition":"Sustained hypertension","expectedFinding":"Out-of-office average meeting locally adopted threshold","clinicalRationale":"Confirm persistence and identify white-coat or masked hypertension."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Creatinine, estimated glomerular filtration rate, electrolytes, urine albumin, and urinalysis","modalityTarget":"Creatinine, estimated glomerular filtration rate, electrolytes, urine albumin, and urinalysis — Target-organ involvement or possible secondary hypertension","targetCondition":"Target-organ involvement or possible secondary hypertension","expectedFinding":"Renal impairment, albuminuria, electrolyte abnormality, or other finding needing assessment","clinicalRationale":"Assess baseline kidney health and direct further evaluation."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Electrocardiogram","modalityTarget":"Electrocardiogram — Cardiac target-organ involvement","targetCondition":"Cardiac target-organ involvement","expectedFinding":"Possible left ventricular hypertrophy, rhythm abnormality, or prior cardiac disease","clinicalRationale":"Assess cardiovascular context; normal ECG does not exclude hypertension."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Repeat standardised readings after rest","modalityTarget":"Repeat standardised readings after rest — Transient or measurement-related elevation","targetCondition":"Transient or measurement-related elevation","expectedFinding":"Repeat readings below locally adopted threshold","clinicalRationale":"Check for technique-related or transient elevation."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Validated home or ambulatory monitoring","modalityTarget":"Validated home or ambulatory monitoring — White-coat hypertension","targetCondition":"White-coat hypertension","expectedFinding":"Out-of-office average below local threshold despite elevated clinic readings","clinicalRationale":"Avoid relying on clinic readings alone when results are discordant."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Targeted secondary-hypertension investigations","modalityTarget":"Targeted secondary-hypertension investigations — Secondary cause of elevated blood pressure","targetCondition":"Secondary cause of elevated blood pressure","expectedFinding":"No targeted evidence for the suspected cause","clinicalRationale":"Select testing using clinical indications rather than broad routine testing."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Confirm clinic readings of 140/90 to below 180/120 mmHg using ABPM, or HBPM if ABPM is unsuitable.","Use a daytime ABPM or HBPM average of at least 135/85 mmHg to confirm hypertension with raised clinic pressure; assess severe readings for same-day referral indications."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"be6c8987-fa62-4aff-8fb1-736183cdff6e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng136/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2.3–1.2.8; 1.5","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NICE diagnosis thresholds; local Saudi risk tools and treatment implementation require review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Repeated standardised clinic blood-pressure measurement","clinical_question":"Persistently elevated blood pressure","expected_finding":"Repeated readings meeting locally adopted threshold using validated device and correct cuff","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Reduce misclassification from poor technique or transient elevation.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Home or ambulatory blood-pressure monitoring","clinical_question":"Sustained hypertension","expected_finding":"Out-of-office average meeting locally adopted threshold","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Confirm persistence and identify white-coat or masked hypertension.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Creatinine, estimated glomerular filtration rate, electrolytes, urine albumin, and urinalysis","clinical_question":"Target-organ involvement or possible secondary hypertension","expected_finding":"Renal impairment, albuminuria, electrolyte abnormality, or other finding needing assessment","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Assess baseline kidney health and direct further evaluation.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Electrocardiogram","clinical_question":"Cardiac target-organ involvement","expected_finding":"Possible left ventricular hypertrophy, rhythm abnormality, or prior cardiac disease","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Assess cardiovascular context; normal ECG does not exclude hypertension.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Repeat standardised readings after rest","clinical_question":"Transient or measurement-related elevation","expected_finding":"Repeat readings below locally adopted threshold","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Check for technique-related or transient elevation.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Validated home or ambulatory monitoring","clinical_question":"White-coat hypertension","expected_finding":"Out-of-office average below local threshold despite elevated clinic readings","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Avoid relying on clinic readings alone when results are discordant.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Targeted secondary-hypertension investigations","clinical_question":"Secondary cause of elevated blood pressure","expected_finding":"No targeted evidence for the suspected cause","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Select testing using clinical indications rather than broad routine testing.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"be6c8987-fa62-4aff-8fb1-736183cdff6e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng136/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2.3–1.2.8; 1.5","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NICE diagnosis thresholds; local Saudi risk tools and treatment implementation require review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Confirm clinic readings of 140/90 to below 180/120 mmHg using ABPM, or HBPM if ABPM is unsuitable.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use a daytime ABPM or HBPM average of at least 135/85 mmHg to confirm hypertension with raised clinic pressure; assess severe readings for same-day referral indications.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"be6c8987-fa62-4aff-8fb1-736183cdff6e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng136/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2.3–1.2.8; 1.5","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. NICE diagnosis thresholds; local Saudi risk tools and treatment implementation require review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain that hypertension is often symptom-free and needs accurate measurement and follow-up.","Teach home-monitoring technique when used.","Explain urgent symptoms requiring immediate assessment."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Discuss balanced eating and sodium reduction where appropriate.","Encourage regular activity, healthy weight goals, and tobacco cessation.","Discuss alcohol use consistent with health needs and local advice."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary care or family medicine","Dietitian or lifestyle support","Cardiology, nephrology, or endocrinology when indicated","Obstetrics for pregnancy-associated hypertension"],"dischargeCriteria":["Measurement result, confirmation plan, and precautions are documented.","Acute target-organ injury is assessed and disposition determined.","Patient knows when blood pressure will be reassessed."],"followUpPlan":"Arrange repeat clinic or out-of-office measurements and cardiovascular-risk review according to results, patient risk, and local guidance."}}},{"guideline_id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008","original_version_ids":["a326783d-e111-4e09-a483-cdeea297fd59","a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008","title":"Adult Periodic Health Examination","specialty":"Family Medicine and Preventive Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2023-01-01","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Cardiovascular prevention component only; no single NICE guideline verifies the entire Saudi preventive-screening schedule.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Cardiovascular prevention component only; no single NICE guideline verifies the entire Saudi preventive-screening schedule."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["a326783d-e111-4e09-a483-cdeea297fd59","a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Periodic health examination is a risk-based preventive-care process rather than a disease episode. It identifies modifiable cardiovascular, metabolic, cancer, infectious, mental-health and functional risks before symptoms or irreversible complications develop, while avoiding screening that has an unfavourable balance of benefit and harm.","keyMechanisms":["Age, sex, family history, exposures and comorbidity alter baseline disease probability and screening benefit.","Repeated measurement can detect trajectories in blood pressure, adiposity, glycaemia and lipids before complications emerge.","Evidence-based screening shifts selected cancers and chronic diseases toward earlier diagnosis.","Shared decisions reduce harms from false positives, overdiagnosis and preventive medicines with small net benefit."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Often asymptomatic attendance for preventive review","May disclose fatigue, low mood, sleep problems or reduced function during structured history","May report tobacco exposure, inactivity, unhealthy diet or occupational risk","May have overdue vaccination or cancer screening"],"physicalSigns":["Elevated or discrepant blood-pressure readings","Raised body-mass index or waist circumference","Oral-health, vision, hearing or mobility concerns","Abnormal findings requiring conversion from screening to a diagnostic pathway"],"redFlags":["Chest pain, focal neurological deficit, severe breathlessness or syncope discovered during screening","Markedly elevated blood pressure with acute target-organ symptoms","Suicidal ideation or immediate safeguarding concern","Alarm cancer symptoms such as unexplained bleeding, persistent mass or major unintentional weight loss"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Routine preventive need","distinguishingFeatures":"Asymptomatic, eligible by age or risk and suitable for a validated screening intervention."},{"condition":"Established disease requiring chronic-care review","distinguishingFeatures":"Known diagnosis or repeated abnormal result requiring disease-specific targets rather than screening thresholds."},{"condition":"Symptomatic undiagnosed disease","distinguishingFeatures":"Symptoms or signs raise pre-test probability and require diagnostic, not screening, tests."},{"condition":"Transient measurement abnormality","distinguishingFeatures":"Single clinic value is not confirmed on repeat or out-of-office measurement."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Standardised blood-pressure measurement with out-of-office confirmation","modalityTarget":"Standardised blood-pressure measurement with out-of-office confirmation — Hypertension","targetCondition":"Hypertension","expectedFinding":"Persistently elevated readings confirmed outside the clinic when indicated.","clinicalRationale":"Reduces misclassification from technique, white-coat effect and isolated readings."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Risk-based glucose testing","modalityTarget":"Risk-based glucose testing — Prediabetes or diabetes","targetCondition":"Prediabetes or diabetes","expectedFinding":"Abnormal fasting glucose, random glucose in context or glycated haemoglobin confirmed through the diagnostic pathway.","clinicalRationale":"PHA guidance begins routine adult testing at the defined age and earlier with overweight plus risk factors."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Age-, sex- and risk-appropriate cancer screening","modalityTarget":"Age-, sex- and risk-appropriate cancer screening — Preclinical breast, colorectal, cervical or lung cancer","targetCondition":"Preclinical breast, colorectal, cervical or lung cancer","expectedFinding":"Negative screening at the recommended interval or an abnormal result requiring timely diagnostic confirmation.","clinicalRationale":"Benefit depends on eligibility, interval and complete follow-through after an abnormal screen."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Repeat or confirmatory diagnostic test after an abnormal screen","modalityTarget":"Repeat or confirmatory diagnostic test after an abnormal screen — False-positive screening result","targetCondition":"False-positive screening result","expectedFinding":"Diagnostic testing does not confirm disease.","clinicalRationale":"Screening tests do not by themselves establish many diagnoses."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Medication and comorbidity review","modalityTarget":"Medication and comorbidity review — Secondary or iatrogenic risk","targetCondition":"Secondary or iatrogenic risk","expectedFinding":"A medicine, pregnancy state, renal disease or other condition explains or changes the preventive finding.","clinicalRationale":"Prevents inappropriate application of general-population screening or treatment advice."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Separate asymptomatic prevention from symptoms needing diagnostic assessment.","Assess cardiovascular risk with a locally appropriate tool; verify cancer, infection and vaccination schedules against current Saudi policy individually."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b5b625ed-5749-42c6-8d45-1dbfb60d06c0","title":"Recommen