evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain that preventive tests are selected by personal risk and that more testing is not always safer.","Use shared decision making for preference-sensitive cancer screening and preventive medicines.","Give accessible instructions for preparation, result access and the next step after an abnormal result."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Support a sustainable dietary pattern rich in vegetables, fruit, whole grains and minimally processed foods while accounting for culture and comorbidity.","Encourage regular aerobic and strengthening activity adapted to ability.","Provide tobacco cessation, sleep, weight and oral-health support without stigma."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary-care nurse or preventive-care coordinator for recall and result tracking","Dietitian, tobacco-cessation service or exercise professional according to risk","Mental-health service for confirmed depression, anxiety or safety concern","Diagnostic specialty pathway for any abnormal screening result"],"dischargeCriteria":["Risk profile, due interventions and deferred shared decisions are documented.","Every test and referral has a named owner and result-communication method.","Urgent symptoms or severe abnormalities have been diverted to immediate assessment."],"followUpPlan":"Maintain a personalised recall schedule based on the 2023 PHA age and risk tables, review abnormal results promptly, and update eligibility whenever health status, family history, pregnancy status or exposure changes."}}},{"guideline_id":"1dd5fa99-fc60-44e6-94f4-6de6287a1244","original_version_ids":["99c12136-f664-4e78-83d6-a81d4db6dd88","e22900b7-652e-4daf-97a9-ea000ece3f7a"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng218/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"1dd5fa99-fc60-44e6-94f4-6de6287a1244","title":"Adult Vaccination Review","specialty":"Family Medicine / Public Health","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Vaccine uptake only; NG218 does not supply an adult vaccine product/dose schedule, and CDC schedules are not automatically Saudi schedules.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","Diagnostic referral or uptake guidance is not sufficient evidence for a Saudi population screening or vaccination schedule.","Vaccine uptake only; NG218 does not supply an adult vaccine product/dose schedule, and CDC schedules are not automatically Saudi schedules.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["99c12136-f664-4e78-83d6-a81d4db6dd88","e22900b7-652e-4daf-97a9-ea000ece3f7a"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Vaccination reduces susceptible-host risk and community transmission through antigen-specific immune memory. Benefit and safety depend on age, comorbidity, immune status, prior doses, exposure, and current national recommendations. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Vaccination reduces susceptible-host risk and community transmission through antigen-specific immune memory. Benefit and safety depend on age, comorbidity, immune status, prior doses, exposure, and current national recommendations.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Adult Vaccination Review, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Severe allergic reaction history","Immunocompromise affecting live vaccines","Current acute illness or pregnancy influencing timing","Travel exposure with urgent prophylaxis window"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Natural immunity or previous vaccination","distinguishingFeatures":"Use records and serology only where nationally recommended."},{"condition":"Vaccine adverse event","distinguishingFeatures":"Separate expected symptoms from contraindication-level reaction."},{"condition":"Unrecorded dose","distinguishingFeatures":"Check registry or prior provider before deciding repeat schedule."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Reconcile immunisation registry and records; review age, comorbidities, medicines, pregnancy, travel and occupational exposures.","modalityTarget":"Reconcile immunisation registry and records; review age, comorbidities, medicines, pregnancy, travel and occupational exposures. — Adult Vaccination Review","targetCondition":"Adult Vaccination Review","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Compare against current Saudi MOH/PHA schedule and product information; document plan and next due date.","modalityTarget":"Compare against current Saudi MOH/PHA schedule and product information; document plan and next due date. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Adult Vaccination Review","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Adult Vaccination Review","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Adult Vaccination Review","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Adult Vaccination Review","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Check reliable immunisation records, eligibility and individual contraindications before planning catch-up.","Use current Saudi vaccine schedules and product guidance for intervals and doses; address uptake barriers and informed consent."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"6a326d01-df4c-4fe5-839c-8c0cf9c7c07f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng218/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Identifying eligible people; discussing vaccination","primary_source":true},{"id":"4685fc57-8187-4dac-b385-908689fbcc10","title":"CDC Recommended Adult Immunization Schedule for Ages 19 Years or Older","issuer":"Other","edition":"United States, 2025 schedule currently displayed by CDC under court-order notice","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/vaccines/hcp/imz-schedules/downloads/adult/adult-combined-schedule-bw.pdf","locator":"Tables 1 and 2, Notes, and Appendix on contraindications and pre