nstruction":"Check reliable immunisation records, eligibility and individual contraindications before planning catch-up.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use current Saudi vaccine schedules and product guidance for intervals and doses; address uptake barriers and informed consent.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"6a326d01-df4c-4fe5-839c-8c0cf9c7c07f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng218/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Identifying eligible people; discussing vaccination","primary_source":true},{"id":"4685fc57-8187-4dac-b385-908689fbcc10","title":"CDC Recommended Adult Immunization Schedule for Ages 19 Years or Older","issuer":"Other","edition":"United States, 2025 schedule currently displayed by CDC under court-order notice","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/vaccines/hcp/imz-schedules/downloads/adult/adult-combined-schedule-bw.pdf","locator":"Tables 1 and 2, Notes, and Appendix on contraindications and precautions","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Vaccine uptake only; NG218 does not supply an adult vaccine product/dose schedule, and CDC schedules are not automatically Saudi schedules. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain adult vaccination review in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Family Medicine / Public Health","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"17fa021f-7661-44bf-9e70-1754632b4e9c","original_version_ids":["76ab7f97-09fa-4c03-ad05-a83567678e40","a67f8d61-8f8b-46dc-b6ed-d3cd45f76f39"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng115/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"17fa021f-7661-44bf-9e70-1754632b4e9c","title":"Advanced COPD Supportive Care","specialty":"Respiratory Medicine / Palliative Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Palliative Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Advanced COPD supportive care, not an opioid or home-oxygen prescribing protocol.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","Advanced COPD supportive care, not an opioid or home-oxygen prescribing protocol.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["76ab7f97-09fa-4c03-ad05-a83567678e40","a67f8d61-8f8b-46dc-b6ed-d3cd45f76f39"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Advanced airflow limitation causes chronic breathlessness and reduced reserve; anxiety, deconditioning, cardiac disease, anaemia, infection, and environment may amplify distress. Palliative support complements respiratory treatment. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Advanced airflow limitation causes chronic breathlessness and reduced reserve","anxiety, deconditioning, cardiac disease, anaemia, infection, and environment may amplify distress. Palliative support complements respiratory treatment."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Advanced COPD Supportive Care, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Acute severe exacerbation or hypoxaemia","New chest pain, haemoptysis, or unilateral findings","Confusion suggesting hypercapnia","Uncontrolled panic or unsafe home support"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Heart failure","distinguishingFeatures":"Congestion may coexist."},{"condition":"Pulmonary embolism or pneumothorax","distinguishingFeatures":"Consider acute disproportionate change."},{"condition":"Anaemia, infection, anxiety, deconditioning","distinguishingFeatures":"May amplify breathlessness and be treatable."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Review symptom trajectory, inhalers, oxygenation, exacerbations, comorbidities, function and anxiety; targeted tests for new change.","modalityTarget":"Review symptom trajectory, inhalers, oxygenation, exacerbations, comorbidities, function and anxiety; targeted tests for new change. — Advanced COPD Supportive Care","targetCondition":"Advanced COPD Supportive Care","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Assess oxygen/ventilation indications using current respiratory guidance, not breathlessness alone.","modalityTarget":"Assess oxygen/ventilation indications using current respiratory guidance, not breathlessness alone. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Advanced COPD Supportive Care","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Advanced COPD Supportive Care","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Advanced COPD Supportive Care","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Advanced COPD Supportive Care","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Address breathlessness, function and advance-care preferences alongside respiratory treatment.","Coordinate respiratory, rehabilitation and palliative support; verify drug and oxygen decisions separately."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the i