,"title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Address breathlessness, function and advance-care preferences alongside respiratory treatment.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Coordinate respiratory, rehabilitation and palliative support; verify drug and oxygen decisions separately.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b0ae3287-fdfd-4c81-8036-70e9b76b5884","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng115/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Palliative care; multidisciplinary management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Advanced COPD supportive care, not an opioid or home-oxygen prescribing protocol. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain advanced copd supportive care in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Respiratory Medicine / Palliative Medicine","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"7c1b7028-68a7-4fdb-ae44-be27da67e5e1","original_version_ids":["04122c28-18cc-4f3e-bec6-da593663a0d3","3fcc3ad7-6211-4a1b-9a34-644dd761b715"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng97/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"7c1b7028-68a7-4fdb-ae44-be27da67e5e1","title":"Advanced Dementia and Comfort-Focused Care","specialty":"Geriatrics / Palliative Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Palliative Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Advanced dementia; feeding and treatment goals require shared decisions.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","Advanced dementia; feeding and treatment goals require shared decisions.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["04122c28-18cc-4f3e-bec6-da593663a0d3","3fcc3ad7-6211-4a1b-9a34-644dd761b715"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Progressive neurodegeneration impairs cognition, communication, mobility, and swallowing. Complications such as infection and aspiration interact with frailty; care decisions should reflect prior wishes and current comfort. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Progressive neurodegeneration impairs cognition, communication, mobility, and swallowing. Complications such as infection and aspiration interact with frailty","care decisions should reflect prior wishes and current comfort."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Advanced Dementia and Comfort-Focused Care, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Acute choking or respiratory distress","Pain, fracture, or untreated infection","Family conflict affecting immediate care","Caregiver burnout or neglect risk"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Delirium on dementia","distinguishingFeatures":"Acute change warrants reversible-cause assessment."},{"condition":"Depression or medication sedation","distinguishingFeatures":"May worsen function and intake."},{"condition":"Dysphagia from stroke or structural lesion","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess if presentation is abrupt or focal."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Collateral history, pain and swallowing assessment, medication review, hydration/nutrition status and focused exam.","modalityTarget":"Collateral history, pain and swallowing assessment, medication review, hydration/nutrition status and focused exam. — Advanced Dementia and Comfort-Focused Care","targetCondition":"Advanced Dementia and Comfort-Focused Care","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Investigate only when likely to change goal-concordant care; involve speech-language and nutrition teams.","modalityTarget":"Investigate only when likely to change goal-concordant care; involve speech-language and nutrition teams. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Advanced Dementia and Comfort-Focused Care","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Advanced Dementia and Comfort-Focused Care","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Advanced Dementia and Comfort-Focused Care","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Advanced Dementia and Comfort-Focused Care","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Support eating and drinking and assess swallowing concerns with speech and language input.","Avoid routine enteral feeding in severe dementia unless a potentially reversible comorbidity provides a specific indication; agree anticipatory and palliative plans."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"