able plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"1f3a8674-fb1a-4c14-9744-8ae2d3eed686","original_version_ids":["c3e27ed6-8882-433e-bfac-78e7390372db","decfdfde-5f89-4a20-8f25-ff5b0cbd9bac"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng106/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"1f3a8674-fb1a-4c14-9744-8ae2d3eed686","title":"Advanced Heart Failure Supportive Care","specialty":"Cardiology / Palliative Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Palliative Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Heart-failure symptom support alongside disease-modifying care.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","Heart-failure symptom support alongside disease-modifying care.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["c3e27ed6-8882-433e-bfac-78e7390372db","decfdfde-5f89-4a20-8f25-ff5b0cbd9bac"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Progressive pump dysfunction causes congestion, fatigue, and episodic decompensation. Symptom management, planning, and specialist heart-failure treatment can proceed concurrently and adapt to changing goals. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Progressive pump dysfunction causes congestion, fatigue, and episodic decompensation. Symptom management, planning, and specialist heart-failure treatment can proceed concurrently and adapt to changing goals.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Advanced Heart Failure Supportive Care, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Acute decompensation or new ischaemia requiring assessment consistent with goals","Refractory dyspnoea or oedema","Repeated crisis admissions or caregiver exhaustion","Device shock or distressing therapy"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"COPD or infection","distinguishingFeatures":"May coexist and alter breathlessness plan."},{"condition":"Depression/anxiety","distinguishingFeatures":"Can intensify symptom burden and need direct support."},{"condition":"Renal deterioration or anaemia","distinguishingFeatures":"May worsen fatigue and congestion."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Review heart-failure phenotype, symptoms, admissions, medicines, renal function, device status and patient priorities.","modalityTarget":"Review heart-failure phenotype, symptoms, admissions, medicines, renal function, device status and patient priorities. — Advanced Heart Failure Supportive Care","targetCondition":"Advanced Heart Failure Supportive Care","expectedFinding":"A result that supports the working diagnosis or defines its severity, interpreted with the clinical picture and current criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Choose this investigation because it can confirm the suspected process, establish baseline risk, or change the next decision in this case."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Use focused testing when it changes treatment or comfort plan; reconcile advance-care documentation.","modalityTarget":"Use focused testing when it changes treatment or comfort plan; reconcile advance-care documentation. — Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Advanced Heart Failure Supportive Care","targetCondition":"Cause, complication, or risk relevant to Advanced Heart Failure Supportive Care","expectedFinding":"A result that may identify a precipitating factor or complication; interpret in context rather than as a stand-alone diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"This helps detect an important alternative or complication and informs safe monitoring and referral."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses","modalityTarget":"Focused evaluation for the leading alternative diagnoses — Important alternative to Advanced Heart Failure Supportive Care","targetCondition":"Important alternative to Advanced Heart Failure Supportive Care","expectedFinding":"Findings that lower the likelihood of the selected alternative; a normal result does not exclude every urgent cause.","clinicalRationale":"The differential matters because it changes urgency or treatment and should be actively considered."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated","modalityTarget":"Serial clinical reassessment with targeted repeat testing when indicated — Progression or evolving complication","targetCondition":"Progression or evolving complication","expectedFinding":"Stable or improving clinical trend without new evidence of the suspected complication.","clinicalRationale":"A single early assessment may miss an evolving problem; repeat only when it can guide care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Review symptom burden and discuss palliative support according to need and preferences.","Coordinate the heart-failure team, primary care and palliative services; do not use a prognostic score alone to restrict access to supportive care."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"82db41ca-2202-4819-8990-f9bf3a153a77","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng106/chapter