 and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"3f22251d-c5e6-4dfa-b52c-599b05e0bd4c","original_version_ids":["100862de-32b3-44a5-a4a4-a280f9bc4495"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng201/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"3f22251d-c5e6-4dfa-b52c-599b05e0bd4c","title":"Antenatal Care for Uncomplicated Pregnancy","specialty":"Obstetrics","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Safe Birth","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Uncomplicated antenatal care; local screening availability requires adaptation.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Uncomplicated antenatal care; local screening availability requires adaptation."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["100862de-32b3-44a5-a4a4-a280f9bc4495"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Pregnancy causes coordinated cardiovascular, renal, endocrine, and immune adaptations to support fetal growth. Antenatal care detects maternal/fetal risks, supports prevention, and provides timely response to emerging complications. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Pregnancy causes coordinated cardiovascular, renal, endocrine, and immune adaptations to support fetal growth. Antenatal care detects maternal/fetal risks, supports prevention, and provides timely response to emerging complications.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Antenatal Care for Uncomplicated Pregnancy, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Bleeding with pain or syncope","Severe headache, visual change, or upper abdominal pain later in pregnancy","Reduced fetal movement after the expected pattern is established","Fever, fluid loss, or preterm contractions"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Ectopic pregnancy","distinguishingFeatures":"Pain/bleeding and uncertain location require urgent assessment."},{"condition":"Molar pregnancy","distinguishingFeatures":"Symptoms or ultrasound pattern may suggest abnormal gestation."},{"condition":"High-risk pregnancy","distinguishingFeatures":"Comorbidity or prior complication changes care setting and schedule."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Dating ultrasound and gestation-appropriate fetal screening","modalityTarget":"Dating ultrasound and gestation-appropriate fetal screening — Gestational age, fetal number and structural/developmental concerns","targetCondition":"Gestational age, fetal number and structural/developmental concerns","expectedFinding":"Biometry establishes dating; screening findings may identify a need for specialist assessment rather than a definitive diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"Sets the pregnancy timetable and offers informed, risk-appropriate screening under the Saudi antenatal pathway."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Full blood count","modalityTarget":"Full blood count — Anaemia or platelet abnormality","targetCondition":"Anaemia or platelet abnormality","expectedFinding":"Low haemoglobin or abnormal platelets require assessment using pregnancy-appropriate reference ranges.","clinicalRationale":"Detects maternal haematological problems that influence care and delivery planning."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Blood group, RhD and antibody screen","modalityTarget":"Blood group, RhD and antibody screen — RhD status and clinically significant red-cell antibodies","targetCondition":"RhD status and clinically significant red-cell antibodies","expectedFinding":"Antibody identification determines whether fetal risk or specialist follow-up is present.","clinicalRationale":"Supports alloimmunisation prevention and management using the current obstetric protocol."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Infection screening selected by the antenatal pathway","modalityTarget":"Infection screening selected by the antenatal pathway — Maternal infection with implications for pregnancy or the newborn","targetCondition":"Maternal infection with implications for pregnancy or the newborn","expectedFinding":"Interpret each named assay using the current screening/confirmation algorithm.","clinicalRationale":"Enables timely maternal treatment and prevention of transmission; the exact tests and consent requirements follow local policy."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Arrange timely booking, explain the antenatal schedule and review medical, obstetric and psychosocial risks.","Assess blood pressure, fetal growth and movement concerns at the recommended contacts, and move to a specialist pathway if complications develop."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"10d7b787-827f-4590-8cc5-2a59d22d6311","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng201/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.2","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Uncomplicated antenatal care; local screening availability requires adaptation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Dating ultrasound and gestation-appropriate fetal screening","clinical_question":"Gestational age, fetal number and structural/developmental concerns","expected_finding":"Biometry establishes dating; screening findings may identify a need for specialist assessment rather than a definitive diagnosis.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Sets the pregnancy timetable and offers informed, risk-appropriate screening under the Saudi antenatal pathway.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Full blood count","clinical_question":"Anaemia or platelet abnormality","expected_finding":"Low haemoglobin or abnormal platelets require assessment using pregnancy-appropriate reference ranges.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects maternal haematological problems that influence care and delivery planning.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Blood group, RhD and antibody screen","clinical_question":"RhD status and clinically significant red-cell antibodies","expected_finding":"Antibody identification determines whether fetal risk or specialist follow-up is present.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports alloimmunisation prevention and management using the current obstetric protocol.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Infection screening selected by the antenatal pathway","clinical_question":"Maternal infection with implications for pregnancy or the newborn","expected_finding":"Interpret each named assay using the current screening/confirmation algorithm.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Enables timely maternal treatment and prevention of transmission; the exact tests and consent requirements follow local policy.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"10d7b787-827f-4590-8cc5-2a59d22d6311","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng201/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.2","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Uncomplicated antenatal care; local screening availability requires adaptation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Arrange timely booking, explain the antenatal schedule and review medical, obstetric and psychosocial risks.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Assess blood pressure, fetal growth and movement concerns at the recommended contacts, and move to a specialist pathway if complications develop.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"10d7b787-827f-4590-8cc5-2a59d22d6311","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng201/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.2","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Uncomplicated antenatal care; local screening availability requires adaptation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain antenatal care for uncomplicated pregnancy in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Obstetrics","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"ce9316d7-2fe5-415d-a633-b0ebb79a4693","original_version_ids":["7a518026-5235-46d1-999c-412ed45c39cf"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"ce9316d7-2fe5-415d-a633-b0ebb79a4693","title":"Asthma","specialty":"Respiratory Medicine / Primary Care","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Chronic Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Chronic asthma; age-specific treatment must remain distinct from acute attacks.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Chronic asthma; age-specific treatment must remain distinct from acute attacks."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["7a518026-5235-46d1-999c-412ed45c39cf"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Airway inflammation and hyperresponsiveness cause variable bronchoconstriction and airflow limitation. Symptoms may fluctuate, while risk of severe exacerbation persists even between apparently well periods. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Airway inflammation and hyperresponsiveness cause variable bronchoconstriction and airflow limitation. Symptoms may fluctuate, while risk of severe exacerbation persists even between apparently well periods.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Asthma, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Silent chest or inability to speak during attack","Night waking or reliever use rising rapidly","Prior intensive-care admission or severe attack","Persistent symptoms despite verified treatment and technique"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"COPD","distinguishingFeatures":"Persistent obstruction and exposure history may suggest another or overlapping diagnosis."},{"condition":"Vocal cord dysfunction","distinguishingFeatures":"Inspiratory symptoms and targeted assessment may clarify."},{"condition":"Heart failure or anaphylaxis","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess cardiovascular or acute multisystem allergic features."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Spirometry with bronchodilator response","modalityTarget":"Spirometry with bronchodilator response — Variable expiratory airflow limitation","targetCondition":"Variable expiratory airflow limitation","expectedFinding":"Obstruction with reversibility supports asthma; normal spirometry between episodes does not exclude it.","clinicalRationale":"Provides objective support for the diagnosis instead of relying on symptoms alone."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Peak-flow diary when indicated","modalityTarget":"Peak-flow diary when indicated — Variability in expiratory airflow","targetCondition":"Variability in expiratory airflow","expectedFinding":"Variation over time or with exposure supports variable airflow limitation when measurements are reliable.","clinicalRationale":"Helps investigate intermittent or work-related symptoms when office spirometry is inconclusive."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Focused assessment for competing causes of wheeze or dyspnoea","modalityTarget":"Focused assessment for competing causes of wheeze or dyspnoea — COPD, cardiac disease, upper-airway dysfunction or another mimic","targetCondition":"COPD, cardiac disease, upper-airway dysfunction or another mimic","expectedFinding":"Smoking history, fixed obstruction, cardiac signs or upper-airway symptoms direct additional testing.","clinicalRationale":"Prevents misdiagnosis; select a named additional test only for the suspected alternative."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Confirm a compatible clinical history with objective testing; account for the effect of existing inhaled steroid treatment on results.","For newly diagnosed asthma at age 12 or over, consider the NICE as-needed low-dose ICS/formoterol AIR branch, with locally licensed products and a written action plan."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; 1.6; 1.7; supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Chronic asthma; age-specific treatment must remain distinct from acute attacks. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Spirometry with bronchodilator response","clinical_question":"Variable expiratory airflow limitation","expected_finding":"Obstruction with reversibility supports asthma; normal spirometry between episodes does not exclude it.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides objective support for the diagnosis instead of relying on symptoms alone.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Peak-flow diary when indicated","clinical_question":"Variability in expiratory airflow","expected_finding":"Variation over time or with exposure supports variable airflow limitation when measurements are reliable.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Helps investigate intermittent or work-related symptoms when office spirometry is inconclusive.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Focused assessment for competing causes of wheeze or dyspnoea","clinical_question":"COPD, cardiac disease, upper-airway dysfunction or another mimic","expected_finding":"Smoking history, fixed obstruction, cardiac signs or upper-airway symptoms direct additional testing.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Prevents misdiagnosis; select a named additional test only for the suspected alternative.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; 1.6; 1.7; supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Chronic asthma; age-specific treatment must remain distinct from acute attacks. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Confirm a compatible clinical history with objective testing; account for the effect of existing inhaled steroid treatment on results.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"For newly diagnosed asthma at age 12 or over, consider the NICE as-needed low-dose ICS/formoterol AIR branch, with locally licensed products and a written action plan.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"7e192f39-5cc8-4f88-827f-358c8dd39ea0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng245/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; 1.6; 1.7; supported self-management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Chronic asthma; age-specific treatment must remain distinct from acute attacks. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain asthma in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Respiratory Medicine / Primary Care","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"a1020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","original_version_ids":["a1020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng196/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a1020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","title":"Atrial Fibrillation [Adapted from NICE]","specialty":"Cardiology and Internal Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2021-06-30","pillar":"Chronic Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult AF; anticoagulation and cardioversion need individual assessment.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Adult AF; anticoagulation and cardioversion need individual assessment."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["a1020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Atrial fibrillation is a supraventricular tachyarrhythmia with disorganised atrial activation and ineffective atrial contraction. Irregular ventricular conduction can cause symptoms or tachycardia-mediated dysfunction, while atrial blood stasis promotes thrombus formation and systemic embolism.","keyMechanisms":["Ectopic atrial triggers and a susceptible atrial substrate sustain chaotic electrical activation.","Loss of coordinated atrial contraction and irregular atrioventricular conduction reduce haemodynamic efficiency.","Blood stasis, endothelial dysfunction and prothrombotic factors increase left-atrial thrombus and stroke risk.","Hypertension, heart failure, valve disease, thyroid disease, obesity, sleep apnoea and alcohol can promote onset or recurrence."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Palpitations or an irregular heartbeat","Breathlessness or reduced exercise tolerance","Fatigue, dizziness, presyncope or syncope","Chest discomfort or presentation with stroke or transient ischaemic attack"],"physicalSigns":["Irregularly irregular pulse","Variable first heart sound and pulse deficit","Tachycardia or, with conduction disease or medication, bradycardia","Signs of heart failure, valve disease or systemic embolism"],"redFlags":["Haemodynamic instability, shock, ongoing myocardial ischaemia or severe pulmonary oedema","New focal neurological deficit suggesting stroke","Syncope with a very rapid or very slow ventricular response","Acute decompensated heart failure or pre-excited atrial fibrillation"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Atrial flutter with variable block","distinguishingFeatures":"Organised flutter activity on electrocardiogram, often with a regular or patterned ventricular response."},{"condition":"Frequent atrial ectopy","distinguishingFeatures":"Discrete premature P waves with intervening sinus rhythm rather than sustained fibrillatory activity."},{"condition":"Multifocal atrial tachycardia","distinguishingFeatures":"At least three P-wave morphologies and an isoelectric baseline, often in severe pulmonary disease."},{"condition":"Sinus tachycardia with artefact","distinguishingFeatures":"Consistent P waves and a physiological trigger; careful lead review separates artefact from atrial activity."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"12-lead electrocardiogram","modalityTarget":"12-lead electrocardiogram — Atrial fibrillation","targetCondition":"Atrial fibrillation","expectedFinding":"Irregularly irregular R-R intervals with no consistent discrete P waves.","clinicalRationale":"Provides rhythm confirmation and identifies conduction, ischaemic or pre-excitation features that alter management."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Ambulatory electrocardiographic monitoring","modalityTarget":"Ambulatory electrocardiographic monitoring — Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation","targetCondition":"Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation","expectedFinding":"Intermittent electrocardiographically documented atrial fibrillation during symptoms or silent episodes.","clinicalRationale":"Monitoring duration should match symptom frequency when the resting electrocardiogram is normal."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Transthoracic echocardiography when indicated","modalityTarget":"Transthoracic echocardiography when indicated — Structural or functional heart disease","targetCondition":"Structural or functional heart disease","expectedFinding":"Atrial enlargement, ventricular dysfunction, valve disease or another finding that changes management.","clinicalRationale":"Supports rhythm-control planning, heart-failure assessment and selected refinement of thromboembolic risk."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Thyroid function testing","modalityTarget":"Thyroid function testing — Thyrotoxicosis","targetCondition":"Thyrotoxicosis","expectedFinding":"No biochemical hyperthyroidism, or a reversible driver is identified.","clinicalRationale":"Thyroid disease can precipitate atrial fibrillation and requires concurrent treatment."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Electrolytes, renal and liver function","modalityTarget":"Electrolytes, renal and liver function — Metabolic precipitant or medicine contraindication","targetCondition":"Metabolic precipitant or medicine contraindication","expectedFinding":"No correctable electrolyte disturbance; organ function is adequate for the selected medicine or prompts adjustment.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies reversible contributors and is essential before anticoagulant or antiarrhythmic selection."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Acute coronary and pulmonary assessment when clinically indicated","modalityTarget":"Acute coronary and pulmonary assessment when clinically indicated — Acute coronary syndrome or pulmonary embolism","targetCondition":"Acute coronary syndrome or pulmonary embolism","expectedFinding":"No acute ischaemic or thromboembolic trigger, or one is identified and treated through its urgent pathway.","clinicalRationale":"New atrial fibrillation may be secondary to another time-critical condition."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Confirm AF on a 12-lead ECG, using ambulatory monitoring when episodes are intermittent.","Assess stroke and bleeding risks and discuss appropriate anticoagulation; do not substitute aspirin monotherapy for indicated stroke prevention."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"1d5198bd-cde5-410a-84f5-9db40e7cd9b4","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng196/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.2; 1.6; rate and rhythm control","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult AF; anticoagulation and cardioversion need individual assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"12-lead electrocardiogram","clinical_question":"Atrial fibrillation","expected_finding":"Irregularly irregular R-R intervals with no consistent discrete P waves.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides rhythm confirmation and identifies conduction, ischaemic or pre-excitation features that alter management.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Ambulatory electrocardiographic monitoring","clinical_question":"Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation","expected_finding":"Intermittent electrocardiographically documented atrial fibrillation during symptoms or silent episodes.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Monitoring duration should match symptom frequency when the resting electrocardiogram is normal.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Transthoracic echocardiography when indicated","clinical_question":"Structural or functional heart disease","expected_finding":"Atrial enlargement, ventricular dysfunction, valve disease or another finding that changes management.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports rhythm-control planning, heart-failure assessment and selected refinement of thromboembolic risk.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Thyroid function testing","clinical_question":"Thyrotoxicosis","expected_finding":"No biochemical hyperthyroidism, or a reversible driver is identified.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Thyroid disease can precipitate atrial fibrillation and requires concurrent treatment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Electrolytes, renal and liver function","clinical_question":"Metabolic precipitant or medicine contraindication","expected_finding":"No correctable electrolyte disturbance; organ function is adequate for the selected medicine or prompts adjustment.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies reversible contributors and is essential before anticoagulant or antiarrhythmic selection.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Acute coronary and pulmonary assessment when clinically indicated","clinical_question":"Acute coronary syndrome or pulmonary embolism","expected_finding":"No acute ischaemic or thromboembolic trigger, or one is identified and treated through its urgent pathway.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: New atrial fibrillation may be secondary to another time-critical condition.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"1d5198bd-cde5-410a-84f5-9db40e7cd9b4","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng196/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.2; 1.6; rate and rhythm control","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult AF; anticoagulation and cardioversion need individual assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Confirm AF on a 12-lead ECG, using ambulatory monitoring when episodes are intermittent.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Assess stroke and bleeding risks and discuss appropriate anticoagulation; do not substitute aspirin monotherapy for indicated stroke prevention.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"1d5198bd-cde5-410a-84f5-9db40e7cd9b4","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng196/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.2; 1.6; rate and rhythm control","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult AF; anticoagulation and cardioversion need individual assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain the irregular rhythm, symptom-control options and the distinct purpose of anticoagulation.","Teach stroke warning signs and the need for immediate emergency assessment.","Provide medicine-specific bleeding, missed-dose, procedure and interaction advice using approved Saudi information."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Support weight management, regular physical activity and control of blood pressure and diabetes.","Screen for and treat obstructive sleep apnoea when suspected.","Reduce excessive alcohol and stimulant exposure and stop smoking.","For warfarin, advise consistency rather than avoidance of vitamin-K-containing foods and arrange INR education."],"mdtReferrals":["Cardiology or electrophysiology for rhythm-control and ablation decisions","Anticoagulation or clinical pharmacy service for medicine selection, interactions and adherence","Stroke service for any acute or previous cerebrovascular event","Sleep medicine and weight-management services where relevant"],"dischargeCriteria":["Haemodynamics are stable and acute triggers have been addressed.","A rate/rhythm strategy and anticoagulation decision are documented with renal-function-appropriate prescribing.","The patient understands stroke and bleeding precautions and has timely follow-up."],"followUpPlan":"Review symptoms, pulse/rate, blood pressure, anticoagulant adherence, bleeding risk and renal function at a medicine-appropriate interval; reassess stroke risk at least annually and whenever age or comorbidity changes."}}},{"guideline_id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006","original_version_ids":["a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng101/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006","title":"Breast Cancer Management","specialty":"Medical Oncology, Breast Surgery and Radiation Oncology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2018-01-01","pillar":"Planned Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Early and locally advanced disease only; advanced breast cancer requires CG81 and current technology-appraisal review. The 2018 Saudi source alone cannot verify current systemic treatment.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Early and locally advanced disease only; advanced breast cancer requires CG81 and current technology-appraisal review. The 2018 Saudi source alone cannot verify current systemic treatment."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Breast cancer comprises malignant epithelial tumours with heterogeneous hormone-receptor, HER2 and genomic biology. Disease may remain in situ, invade breast and regional lymphatics, or spread haematogenously to bone, liver, lung and brain; biology and stage jointly determine treatment and prognosis.","keyMechanisms":["Accumulated genomic and epigenetic alterations enable uncontrolled proliferation and invasion.","Oestrogen/progesterone-receptor signalling and HER2 amplification define actionable biological subsets.","Lymphatic spread commonly involves axillary and regional nodes.","Tumour heterogeneity and treatment selection pressure can change receptor status in recurrent disease."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["New breast or axillary lump","Nipple retraction or bloody discharge","Persistent focal breast change or skin dimpling","Bone pain, breathlessness, neurological symptoms or weight loss in advanced disease"],"physicalSigns":["Discrete breast mass or asymmetric thickening","Peau d'orange, ulceration or inflammatory change","Nipple inversion or eczematous nipple lesion","Palpable axillary or supraclavicular nodes"],"redFlags":["Rapidly progressive inflammatory breast change","Spinal pain with weakness, sensory change or bladder/bowel dysfunction","New focal neurological deficit, seizure or raised intracranial-pressure symptoms","Visceral crisis with organ dysfunction requiring rapid oncology assessment"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Fibroadenoma","distinguishingFeatures":"Often mobile, well-circumscribed and benign on age-appropriate imaging, but tissue diagnosis is required when assessment is discordant."},{"condition":"Breast cyst","distinguishingFeatures":"Fluid-filled lesion on ultrasound with resolution after aspiration in selected cases."},{"condition":"Mastitis or abscess","distinguishingFeatures":"Pain, erythema, fever and a collection; non-resolution requires investigation for inflammatory malignancy."},{"condition":"Fat necrosis","distinguishingFeatures":"History of trauma or surgery with characteristic imaging, although biopsy may be needed if suspicious."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Triple assessment","modalityTarget":"Triple assessment — Breast malignancy","targetCondition":"Breast malignancy","expectedFinding":"Concordant suspicious clinical examination, mammography/ultrasound and core-biopsy histology.","clinicalRationale":"Integrates anatomy and tissue diagnosis while minimising false reassurance from any single test."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Histopathology with ER, PR and HER2 testing","modalityTarget":"Histopathology with ER, PR and HER2 testing — Invasive breast-cancer subtype","targetCondition":"Invasive breast-cancer subtype","expectedFinding":"Malignant morphology with grade and validated receptor status.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms diagnosis and directs endocrine, anti-HER2 and chemotherapy decisions."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Stage-directed imaging","modalityTarget":"Stage-directed imaging — Regional or distant metastatic disease","targetCondition":"Regional or distant metastatic disease","expectedFinding":"Imaging defines tumour, nodal and metastatic burden when stage or symptoms justify it.","clinicalRationale":"Avoids indiscriminate staging in low-risk disease while identifying treatment-changing metastases."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Image-guided core biopsy of a suspicious benign-appearing lesion","modalityTarget":"Image-guided core biopsy of a suspicious benign-appearing lesion — Benign breast disease","targetCondition":"Benign breast disease","expectedFinding":"Pathology is benign and concordant with clinical and imaging findings.","clinicalRationale":"Discordance requires repeat sampling or excision rather than simple reassurance."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Targeted imaging of new symptoms","modalityTarget":"Targeted imaging of new symptoms — Metastatic complication","targetCondition":"Metastatic complication","expectedFinding":"No metastasis explaining the symptom, or a lesion is identified for urgent management.","clinicalRationale":"Routine surveillance imaging in asymptomatic early-stage survivors is not a substitute for symptom-led assessment."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Confirm diagnosis, stage, receptor profile and fitness before multidisciplinary treatment planning.","Select surgery, radiotherapy and systemic treatment by stage and biomarkers; check current recommendations and local oncology access rather than adopting a historical drug list."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"525840b3-4689-445c-8d0b-093abe97562e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng101/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Diagnosis; multidisciplinary management; systemic treatment","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Early and locally advanced disease only; advanced breast cancer requires CG81 and current technology-appraisal review. The 2018 Saudi source alone cannot verify current systemic treatment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Triple assessment","clinical_question":"Breast malignancy","expected_finding":"Concordant suspicious clinical examination, mammography/ultrasound and core-biopsy histology.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Integrates anatomy and tissue diagnosis while minimising false reassurance from any single test.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Histopathology with ER, PR and HER2 testing","clinical_question":"Invasive breast-cancer subtype","expected_finding":"Malignant morphology with grade and validated receptor status.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Confirms diagnosis and directs endocrine, anti-HER2 and chemotherapy decisions.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Stage-directed imaging","clinical_question":"Regional or distant metastatic disease","expected_finding":"Imaging defines tumour, nodal and metastatic burden when stage or symptoms justify it.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Avoids indiscriminate staging in low-risk disease while identifying treatment-changing metastases.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Image-guided core biopsy of a suspicious benign-appearing lesion","clinical_question":"Benign breast disease","expected_finding":"Pathology is benign and concordant with clinical and imaging findings.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Discordance requires repeat sampling or excision rather than simple reassurance.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Targeted imaging of new symptoms","clinical_question":"Metastatic complication","expected_finding":"No metastasis explaining the symptom, or a lesion is identified for urgent management.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Routine surveillance imaging in asymptomatic early-stage survivors is not a substitute for symptom-led assessment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"525840b3-4689-445c-8d0b-093abe97562e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng101/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Diagnosis; multidisciplinary management; systemic treatment","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Early and locally advanced disease only; advanced breast cancer requires CG81 and current technology-appraisal review. The 2018 Saudi source alone cannot verify current systemic treatment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Confirm diagnosis, stage, receptor profile and fitness before multidisciplinary treatment planning.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Select surgery, radiotherapy and systemic treatment by stage and biomarkers; check current recommendations and local oncology access rather than adopting a historical drug list.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"525840b3-4689-445c-8d0b-093abe97562e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng101/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Diagnosis; multidisciplinary management; systemic treatment","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Early and locally advanced disease only; advanced breast cancer requires CG81 and current technology-appraisal review. The 2018 Saudi source alone cannot verify current systemic treatment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain stage, receptor status, treatment intent and the role of each modality in plain language.","Discuss expected adverse effects, fertility, sexual health, pregnancy considerations and when to seek urgent care.","Provide individualised information on recurrence symptoms without encouraging harmful routine self-testing."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Support regular physical activity and maintenance of a healthy body composition during and after treatment.","Provide dietetic advice for treatment-related weight change, nausea or malnutrition.","Offer smoking-cessation support and advise avoidance of unreviewed supplements that may interact with therapy."],"mdtReferrals":["Breast surgeon, medical oncologist, radiation oncologist and breast-care nurse","Genetics for hereditary-risk criteria","Fertility service before gonadotoxic treatment when relevant","Physiotherapy/lymphoedema, psycho-oncology and palliative care according to need"],"dischargeCriteria":["The diagnosis, stage, receptor profile and MDT plan are documented.","Acute treatment complications are controlled and the patient has clear contacts.","Surveillance ownership, medicine monitoring and urgent symptom pathways are explicit."],"followUpPlan":"Follow the current Saudi oncology surveillance schedule, including clinical review and mammography where breast tissue remains; monitor therapy-specific cardiac, bone, gynaecological and lymphoedema risks and investigate new symptoms promptly."}}},{"guideline_id":"d2743507-415a-4bc7-8857-3604c97bab42","original_version_ids":["05890fd0-f671-46fd-9fd2-28d0acaca968"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg164/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"d2743507-415a-4bc7-8857-3604c97bab42","title":"Breast Cancer Screening Discussion","specialty":"Primary Care / Public Health","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Familial-risk surveillance only; population screening ages and intervals require current Saudi programme evidence.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Diagnostic referral or uptake guidance is not sufficient evidence for a Saudi population screening or vaccination schedule.","Familial-risk surveillance only; population screening ages and intervals require current Saudi programme evidence."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["05890fd0-f671-46fd-9fd2-28d0acaca968"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Screening aims to detect clinically important cancer earlier in asymptomatic populations but can cause false positives, overdiagnosis, anxiety, and unnecessary procedures. Absolute benefit varies with baseline risk and age. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Screening aims to detect clinically important cancer earlier in asymptomatic populations but can cause false positives, overdiagnosis, anxiety, and unnecessary procedures. Absolute benefit varies with baseline risk and age.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Breast Cancer Screening Discussion, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["New lump, nipple retraction/discharge or skin change is diagnostic assessment, not screening","Strong hereditary pattern or young affected relative","Prior chest irradiation or high-risk lesion","Pregnancy/lactation with new symptom"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Symptomatic breast disease","distinguishingFeatures":"Needs diagnostic examination/imaging rather than routine screening."},{"condition":"High-risk inherited susceptibility","distinguishingFeatures":"May need genetics and a different imaging pathway."},{"condition":"Benign palpable change","distinguishingFeatures":"Still requires assessment based on age and finding."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"firstLineImaging","testName":"Screening mammography when eligible","modalityTarget":"Screening mammography when eligible — Suspicious breast lesions before symptoms develop","targetCondition":"Suspicious breast lesions before symptoms develop","expectedFinding":"A recall or abnormal imaging category requires further assessment; a negative screen does not explain a new symptom.","clinicalRationale":"Detects possible early disease in eligible asymptomatic patients after discussion of benefits and harms."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Structured breast-cancer risk and symptom assessment","modalityTarget":"Structured breast-cancer risk and symptom assessment — High-risk family history or a symptom requiring diagnostic assessment","targetCondition":"High-risk family history or a symptom requiring diagnostic assessment","expectedFinding":"A lump, skin/nipple change or important hereditary pattern changes the pathway.","clinicalRationale":"Separates asymptomatic screening from symptomatic diagnosis and selects the appropriate Saudi programme or specialist referral."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Assess family history and eligibility for genetics or enhanced surveillance.","Discuss benefits and harms; do not extrapolate familial-risk surveillance schedules to all asymptomatic adults."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"749ea801-0286-47a7-8e4c-89b4033f27e7","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg164/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Familial risk assessment and surveillance","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Familial-risk surveillance only; population screening ages and intervals require current Saudi programme evidence. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Screening mammography when eligible","clinical_question":"Suspicious breast lesions before symptoms develop","expected_finding":"A recall or abnormal imaging category requires further assessment; a negative screen does not explain a new symptom.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects possible early disease in eligible asymptomatic patients after discussion of benefits and harms.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Structured breast-cancer risk and symptom assessment","clinical_question":"High-risk family history or a symptom requiring diagnostic assessment","expected_finding":"A lump, skin/nipple change or important hereditary pattern changes the pathway.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Separates asymptomatic screening from symptomatic diagnosis and selects the appropriate Saudi programme or specialist referral.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"749ea801-0286-47a7-8e4c-89b4033f27e7","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg164/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Familial risk assessment and surveillance","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Familial-risk surveillance only; population screening ages and intervals require current Saudi programme evidence. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Assess family history and eligibility for genetics or enhanced surveillance.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Discuss benefits and harms; do not extrapolate familial-risk surveillance schedules to all asymptomatic adults.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"749ea801-0286-47a7-8e4c-89b4033f27e7","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg164/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Familial risk assessment and surveillance","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Familial-risk surveillance only; population screening ages and intervals require current Saudi programme evidence. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain breast cancer screening discussion in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary Care / Public Health","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"cc78da1f-1df1-477a-b691-56ef783e4054","original_version_ids":["30f722bf-7337-489e-b5b4-d3df0a66a6d6"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg140/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"cc78da1f-1df1-477a-b691-56ef783e4054","title":"Cancer Pain Assessment and Support","specialty":"Palliative Medicine / Oncology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Palliative Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult strong-opioid support; complete oncology pain and renal-dose review remains required.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Adult strong-opioid support; complete oncology pain and renal-dose review remains required."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["30f722bf-7337-489e-b5b4-d3df0a66a6d6"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Cancer pain may arise from tissue injury, inflammation, bone destruction, nerve infiltration, treatment, or interacting mechanisms. Relief requires repeated assessment of both pain and function while minimising adverse effects. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Cancer pain may arise from tissue injury, inflammation, bone destruction, nerve infiltration, treatment, or interacting mechanisms. Relief requires repeated assessment of both pain and function while minimising adverse effects.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Cancer Pain Assessment and Support, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["New weakness, sensory loss, or bladder/bowel dysfunction","Sudden severe pain suggesting fracture or cord compression","Uncontrolled pain or medication toxicity","New delirium, respiratory suppression, or falls"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Neuropathic pain","distinguishingFeatures":"Burning, shooting, allodynia, or sensory change may indicate nerve involvement."},{"condition":"Incident/bone pain","distinguishingFeatures":"Movement-related focal pain suggests structural complication."},{"condition":"Treatment-related pain","distinguishingFeatures":"Temporal relation to therapy or procedure informs cause."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Pain score, pain-character and neurological assessment","modalityTarget":"Pain score, pain-character and neurological assessment — Pain severity, neuropathic features and neurological compromise","targetCondition":"Pain severity, neuropathic features and neurological compromise","expectedFinding":"Document intensity, interference, neuropathic descriptors and any motor/sensory deficit.","clinicalRationale":"Defines the likely pain mechanism and identifies emergencies such as possible cord compression."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Creatinine and liver tests when prescribing decisions require them","modalityTarget":"Creatinine and liver tests when prescribing decisions require them — Impaired drug clearance","targetCondition":"Impaired drug clearance","expectedFinding":"Renal or hepatic dysfunction may increase medicine accumulation and toxicity.","clinicalRationale":"Informs analgesic selection and monitoring under the palliative formulary."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"Targeted imaging for suspected structural complication","modalityTarget":"Targeted imaging for suspected structural complication — Pathological fracture, spinal cord compression or obstructive disease","targetCondition":"Pathological fracture, spinal cord compression or obstructive disease","expectedFinding":"Imaging may show the lesion responsible for focal pain or new neurological signs.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies a treatable complication; choose the modality and urgency for the specific clinical question."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Discuss strong-opioid benefits, adverse effects and the plan for breakthrough pain when indicated.","Review constipation, nausea and sedation; seek specialist advice for significant renal or hepatic impairment before choosing or adjusting an opioid."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f94adccb-d920-4477-8d73-7c2954731267","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg140/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Starting strong opioids; breakthrough pain; adverse effects","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult strong-opioid support; complete oncology pain and renal-dose review remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Pain score, pain-character and neurological assessment","clinical_question":"Pain severity, neuropathic features and neurological compromise","expected_finding":"Document intensity, interference, neuropathic descriptors and any motor/sensory deficit.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Defines the likely pain mechanism and identifies emergencies such as possible cord compression.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Creatinine and liver tests when prescribing decisions require them","clinical_question":"Impaired drug clearance","expected_finding":"Renal or hepatic dysfunction may increase medicine accumulation and toxicity.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Informs analgesic selection and monitoring under the palliative formulary.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Targeted imaging for suspected structural complication","clinical_question":"Pathological fracture, spinal cord compression or obstructive disease","expected_finding":"Imaging may show the lesion responsible for focal pain or new neurological signs.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies a treatable complication; choose the modality and urgency for the specific clinical question.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f94adccb-d920-4477-8d73-7c2954731267","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg140/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Starting strong opioids; breakthrough pain; adverse effects","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult strong-opioid support; complete oncology pain and renal-dose review remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Discuss strong-opioid benefits, adverse effects and the plan for breakthrough pain when indicated.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Review constipation, nausea and sedation; seek specialist advice for significant renal or hepatic impairment before choosing or adjusting an opioid.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f94adccb-d920-4477-8d73-7c2954731267","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg140/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Starting strong opioids; breakthrough pain; adverse effects","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult strong-opioid support; complete oncology pain and renal-dose review remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain cancer pain assessment and support in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Palliative Medicine / Oncology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"3eaa3e4b-00e8-4bb1-b98a-c18526c67c8e","original_version_ids":["e43a0221-6095-4d39-abbe-fb8eda044c35"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"3eaa3e4b-00e8-4bb1-b98a-c18526c67c8e","title":"Cardiovascular Risk Assessment","specialty":"Family Medicine / Preventive Cardiology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"UK risk-estimation recommendations require local validation for Saudi use.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","UK risk-estimation recommendations require local validation for Saudi use."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["e43a0221-6095-4d39-abbe-fb8eda044c35"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Atherosclerotic events arise from cumulative vascular exposure and thrombosis; risk-factor combinations alter absolute event probability. Preventive benefit should be judged against baseline risk, treatment burden, and patient preferences. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Atherosclerotic events arise from cumulative vascular exposure and thrombosis","risk-factor combinations alter absolute event probability. Preventive benefit should be judged against baseline risk, treatment burden, and patient preferences."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Cardiovascular Risk Assessment, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Chest pain, focal neurological symptoms or exertional syncope require diagnostic assessment","Severe hypertension with acute organ symptoms","Known vascular disease shifts to secondary prevention","Very high inherited lipid risk"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Secondary prevention","distinguishingFeatures":"Prior cardiovascular event has a different risk and treatment framework."},{"condition":"Familial lipid disorder","distinguishingFeatures":"Marked LDL and family pattern warrant evaluation."},{"condition":"White-coat or masked hypertension","distinguishingFeatures":"Confirm with appropriate repeat or out-of-office measures."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Standardised blood-pressure measurement","modalityTarget":"Standardised blood-pressure measurement — Sustained elevated blood pressure","targetCondition":"Sustained elevated blood pressure","expectedFinding":"Repeated readings and out-of-office confirmation distinguish persistent elevation from measurement effects.","clinicalRationale":"Provides an accurate modifiable-risk measure for the overall cardiovascular assessment."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Lipid profile","modalityTarget":"Lipid profile — Atherogenic lipid burden","targetCondition":"Atherogenic lipid burden","expectedFinding":"LDL and other lipid fractions inform risk estimation and possible inherited dyslipidaemia.","clinicalRationale":"Supports prevention decisions alongside age, smoking, diabetes and established vascular disease."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"HbA1c or fasting glucose and kidney assessment when indicated","modalityTarget":"HbA1c or fasting glucose and kidney assessment when indicated — Diabetes or chronic kidney disease modifying cardiovascular risk","targetCondition":"Diabetes or chronic kidney disease modifying cardiovascular risk","expectedFinding":"Abnormal glycaemia, reduced filtration or albuminuria changes risk categorisation.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies important comorbidity; use a locally accepted risk method and confirm abnormalities appropriately."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Review smoking, blood pressure, lipids, diabetes, renal disease and family history before discussing absolute risk.","Choose a locally appropriate risk tool and discuss prevention benefits, harms and preferences rather than relying on a single laboratory result."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b5b625ed-5749-42c6-8d45-1dbfb60d06c0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Risk assessment; primary prevention","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. UK risk-estimation recommendations require local validation for Saudi use. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Standardised blood-pressure measurement","clinical_question":"Sustained elevated blood pressure","expected_finding":"Repeated readings and out-of-office confirmation distinguish persistent elevation from measurement effects.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides an accurate modifiable-risk measure for the overall cardiovascular assessment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Lipid profile","clinical_question":"Atherogenic lipid burden","expected_finding":"LDL and other lipid fractions inform risk estimation and possible inherited dyslipidaemia.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports prevention decisions alongside age, smoking, diabetes and established vascular disease.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"HbA1c or fasting glucose and kidney assessment when indicated","clinical_question":"Diabetes or chronic kidney disease modifying cardiovascular risk","expected_finding":"Abnormal glycaemia, reduced filtration or albuminuria changes risk categorisation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies important comorbidity; use a locally accepted risk method and confirm abnormalities appropriately.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b5b625ed-5749-42c6-8d45-1dbfb60d06c0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Risk assessment; primary prevention","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. UK risk-estimation recommendations require local validation for Saudi use. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Review smoking, blood pressure, lipids, diabetes, renal disease and family history before discussing absolute risk.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Choose a locally appropriate risk tool and discuss prevention benefits, harms and preferences rather than relying on a single laboratory result.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b5b625ed-5749-42c6-8d45-1dbfb60d06c0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Risk assessment; primary prevention","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. UK risk-estimation recommendations require local validation for Saudi use. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain cardiovascular risk assessment in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Family Medicine / Preventive Cardiology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"eab57274-e256-4281-bd97-7ebe1fb49472","original_version_ids":["8c6180c2-49c8-4391-ac17-f96e447e5be0"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng77/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"eab57274-e256-4281-bd97-7ebe1fb49472","title":"Cataract Surgery Assessment and Preparation","specialty":"Ophthalmology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Planned Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult cataract surgery assessment.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Adult cataract surgery assessment."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["8c6180c2-49c8-4391-ac17-f96e447e5be0"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Lens opacity scatters light and reduces visual function; surgery replaces the opaque lens with an intraocular implant. Benefit depends on cataract contribution, ocular comorbidity, refractive goals, and safe perioperative care. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Lens opacity scatters light and reduces visual function","surgery replaces the opaque lens with an intraocular implant. Benefit depends on cataract contribution, ocular comorbidity, refractive goals, and safe perioperative care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Cataract Surgery Assessment and Preparation, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Sudden visual loss or painful red eye is not routine cataract","Retinal disease or optic neuropathy may limit visual gain","Active ocular infection","Unclear capacity or unrealistic expectations requiring discussion"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Refractive error","distinguishingFeatures":"Refraction may improve symptoms without surgery."},{"condition":"Macular degeneration or diabetic retinopathy","distinguishingFeatures":"May be the limiting cause of visual impairment."},{"condition":"Glaucoma","distinguishingFeatures":"May require separate or combined planning."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Visual acuity and slit-lamp examination","modalityTarget":"Visual acuity and slit-lamp examination — Lens opacity and its effect on vision","targetCondition":"Lens opacity and its effect on vision","expectedFinding":"A cataract consistent with symptoms supports the diagnosis; acuity alone does not establish the cause.","clinicalRationale":"Determines whether cataract is the main source of visual disability and whether surgery is likely to help."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Ocular biometry","modalityTarget":"Ocular biometry — Measurements needed for intraocular-lens selection","targetCondition":"Measurements needed for intraocular-lens selection","expectedFinding":"Axial length and corneal measurements guide lens-power calculation.","clinicalRationale":"Supports surgical planning and reduces avoidable refractive error."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Retinal and optic-nerve assessment","modalityTarget":"Retinal and optic-nerve assessment — Other ocular disease limiting postoperative vision","targetCondition":"Other ocular disease limiting postoperative vision","expectedFinding":"Macular, retinal or optic-nerve abnormalities may reduce the expected benefit.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies competing causes of poor vision and informs consent and referral."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Base referral on the effect on vision and quality of life and the person's preferences, rather than a fixed visual-acuity cutoff.","Complete appropriate biometry and discuss procedure-specific benefits, risks and refractive expectations."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ca6a9840-5c38-47c2-8d2e-c3fadb5d2b8f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng77/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; 1.3","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult cataract surgery assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Visual acuity and slit-lamp examination","clinical_question":"Lens opacity and its effect on vision","expected_finding":"A cataract consistent with symptoms supports the diagnosis; acuity alone does not establish the cause.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Determines whether cataract is the main source of visual disability and whether surgery is likely to help.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Ocular biometry","clinical_question":"Measurements needed for intraocular-lens selection","expected_finding":"Axial length and corneal measurements guide lens-power calculation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports surgical planning and reduces avoidable refractive error.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Retinal and optic-nerve assessment","clinical_question":"Other ocular disease limiting postoperative vision","expected_finding":"Macular, retinal or optic-nerve abnormalities may reduce the expected benefit.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies competing causes of poor vision and informs consent and referral.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ca6a9840-5c38-47c2-8d2e-c3fadb5d2b8f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng77/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; 1.3","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult cataract surgery assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Base referral on the effect on vision and quality of life and the person's preferences, rather than a fixed visual-acuity cutoff.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Complete appropriate biometry and discuss procedure-specific benefits, risks and refractive expectations.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ca6a9840-5c38-47c2-8d2e-c3fadb5d2b8f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng77/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; 1.3","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult cataract surgery assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain cataract surgery assessment and preparation in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Ophthalmology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"3f47a009-d923-4a43-bce4-9357e38111e7","original_version_ids":["9082ec9c-e44e-42a7-9832-e6319d5e8e71"],"source_title":"Recommendations organised by site of cancer","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng12/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"3f47a009-d923-4a43-bce4-9357e38111e7","title":"Cervical Cancer Screening and Follow-Up","specialty":"Primary Care / Gynaecology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Suspected-cancer referral, not a population HPV screening schedule.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Diagnostic referral or uptake guidance is not sufficient evidence for a Saudi population screening or vaccination schedule.","Suspected-cancer referral, not a population HPV screening schedule."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["9082ec9c-e44e-42a7-9832-e6319d5e8e71"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Persistent oncogenic HPV infection can cause cervical epithelial change and invasive cancer. Vaccination and screening reduce risk, while age, prior history, test performance, and follow-up completion determine benefit. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Persistent oncogenic HPV infection can cause cervical epithelial change and invasive cancer. Vaccination and screening reduce risk, while age, prior history, test performance, and follow-up completion determine benefit.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Cervical Cancer Screening and Follow-Up, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Postcoital or unexplained bleeding requires diagnostic assessment","Visible cervical lesion or persistent discharge","Immunosuppression or prior high-grade disease","Pregnancy with a concerning symptom"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Cervical cancer symptom evaluation","distinguishingFeatures":"Symptoms need diagnostic assessment, not screening alone."},{"condition":"Prior high-grade lesion","distinguishingFeatures":"Requires surveillance beyond routine screening."},{"condition":"Pregnancy-related bleeding","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess obstetric and cervical causes appropriately."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"HPV testing or cervical cytology according to the adopted programme","modalityTarget":"HPV testing or cervical cytology according to the adopted programme — High-risk HPV or abnormal cervical cells","targetCondition":"High-risk HPV or abnormal cervical cells","expectedFinding":"A positive HPV result or abnormal cytology requires risk-based triage; neither alone establishes invasive cancer.","clinicalRationale":"Detects risk or precancer in eligible patients and determines tracked follow-up."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Colposcopy and directed biopsy when indicated","modalityTarget":"Colposcopy and directed biopsy when indicated — Cervical intraepithelial neoplasia or invasive disease","targetCondition":"Cervical intraepithelial neoplasia or invasive disease","expectedFinding":"Histology defines the lesion and grade after an abnormal screen or suspicious examination.","clinicalRationale":"Provides diagnostic confirmation before treatment planning."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Assess symptoms or an abnormal-appearing cervix through the appropriate diagnostic and suspected-cancer pathway.","Verify screening eligibility, HPV testing intervals and abnormal-result follow-up using the current Saudi screening programme; symptomatic assessment is separate."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ec2e9e7a-6115-479b-82a1-47782cc5993d","title":"Recommendations organised by site of cancer","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng12/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Gynaecological cancers","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Suspected-cancer referral, not a population HPV screening schedule. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"HPV testing or cervical cytology according to the adopted programme","clinical_question":"High-risk HPV or abnormal cervical cells","expected_finding":"A positive HPV result or abnormal cytology requires risk-based triage; neither alone establishes invasive cancer.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects risk or precancer in eligible patients and determines tracked follow-up.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Colposcopy and directed biopsy when indicated","clinical_question":"Cervical intraepithelial neoplasia or invasive disease","expected_finding":"Histology defines the lesion and grade after an abnormal screen or suspicious examination.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides diagnostic confirmation before treatment planning.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ec2e9e7a-6115-479b-82a1-47782cc5993d","title":"Recommendations organised by site of cancer","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng12/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Gynaecological cancers","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Suspected-cancer referral, not a population HPV screening schedule. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Assess symptoms or an abnormal-appearing cervix through the appropriate diagnostic and suspected-cancer pathway.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Verify screening eligibility, HPV testing intervals and abnormal-result follow-up using the current Saudi screening programme; symptomatic assessment is separate.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ec2e9e7a-6115-479b-82a1-47782cc5993d","title":"Recommendations organised by site of cancer","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng12/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Gynaecological cancers","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Suspected-cancer referral, not a population HPV screening schedule. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain cervical cancer screening and follow-up in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary Care / Gynaecology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"81ec89af-5bc1-40e0-bf3b-52097c45af9f","original_version_ids":["992a2ff7-42f4-4c8f-ab4b-9b5ef430a52f"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng218/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"81ec89af-5bc1-40e0-bf3b-52097c45af9f","title":"Childhood Immunisation and Catch-Up","specialty":"Paediatrics / Public Health","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Uptake and access only; paediatric catch-up intervals and vaccine contraindications require Saudi product/schedule sources.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Diagnostic referral or uptake guidance is not sufficient evidence for a Saudi population screening or vaccination schedule.","Uptake and access only; paediatric catch-up intervals and vaccine contraindications require Saudi product/schedule sources."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["992a2ff7-42f4-4c8f-ab4b-9b5ef430a52f"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Vaccination primes adaptive immune memory and reduces individual disease risk and transmission. Schedule timing, product, immune status, prior doses, and local epidemiology affect protection and catch-up planning. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Vaccination primes adaptive immune memory and reduces individual disease risk and transmission. Schedule timing, product, immune status, prior doses, and local epidemiology affect protection and catch-up planning.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Childhood Immunisation and Catch-Up, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Possible anaphylaxis after a prior dose","Severe acute illness requiring timing assessment","Immunocompromise or complex vaccine history","Exposure requiring time-sensitive prophylaxis"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Incomplete documentation","distinguishingFeatures":"Use registry and prior-provider records; do not assume an undocumented dose was given."},{"condition":"True contraindication","distinguishingFeatures":"Distinguish severe allergy or live-vaccine restriction from minor illness or expected reaction."},{"condition":"Post-vaccine adverse event","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess timing and severity; report through local safety pathway."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Official vaccination record reconciliation","modalityTarget":"Official vaccination record reconciliation — Missing doses and valid prior immunisations","targetCondition":"Missing doses and valid prior immunisations","expectedFinding":"Product, date and dose spacing establish documented protection and catch-up needs.","clinicalRationale":"Builds a catch-up plan using the current Saudi childhood schedule rather than restarting courses automatically."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Contraindication and immune-status history","modalityTarget":"Contraindication and immune-status history — Severe prior reactions or conditions affecting vaccine eligibility","targetCondition":"Severe prior reactions or conditions affecting vaccine eligibility","expectedFinding":"Immunosuppression or a relevant serious reaction may change product choice or timing.","clinicalRationale":"Avoids inappropriate vaccination and identifies children needing specialist advice; routine blood tests are not required for every catch-up visit."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Reconcile reliable vaccination records and identify missed eligible immunisations.","Use the current Saudi age-specific catch-up schedule, with consent and contraindication checks; do not infer dose intervals from this uptake guideline."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"6a326d01-df4c-4fe5-839c-8c0cf9c7c07f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng218/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Identifying eligible people; barriers to uptake","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Uptake and access only; paediatric catch-up intervals and vaccine contraindications require Saudi product/schedule sources. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Official vaccination record reconciliation","clinical_question":"Missing doses and valid prior immunisations","expected_finding":"Product, date and dose spacing establish documented protection and catch-up needs.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Builds a catch-up plan using the current Saudi childhood schedule rather than restarting courses automatically.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Contraindication and immune-status history","clinical_question":"Severe prior reactions or conditions affecting vaccine eligibility","expected_finding":"Immunosuppression or a relevant serious reaction may change product choice or timing.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Avoids inappropriate vaccination and identifies children needing specialist advice; routine blood tests are not required for every catch-up visit.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"6a326d01-df4c-4fe5-839c-8c0cf9c7c07f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng218/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Identifying eligible people; barriers to uptake","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Uptake and access only; paediatric catch-up intervals and vaccine contraindications require Saudi product/schedule sources. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Reconcile reliable vaccination records and identify missed eligible immunisations.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use the current Saudi age-specific catch-up schedule, with consent and contraindication checks; do not infer dose intervals from this uptake guideline.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"6a326d01-df4c-4fe5-839c-8c0cf9c7c07f","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng218/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Identifying eligible people; barriers to uptake","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Uptake and access only; paediatric catch-up intervals and vaccine contraindications require Saudi product/schedule sources. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain childhood immunisation and catch-up in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Paediatrics / Public Health","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"2a6b90b6-13a1-443f-a212-1c2f3975327d","original_version_ids":["e3bf3c4b-1daa-4cc8-a7ac-04d129597532"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng203/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"2a6b90b6-13a1-443f-a212-1c2f3975327d","title":"Chronic Kidney Disease","specialty":"Nephrology / Primary Care","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Chronic Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"CKD assessment and longitudinal care.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","CKD assessment and longitudinal care."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["e3bf3c4b-1daa-4cc8-a7ac-04d129597532"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Persistent kidney structural or functional abnormality reduces filtration and homeostasis. Albuminuria and vascular/metabolic injury predict progression and cardiovascular events; comorbidity and medicines modify risk. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Persistent kidney structural or functional abnormality reduces filtration and homeostasis. Albuminuria and vascular/metabolic injury predict progression and cardiovascular events","comorbidity and medicines modify risk."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Chronic Kidney Disease, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Rapid decline or new nephritic features","Severe hyperkalaemia or acidosis","Pulmonary oedema or uraemic symptoms","Suspected obstruction or systemic inflammatory disease"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"AKI","distinguishingFeatures":"Serial values and clinical timing establish acute versus chronic change."},{"condition":"Transient albuminuria","distinguishingFeatures":"Repeat after infection or exercise and use appropriate sampling."},{"condition":"Obstructive or glomerular disease","distinguishingFeatures":"Symptoms, urine sediment, and imaging/serology guide work-up."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serial creatinine/eGFR and urine albumin-creatinine ratio","modalityTarget":"Serial creatinine/eGFR and urine albumin-creatinine ratio — Persistent reduced filtration or kidney damage","targetCondition":"Persistent reduced filtration or kidney damage","expectedFinding":"Persistent eGFR reduction or albuminuria over the required chronicity interval supports CKD.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms chronicity and stratifies kidney/cardiovascular risk instead of labelling one abnormal result as CKD."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Electrolytes and full blood count","modalityTarget":"Electrolytes and full blood count — Hyperkalaemia, acid-base disturbance or anaemia","targetCondition":"Hyperkalaemia, acid-base disturbance or anaemia","expectedFinding":"Potassium, bicarbonate or haemoglobin abnormalities identify complications requiring assessment.","clinicalRationale":"Guides monitoring and management proportionate to disease stage and treatment."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Urinalysis and renal ultrasound when the cause or obstruction is uncertain","modalityTarget":"Urinalysis and renal ultrasound when the cause or obstruction is uncertain — Intrinsic kidney disease or obstruction","targetCondition":"Intrinsic kidney disease or obstruction","expectedFinding":"Haematuria/casts or structural abnormalities direct cause-specific evaluation.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies a potentially treatable cause and helps distinguish chronic disease from a new reversible process."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Use eGFR and urine ACR together, confirming persistence rather than diagnosing CKD from one abnormal result.","Stratify progression and cardiovascular risk; review nephrotoxic medicines, blood pressure and specialist-referral criteria."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"0be05675-6147-4708-8a3d-d682a90195a4","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng203/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; classification; referral; blood pressure control","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. CKD assessment and longitudinal care. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Serial creatinine/eGFR and urine albumin-creatinine ratio","clinical_question":"Persistent reduced filtration or kidney damage","expected_finding":"Persistent eGFR reduction or albuminuria over the required chronicity interval supports CKD.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Confirms chronicity and stratifies kidney/cardiovascular risk instead of labelling one abnormal result as CKD.","tim