 and specialist-referral criteria.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"0be05675-6147-4708-8a3d-d682a90195a4","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng203/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; classification; referral; blood pressure control","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. CKD assessment and longitudinal care. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain chronic kidney disease in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Nephrology / Primary Care","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"e5bf7644-f824-4eca-8828-aacf30dad973","original_version_ids":["01ca9d3a-8f34-4804-9f05-8a14614cca11"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng115/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"e5bf7644-f824-4eca-8828-aacf30dad973","title":"Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease","specialty":"Respiratory Medicine / Primary Care","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Chronic Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Stable adult COPD; acute exacerbation treatment is a separate branch.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Stable adult COPD; acute exacerbation treatment is a separate branch."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["01ca9d3a-8f34-4804-9f05-8a14614cca11"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Persistent airway and parenchymal changes cause expiratory flow limitation, air trapping, and impaired gas exchange. Exacerbations worsen symptoms and may accelerate loss of function. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Persistent airway and parenchymal changes cause expiratory flow limitation, air trapping, and impaired gas exchange. Exacerbations worsen symptoms and may accelerate loss of function.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["New haemoptysis or unexplained weight loss","Rapidly worsening breathlessness or cyanosis","Recurrent severe exacerbations","Resting hypoxaemia or hypercapnia symptoms"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Asthma","distinguishingFeatures":"Variable symptoms and earlier onset may suggest asthma or overlap."},{"condition":"Heart failure","distinguishingFeatures":"Congestion and cardiac evaluation can identify coexisting disease."},{"condition":"Bronchiectasis or lung cancer","distinguishingFeatures":"Persistent purulent sputum, haemoptysis, or focal change needs assessment."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Post-bronchodilator spirometry","modalityTarget":"Post-bronchodilator spirometry — Persistent expiratory airflow obstruction","targetCondition":"Persistent expiratory airflow obstruction","expectedFinding":"Persistent obstruction in the appropriate exposure/symptom context supports COPD.","clinicalRationale":"Provides objective diagnostic evidence and distinguishes symptoms from documented airflow limitation."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Symptom and exacerbation-history assessment","modalityTarget":"Symptom and exacerbation-history assessment — Activity limitation and future exacerbation risk","targetCondition":"Activity limitation and future exacerbation risk","expectedFinding":"Validated symptom measures and prior exacerbations identify the clinical burden.","clinicalRationale":"Guides individualised ongoing care beyond spirometric severity alone."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"firstLineImaging","testName":"Oximetry and targeted chest imaging when indicated","modalityTarget":"Oximetry and targeted chest imaging when indicated — Hypoxaemia or an alternative thoracic diagnosis","targetCondition":"Hypoxaemia or an alternative thoracic diagnosis","expectedFinding":"Low saturation, a focal lesion or another radiographic abnormality directs further investigation.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies complications or mimics; routine repeated imaging is not justified without a clinical question."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Confirm COPD using post-bronchodilator spirometry with an appropriate exposure and symptom history.","Review inhaler technique, smoking cessation, vaccination and pulmonary rehabilitation; individualise inhaled treatment and oxygen eligibility."]}],"med