 audit: Guides individualised ongoing care beyond spirometric severity alone.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Oximetry and targeted chest imaging when indicated","clinical_question":"Hypoxaemia or an alternative thoracic diagnosis","expected_finding":"Low saturation, a focal lesion or another radiographic abnormality directs further investigation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies complications or mimics; routine repeated imaging is not justified without a clinical question.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b0ae3287-fdfd-4c81-8036-70e9b76b5884","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng115/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.2","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Stable adult COPD; acute exacerbation treatment is a separate branch. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Confirm COPD using post-bronchodilator spirometry with an appropriate exposure and symptom history.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Review inhaler technique, smoking cessation, vaccination and pulmonary rehabilitation; individualise inhaled treatment and oxygen eligibility.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b0ae3287-fdfd-4c81-8036-70e9b76b5884","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng115/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.2","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Stable adult COPD; acute exacerbation treatment is a separate branch. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain chronic obstructive pulmonary disease in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Respiratory Medicine / Primary Care","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"433ede2c-6a49-4169-88ca-298ccf2cb065","original_version_ids":["3a435d5d-a2bc-496c-91d7-415dd4337eac"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng151/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"433ede2c-6a49-4169-88ca-298ccf2cb065","title":"Colorectal Cancer Diagnosis and Treatment Planning","specialty":"Colorectal Surgery / Oncology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Planned Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Confirmed colorectal malignancy; molecular testing and systemic treatments need current specialist reconciliation.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Confirmed colorectal malignancy; molecular testing and systemic treatments need current specialist reconciliation."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["3a435d5d-a2bc-496c-91d7-415dd4337eac"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Colorectal malignancy develops through genetic and epigenetic change, with location and stage shaping symptoms and treatment. Multidisciplinary staging balances oncologic control with functional outcomes and patient priorities. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Colorectal malignancy develops through genetic and epigenetic change, with location and stage shaping symptoms and treatment. Multidisciplinary staging balances oncologic control with functional outcomes and patient priorities.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Colorectal Cancer Diagnosis and Treatment Planning, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Obstruction, perforation, or significant bleeding","Severe anaemia or malnutrition","Possible metastatic disease with organ compromise","Hereditary syndrome or multiple affected relatives"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Benign polyp or inflammatory lesion","distinguishingFeatures":"Histology and complete colon evaluation establish diagnosis."},{"condition":"Gynaecologic or gastric source of anaemia","distinguishingFeatures":"Investigate alternative causes when lesion does not explain findings."},{"condition":"Synchronous colorectal lesion","distinguishingFeatures":"Complete colon assessment is important when feasible."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Colonoscopy with biopsy","modalityTarget":"Colonoscopy with biopsy — Colorectal lesion and histological diagnosis","targetCondition":"Colorectal lesion and histological diagnosis","expectedFinding":"A suspicious lesion with histology establishes tumour type; complete colonic evaluation assesses synchronous lesions when feasible.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms diagnosis before cancer treatment decisions."},{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"CT staging according to the oncology pathway","modalityTarget":"CT staging according to the oncology pathway — Regional and distant disease","targetCondition":"Regional and distant disease","expectedFinding":"Nodes and distant lesions influence stage and operability; indeterminate lesions need further evaluation.","clinicalRationale":"Defines extent for multidisciplinary treatment planning."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Full blood count and renal/liver tests","modalityTarget":"Full blood count and renal/liver tests — Anaemia and organ dysfunction affecting treatment fitness","targetCondition":"Anaemia and organ dysfunction affecting treatment fitness","expectedFinding":"Iron-deficiency-pattern anaemia or kidney/liver impairment requires assessment.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies complications and provides a baseline for safe procedures and systemic therapy."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Complete diagnosis and staging and distinguish colon from rectal cancer before MDT planning.","Discuss stage-specific surgery, radiotherapy or systemic treatment with the colorectal MDT and address supportive-care needs."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"90d65564-979f-46a6-8beb-9147d3f5888e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng151/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Diagnosis; localised disease; advanced disease","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Confirmed colorectal malignancy; molecular testing and systemic treatments need current specialist reconciliation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Colonoscopy with biopsy","clinical_question":"Colorectal lesion and histological diagnosis","expected_finding":"A suspicious lesion with histology establishes tumour type; complete colonic evaluation assesses synchronous lesions when feasible.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Confirms diagnosis before cancer treatment decisions.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"CT staging according to the oncology pathway","clinical_question":"Regional and distant disease","expected_finding":"Nodes and distant lesions influence stage and operability; indeterminate lesions need further evaluation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Defines extent for multidisciplinary treatment planning.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Full blood count and renal/liver tests","clinical_question":"Anaemia and organ dysfunction affecting treatment fitness","expected_finding":"Iron-deficiency-pattern anaemia or kidney/liver impairment requires assessment.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies complications and provides a baseline for safe procedures and systemic therapy.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"90d65564-979f-46a6-8beb-9147d3f5888e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng151/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Diagnosis; localised disease; advanced disease","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Confirmed colorectal malignancy; molecular testing and systemic treatments need current specialist reconciliation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Complete diagnosis and staging and distinguish colon from rectal cancer before MDT planning.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Discuss stage-specific surgery, radiotherapy or systemic treatment with the colorectal MDT and address supportive-care needs.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"90d65564-979f-46a6-8beb-9147d3f5888e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng151/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Diagnosis; localised disease; advanced disease","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Confirmed colorectal malignancy; molecular testing and systemic treatments need current specialist reconciliation. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain colorectal cancer diagnosis and treatment planning in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Colorectal Surgery / Oncology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"d0389517-2846-49bc-8a01-eb7265f8e139","original_version_ids":["8b84e8ad-ef09-4643-8cc1-9d7d1cc2d1b3"],"source_title":"Recommendations organised by site of cancer","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng12/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"d0389517-2846-49bc-8a01-eb7265f8e139","title":"Colorectal Cancer Screening","specialty":"Primary Care / Gastroenterology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Symptomatic referral only; diagnostic FIT recommendations do not define population-screening ages or intervals.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Diagnostic referral or uptake guidance is not sufficient evidence for a Saudi population screening or vaccination schedule.","Symptomatic referral only; diagnostic FIT recommendations do not define population-screening ages or intervals."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["8b84e8ad-ef09-4643-8cc1-9d7d1cc2d1b3"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Most colorectal cancers arise through progressive neoplastic change over time, allowing screening to detect precursor lesions or early cancer. Benefit depends on risk category, test completion, and diagnostic follow-through. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Most colorectal cancers arise through progressive neoplastic change over time, allowing screening to detect precursor lesions or early cancer. Benefit depends on risk category, test completion, and diagnostic follow-through.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Colorectal Cancer Screening, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Rectal bleeding, iron-deficiency anaemia or persistent bowel change is diagnostic work-up","Strong family or hereditary cancer pattern","Unintentional weight loss or abdominal mass","Positive stool test requires timely colon evaluation"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Haemorrhoids","distinguishingFeatures":"Do not use as a reason to dismiss unexplained bleeding."},{"condition":"Inflammatory bowel disease","distinguishingFeatures":"May need surveillance rather than population screening."},{"condition":"Functional bowel disorder","distinguishingFeatures":"Persistent alarm features still require evaluation."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Faecal immunochemical test when used by the national programme","modalityTarget":"Faecal immunochemical test when used by the national programme — Occult lower-gastrointestinal bleeding","targetCondition":"Occult lower-gastrointestinal bleeding","expectedFinding":"A positive result requires follow-up investigation; a negative screen does not exclude cancer in a symptomatic patient.","clinicalRationale":"Selects eligible asymptomatic patients for further assessment through a tracked programme."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Colonoscopy after a positive screen or other indication","modalityTarget":"Colonoscopy after a positive screen or other indication — Polyps or a colorectal tumour","targetCondition":"Polyps or a colorectal tumour","expectedFinding":"Direct visualisation and histology identify the lesion and determine the next step.","clinicalRationale":"Completes diagnostic follow-up rather than repeating a positive screening test to dismiss it."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Risk and symptom assessment","modalityTarget":"Risk and symptom assessment — Symptoms or high-risk history requiring a diagnostic/surveillance pathway","targetCondition":"Symptoms or high-risk history requiring a diagnostic/surveillance pathway","expectedFinding":"Bleeding, iron-deficiency anaemia, prior polyps or hereditary risk changes the pathway.","clinicalRationale":"Avoids using routine screening to reassure a symptomatic or high-risk patient."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Keep symptomatic colorectal investigation separate from an asymptomatic screening offer.","Use current Saudi screening eligibility and follow-up; a low FIT result must not override persistent concerning symptoms or clinical judgement."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ec2e9e7a-6115-479b-82a1-47782cc5993d","title":"Recommendations organised by site of cancer","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng12/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Lower gastrointestinal cancers; FIT","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Symptomatic referral only; diagnostic FIT recommendations do not define population-screening ages or intervals. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Faecal immunochemical test when used by the national programme","clinical_question":"Occult lower-gastrointestinal bleeding","expected_finding":"A positive result requires follow-up investigation; a negative screen does not exclude cancer in a symptomatic patient.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Selects eligible asymptomatic patients for further assessment through a tracked programme.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Colonoscopy after a positive screen or other indication","clinical_question":"Polyps or a colorectal tumour","expected_finding":"Direct visualisation and histology identify the lesion and determine the next step.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Completes diagnostic follow-up rather than repeating a positive screening test to dismiss it.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Risk and symptom assessment","clinical_question":"Symptoms or high-risk history requiring a diagnostic/surveillance pathway","expected_finding":"Bleeding, iron-deficiency anaemia, prior polyps or hereditary risk changes the pathway.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Avoids using routine screening to reassure a symptomatic or high-risk patient.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ec2e9e7a-6115-479b-82a1-47782cc5993d","title":"Recommendations organised by site of cancer","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng12/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Lower gastrointestinal cancers; FIT","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Symptomatic referral only; diagnostic FIT recommendations do not define population-screening ages or intervals. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Keep symptomatic colorectal investigation separate from an asymptomatic screening offer.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use current Saudi screening eligibility and follow-up; a low FIT result must not override persistent concerning symptoms or clinical judgement.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ec2e9e7a-6115-479b-82a1-47782cc5993d","title":"Recommendations organised by site of cancer","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng12/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Lower gastrointestinal cancers; FIT","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Symptomatic referral only; diagnostic FIT recommendations do not define population-screening ages or intervals. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain colorectal cancer screening in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary Care / Gastroenterology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004","original_version_ids":["a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng250/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004","title":"Community-Acquired Pneumonia","specialty":"Internal Medicine, Respiratory Medicine and Infectious Diseases","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2021-01-01","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Current NICE pneumonia guidance, replacing reliance on older pneumonia guidance alone; local antibiotic selection remains required.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Current NICE pneumonia guidance, replacing reliance on older pneumonia guidance alone; local antibiotic selection remains required."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Community-acquired pneumonia is infection of the distal airways and alveoli acquired outside hospital or early after admission. Alveolar inflammation and exudate impair ventilation and gas exchange; systemic inflammatory effects may cause sepsis and organ dysfunction.","keyMechanisms":["Pathogen aspiration or inhalation overcomes airway and innate immune defences.","Alveolar neutrophilic inflammation and fluid cause consolidation and ventilation-perfusion mismatch.","Host response varies with age, comorbidity, immune status and pathogen virulence.","Complications include parapneumonic effusion, empyema, lung abscess, respiratory failure and sepsis."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Acute cough with or without sputum","Fever, rigors or malaise","Dyspnoea or pleuritic chest pain","Confusion or functional decline, especially in older adults"],"physicalSigns":["Tachypnoea, hypoxaemia or increased work of breathing","Focal crackles, bronchial breathing or dullness to percussion","Fever or hypothermia with tachycardia","Confusion, hypotension or poor perfusion in severe disease"],"redFlags":["Respiratory failure, exhaustion or rapidly increasing oxygen need","Shock, altered mental status, oliguria or other sepsis-associated organ dysfunction","Multilobar disease, cavitation or a large pleural effusion","Immunocompromise, aspiration risk or failure to improve on appropriate initial therapy"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Pulmonary embolism","distinguishingFeatures":"Abrupt pleuritic pain or dyspnoea, thrombosis risk and limited infective prodrome; imaging shows vascular rather than air-space disease."},{"condition":"Acute heart failure","distinguishingFeatures":"Orthopnoea, bilateral congestion, raised jugular venous pressure and cardiac dysfunction."},{"condition":"Viral respiratory infection without pneumonia","distinguishingFeatures":"Diffuse upper-respiratory features without focal consolidation or compatible chest imaging."},{"condition":"Pulmonary tuberculosis","distinguishingFeatures":"Subacute constitutional symptoms, epidemiologic risk, upper-lobe or cavitary change and specific microbiology."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"firstLineImaging","testName":"Chest radiograph","modalityTarget":"Chest radiograph — Pulmonary air-space infection","targetCondition":"Pulmonary air-space infection","expectedFinding":"New focal or multifocal infiltrate compatible with pneumonia.","clinicalRationale":"Supports diagnosis, extent assessment and detection of effusion or another thoracic process in hospital-managed disease."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Pulse oximetry and blood gas when severe","modalityTarget":"Pulse oximetry and blood gas when severe — Gas-exchange impairment","targetCondition":"Gas-exchange impairment","expectedFinding":"Hypoxaemia, with acidaemia or ventilatory failure in advanced disease.","clinicalRationale":"Determines oxygen and ventilatory support needs."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Microbiology selected by severity","modalityTarget":"Microbiology selected by severity — Causative pathogen","targetCondition":"Causative pathogen","expectedFinding":"A plausible bacterial or viral pathogen in good-quality respiratory, blood or molecular samples.","clinicalRationale":"Severe or epidemiologically important disease benefits most from organism identification and antimicrobial narrowing."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Electrocardiogram and cardiac assessment","modalityTarget":"Electrocardiogram and cardiac assessment — Heart failure or acute coronary syndrome","targetCondition":"Heart failure or acute coronary syndrome","expectedFinding":"No primary cardiac process sufficient to explain the presentation.","clinicalRationale":"Cardiac disease commonly mimics or coexists with pneumonia."},{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"CT chest or pleural ultrasound when indicated","modalityTarget":"CT chest or pleural ultrasound when indicated — Pulmonary embolism, malignancy, abscess or complicated effusion","targetCondition":"Pulmonary embolism, malignancy, abscess or complicated effusion","expectedFinding":"No alternative lesion, or a complication is identified for targeted management.","clinicalRationale":"Reserved for diagnostic uncertainty, complication assessment or treatment failure."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Use clinical judgement with CRB65 in primary care or CURB65 in hospital to assess severity and place of care.","Choose prompt severity-appropriate antibiotics after allergy and local-resistance review; reassess clinical stability and course length."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"3776ac33-ac7e-487a-8580-298607ea3dde","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng250/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; antibiotic treatment","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Current NICE pneumonia guidance, replacing reliance on older pneumonia guidance alone; local antibiotic selection remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Chest radiograph","clinical_question":"Pulmonary air-space infection","expected_finding":"New focal or multifocal infiltrate compatible with pneumonia.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports diagnosis, extent assessment and detection of effusion or another thoracic process in hospital-managed disease.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Pulse oximetry and blood gas when severe","clinical_question":"Gas-exchange impairment","expected_finding":"Hypoxaemia, with acidaemia or ventilatory failure in advanced disease.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Determines oxygen and ventilatory support needs.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Microbiology selected by severity","clinical_question":"Causative pathogen","expected_finding":"A plausible bacterial or viral pathogen in good-quality respiratory, blood or molecular samples.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Severe or epidemiologically important disease benefits most from organism identification and antimicrobial narrowing.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Electrocardiogram and cardiac assessment","clinical_question":"Heart failure or acute coronary syndrome","expected_finding":"No primary cardiac process sufficient to explain the presentation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Cardiac disease commonly mimics or coexists with pneumonia.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"CT chest or pleural ultrasound when indicated","clinical_question":"Pulmonary embolism, malignancy, abscess or complicated effusion","expected_finding":"No alternative lesion, or a complication is identified for targeted management.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Reserved for diagnostic uncertainty, complication assessment or treatment failure.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"3776ac33-ac7e-487a-8580-298607ea3dde","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng250/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; antibiotic treatment","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Current NICE pneumonia guidance, replacing reliance on older pneumonia guidance alone; local antibiotic selection remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Use clinical judgement with CRB65 in primary care or CURB65 in hospital to assess severity and place of care.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Choose prompt severity-appropriate antibiotics after allergy and local-resistance review; reassess clinical stability and course length.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"3776ac33-ac7e-487a-8580-298607ea3dde","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng250/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; antibiotic treatment","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Current NICE pneumonia guidance, replacing reliance on older pneumonia guidance alone; local antibiotic selection remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain the expected recovery trajectory and that cough and fatigue may outlast fever.","Give return precautions for worsening breathlessness, confusion, cyanosis, chest pain or inability to maintain intake.","Explain antimicrobial adherence and why unused antibiotics should not be saved or shared."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Encourage hydration and nutrition as tolerated.","Offer smoking-cessation support.","Review influenza, pneumococcal and other indicated vaccination after recovery."],"mdtReferrals":["Critical care for respiratory failure or shock","Respiratory medicine for complications, recurrent pneumonia or diagnostic uncertainty","Microbiology or infectious diseases for resistant organisms, severe immunocompromise or treatment failure","Speech and language therapy for suspected aspiration"],"dischargeCriteria":["Vital signs and oxygen requirement are stable at an appropriate baseline.","The patient can take oral medicine and maintain hydration and nutrition.","A safe antimicrobial plan, follow-up ownership and return precautions are documented."],"followUpPlan":"Arrange clinical review based on severity and comorbidity; follow pending cultures, reassess non-resolution, and consider interval chest imaging for persistent symptoms or higher malignancy risk according to local policy."}}},{"guideline_id":"a44b31ff-1839-4db9-aec2-f73fcaef4d5f","original_version_ids":["b24b7309-8381-4efb-8d70-88f3da0a3b88"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng107/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a44b31ff-1839-4db9-aec2-f73fcaef4d5f","title":"Conservative Kidney Care Planning","specialty":"Nephrology / Palliative Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Palliative Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Shared renal replacement versus conservative-care decisions.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Shared renal replacement versus conservative-care decisions."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["b24b7309-8381-4efb-8d70-88f3da0a3b88"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Advanced kidney disease causes fluid, electrolyte, metabolic, and uraemic symptoms. Conservative kidney management is active care focused on symptoms, function, and quality of life when dialysis is not chosen or is unlikely to meet patient goals. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Advanced kidney disease causes fluid, electrolyte, metabolic, and uraemic symptoms. Conservative kidney management is active care focused on symptoms, function, and quality of life when dialysis is not chosen or is unlikely to meet patient goals.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Conservative Kidney Care Planning, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Refractory fluid overload, hyperkalaemia, acidosis, or uraemic symptoms needing urgent review","Conflict or uncertainty about capacity and preferences","Uncontrolled pain, pruritus, nausea, or breathlessness","Caregiver inability to sustain home plan"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Reversible AKI or obstruction","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess and treat when consistent with goals."},{"condition":"Depression affecting decision","distinguishingFeatures":"Offer support before interpreting preference."},{"condition":"Dialysis as a preference-sensitive choice","distinguishingFeatures":"Present options without coercion."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Symptom, function and goals-of-care assessment","modalityTarget":"Symptom, function and goals-of-care assessment — Uraemic symptom burden and priorities","targetCondition":"Uraemic symptom burden and priorities","expectedFinding":"Document pruritus, nausea, breathlessness, function and the person's preferred care limits.","clinicalRationale":"Aligns monitoring and interventions with comfort and shared decisions."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Potassium, bicarbonate and creatinine when results will change care","modalityTarget":"Potassium, bicarbonate and creatinine when results will change care — Electrolyte/acidosis complications and kidney trajectory","targetCondition":"Electrolyte/acidosis complications and kidney trajectory","expectedFinding":"Abnormal potassium/bicarbonate or a changing filtration trend may explain symptoms and identify treatment options.","clinicalRationale":"Uses proportionate testing for manageable complications rather than routine burdensome testing without a decision."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Focused examination and medication review after new deterioration","modalityTarget":"Focused examination and medication review after new deterioration — Fluid overload, infection or drug-related harm","targetCondition":"Fluid overload, infection or drug-related harm","expectedFinding":"A new focal finding or exposure directs additional investigation.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies reversible problems within the agreed conservative-care plan."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Discuss conservative care and renal replacement with expected burdens, benefits and the person's priorities.","Provide an active symptom, nutrition and advance-care plan with clear ownership; revisit decisions as circumstances change."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"23696bad-4201-4953-8ecb-8d2ea2461336","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng107/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; conservative management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Shared renal replacement versus conservative-care decisions. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Symptom, function and goals-of-care assessment","clinical_question":"Uraemic symptom burden and priorities","expected_finding":"Document pruritus, nausea, breathlessness, function and the person's preferred care limits.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Aligns monitoring and interventions with comfort and shared decisions.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Potassium, bicarbonate and creatinine when results will change care","clinical_question":"Electrolyte/acidosis complications and kidney trajectory","expected_finding":"Abnormal potassium/bicarbonate or a changing filtration trend may explain symptoms and identify treatment options.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Uses proportionate testing for manageable complications rather than routine burdensome testing without a decision.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Focused examination and medication review after new deterioration","clinical_question":"Fluid overload, infection or drug-related harm","expected_finding":"A new focal finding or exposure directs additional investigation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies reversible problems within the agreed conservative-care plan.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"23696bad-4201-4953-8ecb-8d2ea2461336","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng107/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; conservative management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Shared renal replacement versus conservative-care decisions. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Discuss conservative care and renal replacement with expected burdens, benefits and the person's priorities.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Provide an active symptom, nutrition and advance-care plan with clear ownership; revisit decisions as circumstances change.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"23696bad-4201-4953-8ecb-8d2ea2461336","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng107/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; conservative management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Shared renal replacement versus conservative-care decisions. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain conservative kidney care planning in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Nephrology / Palliative Medicine","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","original_version_ids":["a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng158/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","title":"Deep-Vein Thrombosis and Pulmonary Embolism","specialty":"Emergency Medicine, Internal Medicine and Haematology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2024-09-04","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Nonpregnant adult suspected/confirmed VTE; pregnancy requires a separate source.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Nonpregnant adult suspected/confirmed VTE; pregnancy requires a separate source."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Venous thromboembolism results from venous stasis, endothelial injury and hypercoagulability. A deep-vein thrombus may obstruct limb venous return or embolise to pulmonary arteries, increasing dead space and pulmonary vascular resistance and, in severe cases, causing right-ventricular failure and shock.","keyMechanisms":["Thrombus formation is promoted by immobility, surgery, cancer, oestrogen exposure, pregnancy and inherited or acquired thrombophilia.","Pulmonary arterial obstruction produces ventilation-perfusion mismatch and hypoxaemia.","Acute right-ventricular pressure overload can reduce left-ventricular filling and systemic cardiac output.","Residual venous obstruction and valve damage contribute to post-thrombotic syndrome; persistent vascular obstruction may cause chronic thromboembolic pulmonary hypertension."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Unilateral leg pain or swelling","Sudden unexplained dyspnoea","Pleuritic chest pain, cough, haemoptysis or syncope","Reduced exercise tolerance with recent immobility, surgery, cancer or prior thrombosis"],"physicalSigns":["Unilateral pitting oedema, calf asymmetry or deep venous tenderness","Tachycardia, tachypnoea or hypoxaemia","Signs of right-heart strain such as raised jugular venous pressure","Hypotension or poor perfusion in high-risk pulmonary embolism"],"redFlags":["Haemodynamic instability, syncope with persistent hypotension or obstructive-shock features","Severe hypoxaemia, rapidly escalating oxygen requirement or cardiac arrest","Threatened limb with massive swelling, cyanosis or severe pain","Active major bleeding or another absolute barrier to anticoagulation in a patient with confirmed or highly suspected VTE"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Cellulitis","distinguishingFeatures":"Superficial erythema, warmth and a possible portal of entry with inflammatory features rather than isolated deep venous tenderness."},{"condition":"Ruptured Baker cyst","distinguishingFeatures":"Posterior knee pathology with fluid tracking into the calf and diagnostic ultrasound findings."},{"condition":"Acute coronary syndrome","distinguishingFeatures":"Pressure-type pain, ischaemic electrocardiographic change or a coronary biomarker pattern rather than pleuritic pain and right-heart strain."},{"condition":"Pneumonia or pneumothorax","distinguishingFeatures":"Focal infective symptoms or unilateral absent breath sounds with confirmatory chest imaging."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Compression ultrasonography","modalityTarget":"Compression ultrasonography — Proximal lower-limb DVT","targetCondition":"Proximal lower-limb DVT","expectedFinding":"Non-compressible venous segment or directly visualised thrombus.","clinicalRationale":"First-line anatomical confirmation for suspected proximal DVT."},{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"CT pulmonary angiography","modalityTarget":"CT pulmonary angiography — Pulmonary embolism","targetCondition":"Pulmonary embolism","expectedFinding":"Intraluminal filling defect in a pulmonary artery.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms pulmonary embolism and describes clot burden while also identifying some alternative thoracic diagnoses."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Echocardiography in unstable PE","modalityTarget":"Echocardiography in unstable PE — Right-ventricular pressure overload","targetCondition":"Right-ventricular pressure overload","expectedFinding":"Right-ventricular dilatation or dysfunction compatible with acute pressure overload.","clinicalRationale":"Supports urgent risk stratification when instability makes definitive imaging unsafe or delayed."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"High-sensitivity D-dimer in an appropriate low-probability pathway","modalityTarget":"High-sensitivity D-dimer in an appropriate low-probability pathway — Acute VTE","targetCondition":"Acute VTE","expectedFinding":"A negative result below the assay's validated threshold makes acute VTE unlikely in the selected population.","clinicalRationale":"Avoids unnecessary imaging only after structured clinical-probability assessment."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Ventilation-perfusion imaging","modalityTarget":"Ventilation-perfusion imaging — Pulmonary embolism when CTPA is unsuitable","targetCondition":"Pulmonary embolism when CTPA is unsuitable","expectedFinding":"Normal perfusion argues strongly against PE; a mismatched perfusion defect supports it.","clinicalRationale":"Provides an alternative when contrast, radiation distribution or renal considerations make CTPA unsuitable."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Use the relevant two-level Wells pathway with D-dimer and timely imaging; consider interim anticoagulation when testing is delayed and clinically appropriate.","Select treatment after reviewing bleeding risk, renal function, cancer, interactions and instability; escalate haemodynamically unstable PE urgently."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c8fbec8a-55cd-472a-8f3b-e07f3b983e6e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng158/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; anticoagulation; PE management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Nonpregnant adult suspected/confirmed VTE; pregnancy requires a separate source. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Compression ultrasonography","clinical_question":"Proximal lower-limb DVT","expected_finding":"Non-compressible venous segment or directly visualised thrombus.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: First-line anatomical confirmation for suspected proximal DVT.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"CT pulmonary angiography","clinical_question":"Pulmonary embolism","expected_finding":"Intraluminal filling defect in a pulmonary artery.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Confirms pulmonary embolism and describes clot burden while also identifying some alternative thoracic diagnoses.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Echocardiography in unstable PE","clinical_question":"Right-ventricular pressure overload","expected_finding":"Right-ventricular dilatation or dysfunction compatible with acute pressure overload.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports urgent risk stratification when instability makes definitive imaging unsafe or delayed.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"High-sensitivity D-dimer in an appropriate low-probability pathway","clinical_question":"Acute VTE","expected_finding":"A negative result below the assay's validated threshold makes acute VTE unlikely in the selected population.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Avoids unnecessary imaging only after structured clinical-probability assessment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Ventilation-perfusion imaging","clinical_question":"Pulmonary embolism when CTPA is unsuitable","expected_finding":"Normal perfusion argues strongly against PE; a mismatched perfusion defect supports it.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides an alternative when contrast, radiation distribution or renal considerations make CTPA unsuitable.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c8fbec8a-55cd-472a-8f3b-e07f3b983e6e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng158/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; anticoagulation; PE management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Nonpregnant adult suspected/confirmed VTE; pregnancy requires a separate source. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Use the relevant two-level Wells pathway with D-dimer and timely imaging; consider interim anticoagulation when testing is delayed and clinically appropriate.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Select treatment after reviewing bleeding risk, renal function, cancer, interactions and instability; escalate haemodynamically unstable PE urgently.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c8fbec8a-55cd-472a-8f3b-e07f3b983e6e","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng158/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; anticoagulation; PE management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Nonpregnant adult suspected/confirmed VTE; pregnancy requires a separate source. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain clot symptoms, anticoagulant purpose, adherence and what to do after a missed dose using the medicine-specific approved information.","Provide urgent warning signs for recurrent PE and major bleeding.","Discuss procedure, dental and pregnancy-planning precautions before any anticoagulant change."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Encourage mobilisation as tolerated once anticoagulation and clinical stability permit.","Reduce prolonged immobility during travel and recovery and maintain hydration when appropriate.","Address smoking, obesity and other modifiable vascular risks without implying that lifestyle replaces anticoagulation."],"mdtReferrals":["Haematology for recurrent, unusual-site or selected unprovoked VTE","Oncology for suspected or active cancer-associated thrombosis","Vascular or interventional service for threatened limb or selected reperfusion decisions","Obstetric medicine for pregnancy or postpartum VTE"],"dischargeCriteria":["Haemodynamics and oxygenation are stable and validated outpatient-risk criteria are met where outpatient care is proposed.","Anticoagulant access, renal-function appropriateness, administration and follow-up are confirmed.","Bleeding and recurrence precautions are understood and a responsible service owns pending results."],"followUpPlan":"Review early after discharge for symptoms, bleeding, adherence and renal function where relevant; reassess treatment duration at the guideline-defined milestone and investigate persistent dyspnoea for post-PE complications."}}},{"guideline_id":"732644b9-0497-44a8-bfc2-0fca5dfc7392","original_version_ids":["5987c3e4-f5b5-485b-90a4-d4dcbf27fe75"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"732644b9-0497-44a8-bfc2-0fca5dfc7392","title":"Delirium and Agitation Near End of Life","specialty":"Palliative Medicine / Geriatrics","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Palliative Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Last-days-of-life distress only; delirium outside this setting requires CG103 assessment.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Last-days-of-life distress only; delirium outside this setting requires CG103 assessment."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["5987c3e4-f5b5-485b-90a4-d4dcbf27fe75"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Delirium is an acute disturbance of attention and awareness caused by interacting vulnerability and precipitating factors. Near end of life, illness, medicines, dehydration, pain, retention, and environment may contribute. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Delirium is an acute disturbance of attention and awareness caused by interacting vulnerability and precipitating factors. Near end of life, illness, medicines, dehydration, pain, retention, and environment may contribute.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Delirium and Agitation Near End of Life, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Seizure, focal deficit, or sudden severe headache","Respiratory compromise or suspected toxicity","Unsafe agitation or risk of injury","Family distress with unresolved goals or uncertainty"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Dementia progression","distinguishingFeatures":"Acute fluctuation and inattention suggest delirium over baseline decline."},{"condition":"Depression or anxiety","distinguishingFeatures":"May coexist but does not explain acute altered attention alone."},{"condition":"Medication toxicity, infection, retention, constipation, dehydration","distinguishingFeatures":"Common reversible contributors to assess."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Collateral history and validated delirium assessment","modalityTarget":"Collateral history and validated delirium assessment — Acute fluctuating inattention or cognitive change","targetCondition":"Acute fluctuating inattention or cognitive change","expectedFinding":"A change from baseline with fluctuation and impaired attention supports delirium.","clinicalRationale":"Distinguishes delirium from chronic cognitive impairment and establishes the time course."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Pain, bladder, bowel and medication assessment","modalityTarget":"Pain, bladder, bowel and medication assessment — Reversible causes of distress","targetCondition":"Reversible causes of distress","expectedFinding":"Pain, retention, constipation or a recent deliriogenic medicine may explain agitation.","clinicalRationale":"Detects treatable contributors without automatically adding invasive investigations."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Targeted glucose, electrolytes or infection tests when goal-concordant","modalityTarget":"Targeted glucose, electrolytes or infection tests when goal-concordant — A suspected metabolic or infectious precipitant","targetCondition":"A suspected metabolic or infectious precipitant","expectedFinding":"An abnormal result is interpreted against the suspected cause and goals of care.","clinicalRationale":"Order only the named tests likely to change symptom-focused treatment."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Look for reversible causes of distress and use supportive measures.","Individualise symptom treatment and seek specialist advice for diagnostic uncertainty or persistent agitation."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f68c7030-b134-4b46-85b0-2ed092d94f58","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.5.20–1.5.24","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Last-days-of-life distress only; delirium outside this setting requires CG103 assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Collateral history and validated delirium assessment","clinical_question":"Acute fluctuating inattention or cognitive change","expected_finding":"A change from baseline with fluctuation and impaired attention supports delirium.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Distinguishes delirium from chronic cognitive impairment and establishes the time course.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Pain, bladder, bowel and medication assessment","clinical_question":"Reversible causes of distress","expected_finding":"Pain, retention, constipation or a recent deliriogenic medicine may explain agitation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects treatable contributors without automatically adding invasive investigations.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Targeted glucose, electrolytes or infection tests when goal-concordant","clinical_question":"A suspected metabolic or infectious precipitant","expected_finding":"An abnormal result is interpreted against the suspected cause and goals of care.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Order only the named tests likely to change symptom-focused treatment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f68c7030-b134-4b46-85b0-2ed092d94f58","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.5.20–1.5.24","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Last-days-of-life distress only; delirium outside this setting requires CG103 assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Look for reversible causes of distress and use supportive measures.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Individualise symptom treatment and seek specialist advice for diagnostic uncertainty or persistent agitation.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f68c7030-b134-4b46-85b0-2ed092d94f58","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.5.20–1.5.24","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Last-days-of-life distress only; delirium outside this setting requires CG103 assessment. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain delirium and agitation near end of life in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Palliative Medicine / Geriatrics","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"e483d190-076c-49b3-881c-78ca823af167","original_version_ids":["7c744cd5-f70b-4297-8ff3-dc06c75c7334"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ph38/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"e483d190-076c-49b3-881c-78ca823af167","title":"Diabetes Screening in At-Risk Adults","specialty":"Primary Care / Public Health","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Type 2 diabetes risk detection; not a symptomatic DKA pathway.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Diagnostic referral or uptake guidance is not sufficient evidence for a Saudi population screening or vaccination schedule.","Type 2 diabetes risk detection; not a symptomatic DKA pathway."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["7c744cd5-f70b-4297-8ff3-dc06c75c7334"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Type 2 diabetes often develops gradually through insulin resistance and beta-cell dysfunction, allowing a period of asymptomatic dysglycaemia. Screening aims to identify people likely to benefit from preventive support and earlier care. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Type 2 diabetes often develops gradually through insulin resistance and beta-cell dysfunction, allowing a period of asymptomatic dysglycaemia. Screening aims to identify people likely to benefit from preventive support and earlier care.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Diabetes Screening in At-Risk Adults, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Classic symptoms with marked glucose elevation require prompt diagnostic assessment","Pregnancy or recent gestational diabetes has separate follow-up needs","Rapid weight loss or ketosis needs urgent evaluation","Discordant tests require clinical interpretation"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Transient stress hyperglycaemia","distinguishingFeatures":"Repeat testing after acute illness if appropriate."},{"condition":"Medication-induced dysglycaemia","distinguishingFeatures":"Review glucocorticoids and other risks."},{"condition":"Type 1 diabetes","distinguishingFeatures":"Symptoms, ketosis, or rapid progression changes urgency."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Laboratory HbA1c when appropriate","modalityTarget":"Laboratory HbA1c when appropriate — Chronic hyperglycaemia","targetCondition":"Chronic hyperglycaemia","expectedFinding":"An elevated result requires interpretation using the adopted diagnostic pathway; altered red-cell turnover can make it unreliable.","clinicalRationale":"Assesses longer-term glycaemia without fasting when the assay is suitable for the patient."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Fasting plasma glucose","modalityTarget":"Fasting plasma glucose — Fasting hyperglycaemia","targetCondition":"Fasting hyperglycaemia","expectedFinding":"An abnormal fasting value supports dysglycaemia and may require confirmation if the patient is asymptomatic.","clinicalRationale":"Provides a glucose-based assessment when HbA1c is unsuitable or as an alternative screening method."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Repeat diagnostic testing when required","modalityTarget":"Repeat diagnostic testing when required — Persistent rather than isolated hyperglycaemia","targetCondition":"Persistent rather than isolated hyperglycaemia","expectedFinding":"Concordant abnormal laboratory results confirm persistence according to the adopted criteria.","clinicalRationale":"Reduces misclassification from biological variation, acute illness or testing error."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Use risk assessment to select appropriate HbA1c or fasting-glucose testing and confirm diagnostic results when required.","Offer intensive lifestyle support and follow-up to people at high risk, using locally validated risk tools and eligibility."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c00bacae-ab4c-446e-8fad-855c49491948","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ph38/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Risk identification; blood testing; intensive lifestyle change","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Type 2 diabetes risk detection; not a symptomatic DKA pathway. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Laboratory HbA1c when appropriate","clinical_question":"Chronic hyperglycaemia","expected_finding":"An elevated result requires interpretation using the adopted diagnostic pathway; altered red-cell turnover can make it unreliable.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Assesses longer-term glycaemia without fasting when the assay is suitable for the patient.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Fasting plasma glucose","clinical_question":"Fasting hyperglycaemia","expected_finding":"An abnormal fasting value supports dysglycaemia and may require confirmation if the patient is asymptomatic.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides a glucose-based assessment when HbA1c is unsuitable or as an alternative screening method.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Repeat diagnostic testing when required","clinical_question":"Persistent rather than isolated hyperglycaemia","expected_finding":"Concordant abnormal laboratory results confirm persistence according to the adopted criteria.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Reduces misclassification from biological variation, acute illness or testing error.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c00bacae-ab4c-446e-8fad-855c49491948","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ph38/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Risk identification; blood testing; intensive lifestyle change","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Type 2 diabetes risk detection; not a symptomatic DKA pathway. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Use risk assessment to select appropriate HbA1c or fasting-glucose testing and confirm diagnostic results when required.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Offer intensive lifestyle support and follow-up to people at high risk, using locally validated risk tools and eligibility.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c00bacae-ab4c-446e-8fad-855c49491948","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ph38/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Risk identification; blood testing; intensive lifestyle change","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Type 2 diabetes risk detection; not a symptomatic DKA pathway. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain diabetes screening in at-risk adults in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary Care / Public Health","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"625f0d83-3863-47f9-a64e-55c0355f3240","original_version_ids":["88eaf708-8895-48f8-be85-b3656d95ff91"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng17/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"625f0d83-3863-47f9-a64e-55c0355f3240","title":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis","specialty":"Endocrinology / Emergency Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult DKA; an up-to-date local DKA protocol must specify fluid, insulin and potassium dosing and resolution criteria.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Adult DKA; an up-to-date local DKA protocol must specify fluid, insulin and potassium dosing and resolution criteria."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["88eaf708-8895-48f8-be85-b3656d95ff91"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Insulin deficiency and counter-regulatory hormones increase lipolysis and hepatic ketone production; osmotic diuresis produces water and electrolyte loss. Infection, interrupted insulin, new diabetes, medicines, or acute stress may precipitate crisis. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Insulin deficiency and counter-regulatory hormones increase lipolysis and hepatic ketone production","osmotic diuresis produces water and electrolyte loss. Infection, interrupted insulin, new diabetes, medicines, or acute stress may precipitate crisis."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Diabetic Ketoacidosis, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Shock or severe dehydration","Reduced consciousness or inability to protect airway","Severe acidosis or dangerous potassium disturbance","Pregnancy or suspected cerebral injury"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Hyperosmolar hyperglycaemic state","distinguishingFeatures":"More profound hyperosmolality and usually less prominent ketosis/acidosis; mixed presentations occur."},{"condition":"Starvation/alcoholic ketosis","distinguishingFeatures":"Exposure history and biochemical pattern differ."},{"condition":"Sepsis or acute abdomen","distinguishingFeatures":"May precipitate crisis or coexist; do not attribute all pain to DKA."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Blood glucose and blood ketones","modalityTarget":"Blood glucose and blood ketones — Hyperglycaemia and ketonaemia","targetCondition":"Hyperglycaemia and ketonaemia","expectedFinding":"Raised ketones with the clinical context support DKA; glucose may be less elevated in euglycaemic DKA.","clinicalRationale":"Detects the metabolic emergency and tracks ketone resolution alongside acid-base results."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Venous blood gas and electrolytes","modalityTarget":"Venous blood gas and electrolytes — Metabolic acidosis and potassium disturbance","targetCondition":"Metabolic acidosis and potassium disturbance","expectedFinding":"Reduced pH/bicarbonate with ketonaemia supports ketoacidosis; measured potassium may mask total-body depletion.","clinicalRationale":"Defines severity and guides safe treatment and monitoring under the current Saudi DKA protocol."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Creatinine and fluid-balance assessment","modalityTarget":"Creatinine and fluid-balance assessment — Dehydration and kidney impairment","targetCondition":"Dehydration and kidney impairment","expectedFinding":"Renal deterioration and fluid-balance changes help define volume loss and treatment tolerance.","clinicalRationale":"Supports individualised fluid management and complication surveillance."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"ECG and source-directed infection tests when indicated","modalityTarget":"ECG and source-directed infection tests when indicated — A cardiac/infectious precipitant or electrolyte-related arrhythmia","targetCondition":"A cardiac/infectious precipitant or electrolyte-related arrhythmia","expectedFinding":"ECG abnormalities or a positive source investigation directs parallel management; avoid indiscriminate cultures.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies and treats the trigger without delaying the metabolic emergency pathway."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Measure ketones, acid-base status and electrolytes and identify the precipitating cause; seek trained acute diabetes support.","Use protocolised isotonic fluid, intravenous insulin and monitored potassium replacement; bicarbonate is not routine, and glucose-containing fluid permits continued ketone clearance."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"e8abb55b-ed40-4c5e-8f5f-1cf524e0cf42","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng17/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.10.2–1.10.12","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult DKA; an up-to-date local DKA protocol must specify fluid, insulin and potassium dosing and resolution criteria. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Blood glucose and blood ketones","clinical_question":"Hyperglycaemia and ketonaemia","expected_finding":"Raised ketones with the clinical context support DKA; glucose may be less elevated in euglycaemic DKA.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects the metabolic emergency and tracks ketone resolution alongside acid-base results.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Venous blood gas and electrolytes","clinical_question":"Metabolic acidosis and potassium disturbance","expected_finding":"Reduced pH/bicarbonate with ketonaemia supports ketoacidosis; measured potassium may mask total-body depletion.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Defines severity and guides safe treatment and monitoring under the current Saudi DKA protocol.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Creatinine and fluid-balance assessment","clinical_question":"Dehydration and kidney impairment","expected_finding":"Renal deterioration and fluid-balance changes help define volume loss and treatment tolerance.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports individualised fluid management and complication surveillance.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"ECG and source-directed infection tests when indicated","clinical_question":"A cardiac/infectious precipitant or electrolyte-related arrhythmia","expected_finding":"ECG abnormalities or a positive source investigation directs parallel management; avoid indiscriminate cultures.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies and treats the trigger without delaying the metabolic emergency pathway.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"e8abb55b-ed40-4c5e-8f5f-1cf524e0cf42","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng17/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.10.2–1.10.12","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult DKA; an up-to-date local DKA protocol must specify fluid, insulin and potassium dosing and resolution criteria. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Measure ketones, acid-base status and electrolytes and identify the precipitating cause; seek trained acute diabetes support.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use protocolised isotonic fluid, intravenous insulin and monitored potassium replacement; bicarbonate is not routine, and glucose-containing fluid permits continued ketone clearance.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"e8abb55b-ed40-4c5e-8f5f-1cf524e0cf42","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng17/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.10.2–1.10.12","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult DKA; an up-to-date local DKA protocol must specify fluid, insulin and potassium dosing and resolution criteria. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain diabetic ketoacidosis in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Endocrinology / Emergency Medicine","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"65fce08b-a289-44bd-9c91-79b2243f824c","original_version_ids":["48f54143-b376-45d6-92ae-09001b015a45"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"65fce08b-a289-44bd-9c91-79b2243f824c","title":"Dyslipidaemia and Atherosclerotic Risk","specialty":"Primary Care / Cardiology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Chronic Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Risk-based lipid therapy, with local formulary and pregnancy review.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Risk-based lipid therapy, with local formulary and pregnancy review."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["48f54143-b376-45d6-92ae-09001b015a45"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Atherogenic lipoproteins contribute to plaque formation and progression. Absolute preventive benefit depends on baseline risk, lipid level, treatment intensity, competing risks, and patient preference. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Atherogenic lipoproteins contribute to plaque formation and progression. Absolute preventive benefit depends on baseline risk, lipid level, treatment intensity, competing risks, and patient preference.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Dyslipidaemia and Atherosclerotic Risk, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Acute chest pain or stroke symptoms","Severe lipid elevation with abdominal pain suggesting pancreatitis","Family history of premature vascular events","Tendon xanthomas or corneal arcus with very high LDL"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Familial hypercholesterolaemia","distinguishingFeatures":"Marked LDL and family history support inherited-risk evaluation."},{"condition":"Secondary dyslipidaemia","distinguishingFeatures":"Diabetes, thyroid, renal/liver disease, alcohol, and medicines can contribute."},{"condition":"Laboratory variation","distinguishingFeatures":"Repeat or clarify sampling if result conflicts with clinical context."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Lipid profile","modalityTarget":"Lipid profile — LDL elevation and triglyceride abnormality","targetCondition":"LDL elevation and triglyceride abnormality","expectedFinding":"The lipid pattern and degree of elevation inform risk and possible inherited disease.","clinicalRationale":"Provides the baseline for prevention decisions and later response assessment."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Family history and vascular-risk assessment","modalityTarget":"Family history and vascular-risk assessment — Premature atherosclerosis or familial dyslipidaemia","targetCondition":"Premature atherosclerosis or familial dyslipidaemia","expectedFinding":"Premature events, markedly elevated historical LDL or affected relatives may warrant specialist evaluation.","clinicalRationale":"Determines prevention intensity and whether family assessment is appropriate."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"TSH, glycaemia, renal or liver tests when a secondary cause is suspected","modalityTarget":"TSH, glycaemia, renal or liver tests when a secondary cause is suspected — Hypothyroidism, diabetes or organ disease contributing to dyslipidaemia","targetCondition":"Hypothyroidism, diabetes or organ disease contributing to dyslipidaemia","expectedFinding":"A relevant biochemical abnormality redirects assessment to a secondary contributor.","clinicalRationale":"Tests the specific suspected cause rather than assuming all abnormal lipids are primary."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Assess full lipid profile, secondary causes, cardiovascular history and overall risk.","Discuss appropriate statin-based prevention and monitor response and adverse effects; distinguish primary from secondary prevention."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b5b625ed-5749-42c6-8d45-1dbfb60d06c0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Lipid modification; primary and secondary prevention","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Risk-based lipid therapy, with local formulary and pregnancy review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Lipid profile","clinical_question":"LDL elevation and triglyceride abnormality","expected_finding":"The lipid pattern and degree of elevation inform risk and possible inherited disease.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides the baseline for prevention decisions and later response assessment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Family history and vascular-risk assessment","clinical_question":"Premature atherosclerosis or familial dyslipidaemia","expected_finding":"Premature events, markedly elevated historical LDL or affected relatives may warrant specialist evaluation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Determines prevention intensity and whether family assessment is appropriate.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"TSH, glycaemia, renal or liver tests when a secondary cause is suspected","clinical_question":"Hypothyroidism, diabetes or organ disease contributing to dyslipidaemia","expected_finding":"A relevant biochemical abnormality redirects assessment to a secondary contributor.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Tests the specific suspected cause rather than assuming all abnormal lipids are primary.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b5b625ed-5749-42c6-8d45-1dbfb60d06c0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Lipid modification; primary and secondary prevention","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Risk-based lipid therapy, with local formulary and pregnancy review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Assess full lipid profile, secondary causes, cardiovascular history and overall risk.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Discuss appropriate statin-based prevention and monitor response and adverse effects; distinguish primary from secondary prevention.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"b5b625ed-5749-42c6-8d45-1dbfb60d06c0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng238/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Lipid modification; primary and secondary prevention","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Risk-based lipid therapy, with local formulary and pregnancy review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain dyslipidaemia and atherosclerotic risk in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary Care / Cardiology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"c5e62cae-fb6e-47ef-8681-bec748e64dd4","original_version_ids":["e13dac5e-f415-4b9d-b44d-6c510d9d6bdc"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg126/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"c5e62cae-fb6e-47ef-8681-bec748e64dd4","title":"Elective Coronary Revascularisation Review","specialty":"Cardiology / Cardiothoracic Surgery","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Planned Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Stable angina; this source does not replace an ACS pathway.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Stable angina; this source does not replace an ACS pathway."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["e13dac5e-f415-4b9d-b44d-6c510d9d6bdc"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Coronary atherosclerosis may limit perfusion and cause angina or myocardial injury. Revascularisation can improve symptoms or selected prognostic outcomes; choice depends on anatomy, comorbidity, guideline evidence, and patient preference. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Coronary atherosclerosis may limit perfusion and cause angina or myocardial injury. Revascularisation can improve symptoms or selected prognostic outcomes","choice depends on anatomy, comorbidity, guideline evidence, and patient preference."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Elective Coronary Revascularisation Review, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Acute coronary syndrome or rest pain","Decompensated heart failure","Unstable arrhythmia or severe renal injury","Active infection before an elective procedure"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Non-cardiac chest pain","distinguishingFeatures":"Reassess symptoms and objective evidence."},{"condition":"Microvascular angina","distinguishingFeatures":"Epicardial anatomy may not fully explain symptoms."},{"condition":"Vasospastic disease","distinguishingFeatures":"Pattern and response differ; specialist review may be needed."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Review of coronary angiography and ischaemia evidence","modalityTarget":"Review of coronary angiography and ischaemia evidence — Coronary anatomy and clinically important ischaemia","targetCondition":"Coronary anatomy and clinically important ischaemia","expectedFinding":"Anatomical stenoses and functional evidence are assessed together; anatomy alone does not establish benefit from intervention.","clinicalRationale":"Supports Heart Team selection of revascularisation strategy and shared consent."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Echocardiography","modalityTarget":"Echocardiography — Ventricular function and associated valve disease","targetCondition":"Ventricular function and associated valve disease","expectedFinding":"Systolic dysfunction or important valve pathology influences procedural risk and planning.","clinicalRationale":"Defines cardiac function before the proposed intervention."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Full blood count, creatinine and medication review","modalityTarget":"Full blood count, creatinine and medication review — Anaemia, kidney dysfunction and bleeding/antithrombotic risk","targetCondition":"Anaemia, kidney dysfunction and bleeding/antithrombotic risk","expectedFinding":"Anaemia or impaired kidney function may require optimisation; document antiplatelet and anticoagulant exposure.","clinicalRationale":"Plans safe contrast/procedural care and avoids preventable bleeding or medicine interruption."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Review symptom control and optimal medical treatment before considering elective revascularisation.","Use a multidisciplinary discussion of coronary anatomy, comorbidity and preferences to choose between PCI, surgery and continued medical treatment."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9b9f81fb-544f-4873-86c5-f9d1a80cf260","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg126/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Revascularisation; multidisciplinary team","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Stable angina; this source does not replace an ACS pathway. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Review of coronary angiography and ischaemia evidence","clinical_question":"Coronary anatomy and clinically important ischaemia","expected_finding":"Anatomical stenoses and functional evidence are assessed together; anatomy alone does not establish benefit from intervention.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports Heart Team selection of revascularisation strategy and shared consent.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Echocardiography","clinical_question":"Ventricular function and associated valve disease","expected_finding":"Systolic dysfunction or important valve pathology influences procedural risk and planning.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Defines cardiac function before the proposed intervention.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Full blood count, creatinine and medication review","clinical_question":"Anaemia, kidney dysfunction and bleeding/antithrombotic risk","expected_finding":"Anaemia or impaired kidney function may require optimisation; document antiplatelet and anticoagulant exposure.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Plans safe contrast/procedural care and avoids preventable bleeding or medicine interruption.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9b9f81fb-544f-4873-86c5-f9d1a80cf260","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg126/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Revascularisation; multidisciplinary team","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Stable angina; this source does not replace an ACS pathway. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Review symptom control and optimal medical treatment before considering elective revascularisation.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use a multidisciplinary discussion of coronary anatomy, comorbidity and preferences to choose between PCI, surgery and continued medical treatment.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9b9f81fb-544f-4873-86c5-f9d1a80cf260","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg126/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Revascularisation; multidisciplinary team","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Stable angina; this source does not replace an ACS pathway. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain elective coronary revascularisation review in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Cardiology / Cardiothoracic Surgery","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"2ebb8b8e-91bd-44ef-98f9-24daa70738d4","original_version_ids":["68c70995-0e63-404b-95e9-0818a28b32d2"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng45/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"2ebb8b8e-91bd-44ef-98f9-24daa70738d4","title":"Elective Hernia Repair Assessment","specialty":"General Surgery","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Planned Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Preoperative tests only; hernia-specific indication, approach and mesh decisions need a separate surgical source.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Preoperative tests only; hernia-specific indication, approach and mesh decisions need a separate surgical source."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["68c70995-0e63-404b-95e9-0818a28b32d2"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Abdominal wall weakness allows tissue or viscera to protrude; symptoms range from incidental bulge to incarceration or strangulation. Repair choice depends on anatomy, symptoms, operative risk, and patient preference. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Abdominal wall weakness allows tissue or viscera to protrude","symptoms range from incidental bulge to incarceration or strangulation. Repair choice depends on anatomy, symptoms, operative risk, and patient preference."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Elective Hernia Repair Assessment, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Irreducible painful bulge with vomiting","Skin change, fever, or bowel obstruction","Acute testicular pain or vascular compromise","Rapid enlargement or unclear diagnosis"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Lymphadenopathy","distinguishingFeatures":"Examination and ultrasound may distinguish from hernia."},{"condition":"Femoral aneurysm or vascular mass","distinguishingFeatures":"Pulsatility requires vascular assessment."},{"condition":"Hydrocele or scrotal mass","distinguishingFeatures":"Anatomy and imaging clarify diagnosis."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Standing and supine groin/abdominal examination","modalityTarget":"Standing and supine groin/abdominal examination — Hernia location, reducibility and complication signs","targetCondition":"Hernia location, reducibility and complication signs","expectedFinding":"A cough impulse or reducible bulge supports hernia; painful irreducibility requires urgent assessment.","clinicalRationale":"Defines the clinical diagnosis and separates an elective case from possible incarceration or strangulation."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Ultrasound when examination is inconclusive","modalityTarget":"Ultrasound when examination is inconclusive — An occult hernia or alternative groin mass","targetCondition":"An occult hernia or alternative groin mass","expectedFinding":"Dynamic imaging may demonstrate a defect or another lesion.","clinicalRationale":"Clarifies uncertain anatomy rather than routinely imaging every clinically evident hernia."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Targeted anaesthetic and medication assessment","modalityTarget":"Targeted anaesthetic and medication assessment — Modifiable perioperative risk","targetCondition":"Modifiable perioperative risk","expectedFinding":"Cardiopulmonary disease, anticoagulation or impaired functional status directs specific additional testing.","clinicalRationale":"Selects preoperative tests according to comorbidity and planned anaesthesia."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Select preoperative tests by procedure, comorbidity and ASA status rather than a blanket panel.","Confirm a separate hernia-specific surgical plan and assess emergency symptoms before proceeding with elective care."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"89fd5a2b-b2f1-4d63-899c-6f2fb1804d46","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng45/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Routine preoperative testing tables","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Preoperative tests only; hernia-specific indication, approach and mesh decisions need a separate surgical source. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-invest