 goals.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Creatinine and electrolytes when clinically useful","clinical_question":"Dehydration and metabolic disturbance","expected_finding":"Renal impairment or electrolyte losses may accompany vomiting and poor intake.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Guides proportionate fluids and symptom-medicine safety.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f68c7030-b134-4b46-85b0-2ed092d94f58","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Nausea and vomiting","primary_source":true},{"id":"777f11ff-c482-411e-809f-022500cfb067","title":"Small-Bowel Obstruction Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Surgical Care","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public Medscape page retrieved 11 October 2026; limited secondary comparison","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/774140-treatment","locator":"Treatment and Management; detailed prescribing not reconciled","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Last-days-of-life nausea support only; complete malignant-obstruction surgical, decompression and antisecretory treatment evidence remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Assess whether obstruction and potentially reversible causes explain nausea.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Agree comfort goals and seek specialist advice on symptom control and intervention burden.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f68c7030-b134-4b46-85b0-2ed092d94f58","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Nausea and vomiting","primary_source":true},{"id":"777f11ff-c482-411e-809f-022500cfb067","title":"Small-Bowel Obstruction Treatment & Management: Approach Considerations, Surgical Care","issuer":"Other","edition":"Public Medscape page retrieved 11 October 2026; limited secondary comparison","url":"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/774140-treatment","locator":"Treatment and Management; detailed prescribing not reconciled","primary_source":false}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Last-days-of-life nausea support only; complete malignant-obstruction surgical, decompression and antisecretory treatment evidence remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain malignant bowel obstruction support in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Palliative Medicine / General Surgery","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"1759a9d1-015f-40c7-8a11-e8e54f52991d","original_version_ids":["5a535efa-9372-4d09-b441-d26bc97bf21c"],"source_title":"Managing suspected sepsis","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng255/chapter/Managing-suspected-sepsis","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"1759a9d1-015f-40c7-8a11-e8e54f52991d","title":"Maternal Sepsis in Pregnancy or Postpartum","specialty":"Obstetrics / Infectious Diseases","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Safe Birth","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Pregnant or recently pregnant people; do not transfer the NG253 general-adult fluid algorithm automatically.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Pregnant or recently pregnant people; do not transfer the NG253 general-adult fluid algorithm automatically."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["5a535efa-9372-4d09-b441-d26bc97bf21c"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Infection triggers dysregulated host response, endothelial injury, vasodilation, and organ dysfunction. Pregnancy and postpartum changes may mask early signs, and source control is as important as antimicrobial treatment. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Infection triggers dysregulated host response, endothelial injury, vasodilation, and organ dysfunction. Pregnancy and postpartum changes may mask early signs, and source control is as important as antimicrobial treatment.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Maternal Sepsis in Pregnancy or Postpartum, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Hypotension, altered mental state, oliguria, or rising lactate","Respiratory compromise","Suspected necrotising infection or retained products","Rapid deterioration or fetal compromise"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Normal postpartum physiology","distinguishingFeatures":"Expected changes do not explain progressive systemic instability."},{"condition":"Endometritis or retained products","distinguishingFeatures":"Uterine tenderness/discharge and obstetric history support source evaluation."},{"condition":"Pyelonephritis, wound infection, pneumonia","distinguishingFeatures":"Search beyond the genital tract."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Blood cultures and source cultures when indicated","modalityTarget":"Blood cultures and source cultures when indicated — The causative organism","targetCondition":"The causative organism","expectedFinding":"Growth and susceptibility results help target therapy; negative cultures do not exclude sepsis.","clinicalRationale":"Supports antimicrobial narrowing; collection must not cause a meaningful delay to urgent treatment."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Lactate and renal/liver/coagulation profile","modalityTarget":"Lactate and renal/liver/coagulation profile — Hypoperfusion and organ dysfunction","targetCondition":"Hypoperfusion and organ dysfunction","expectedFinding":"Raised lactate or deteriorating organ indices increases concern; a normal lactate does not exclude maternal sepsis.","clinicalRationale":"Assesses severity and response alongside maternal observations and the current sepsis bundle."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Source-directed ultrasound or other imaging","modalityTarget":"Source-directed ultrasound or other imaging — Retained infected tissue, a collection or another treatable focus","targetCondition":"Retained infected tissue, a collection or another treatable focus","expectedFinding":"A localised focus may require drainage, evacuation or another source-control intervention.","clinicalRationale":"Selects the appropriate source-control plan with obstetric and relevant specialist teams."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Use pregnancy-specific risk assessment and urgent senior obstetric review; high-risk suspected sepsis needs prompt antibiotics and source assessment.","Follow NG255 for resuscitation and reassess after each fluid bolus; integrate maternal and fetal monitoring and source control."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"3f96f66e-d66d-4379-8ffe-4fca1aecdc6a","title":"Managing suspected sepsis","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng255/chapter/Managing-suspected-sepsis","locator":"High-risk management; linked fluids chapter","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Pregnant or recently pregnant people; do not transfer the NG253 general-adult fluid algorithm automatically. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Blood cultures and source cultures when indicated","clinical_question":"The causative organism","expected_finding":"Growth and susceptibility results help target therapy; negative cultures do not exclude sepsis.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports antimicrobial narrowing; collection must not cause a meaningful delay to urgent treatment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Lactate and renal/liver/coagulation profile","clinical_question":"Hypoperfusion and organ dysfunction","expected_finding":"Raised lactate or deteriorating organ indices increases concern; a normal lactate does not exclude maternal sepsis.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Assesses severity and response alongside maternal observations and the current sepsis bundle.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Source-directed ultrasound or other imaging","clinical_question":"Retained infected tissue, a collection or another treatable focus","expected_finding":"A localised focus may require drainage, evacuation or another source-control intervention.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Selects the appropriate source-control plan with obstetric and relevant specialist teams.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"3f96f66e-d66d-4379-8ffe-4fca1aecdc6a","title":"Managing suspected sepsis","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng255/chapter/Managing-suspected-sepsis","locator":"High-risk management; linked fluids chapter","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Pregnant or recently pregnant people; do not transfer the NG253 general-adult fluid algorithm automatically. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Use pregnancy-specific risk assessment and urgent senior obstetric review; high-risk suspected sepsis needs prompt antibiotics and source assessment.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Follow NG255 for resuscitation and reassess after each fluid bolus; integrate maternal and fetal monitoring and source control.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"3f96f66e-d66d-4379-8ffe-4fca1aecdc6a","title":"Managing suspected sepsis","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng255/chapter/Managing-suspected-sepsis","locator":"High-risk management; linked fluids chapter","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Pregnant or recently pregnant people; do not transfer the NG253 general-adult fluid algorithm automatically. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain maternal sepsis in pregnancy or postpartum in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Obstetrics / Infectious Diseases","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"e1586073-d5ce-469b-a54a-2eb47edb5a33","original_version_ids":["c5419b76-b03d-448d-9dfd-26bf302d48cd"],"source_title":"Medicines and surgery","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng246/chapter/Medicines-and-surgery","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"e1586073-d5ce-469b-a54a-2eb47edb5a33","title":"Metabolic and Bariatric Surgery Evaluation","specialty":"Bariatric / Metabolic Surgery","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Planned Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult bariatric evaluation; eligibility and long-term care require local adaptation.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Adult bariatric evaluation; eligibility and long-term care require local adaptation."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["c5419b76-b03d-448d-9dfd-26bf302d48cd"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Metabolic surgery changes gastric capacity and gut signalling, producing sustained weight and metabolic effects. Selection requires assessment of benefit, operative risk, nutrition, psychological readiness, and capacity for long-term monitoring. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Metabolic surgery changes gastric capacity and gut signalling, producing sustained weight and metabolic effects. Selection requires assessment of benefit, operative risk, nutrition, psychological readiness, and capacity for long-term monitoring.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Metabolic and Bariatric Surgery Evaluation, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Uncontrolled eating disorder or severe untreated psychiatric illness","Active substance-use disorder","Pregnancy or near-term pregnancy plans","Unoptimised cardiopulmonary disease or severe micronutrient deficiency"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Endocrine cause of weight gain","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess only when history/examination suggests."},{"condition":"Medication-related weight change","distinguishingFeatures":"Review treatment alternatives."},{"condition":"Severe reflux or motility disorder","distinguishingFeatures":"May influence procedure choice."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Glycaemia, lipid and liver assessment when indicated","modalityTarget":"Glycaemia, lipid and liver assessment when indicated — Metabolic comorbidity and hepatic risk","targetCondition":"Metabolic comorbidity and hepatic risk","expectedFinding":"Diabetes, dyslipidaemia or hepatic abnormality may require optimisation or further assessment.","clinicalRationale":"Defines the expected metabolic benefit and perioperative risk."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Nutritional assessment and targeted deficiency tests","modalityTarget":"Nutritional assessment and targeted deficiency tests — Pre-existing nutrient deficiency or inadequate intake","targetCondition":"Pre-existing nutrient deficiency or inadequate intake","expectedFinding":"Iron, vitamin or other selected abnormalities depend on diet, history and the proposed procedure.","clinicalRationale":"Corrects deficiencies and establishes a plan for procedure-specific long-term monitoring."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Sleep-apnoea and psychological assessment","modalityTarget":"Sleep-apnoea and psychological assessment — Respiratory and behavioural risks affecting surgery and recovery","targetCondition":"Respiratory and behavioural risks affecting surgery and recovery","expectedFinding":"Sleep-apnoea symptoms or identified support needs direct specialist review and testing.","clinicalRationale":"Supports safe anaesthesia, informed expectations and sustained postoperative care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Assess eligibility and suitability through a multidisciplinary medical, nutritional and psychological review.","Discuss procedure-specific risks and lifelong nutritional monitoring, supplementation and follow-up before surgery."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ff76d8d8-9b88-4b64-80fe-daed5ed9758e","title":"Medicines and surgery","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng246/chapter/Medicines-and-surgery","locator":"Surgical referral; preoperative assessment; postoperative follow-up","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult bariatric evaluation; eligibility and long-term care require local adaptation. Inherited