terpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Bariatric / Metabolic Surgery","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"f7b63e19-fee5-4238-a31a-f115d1beb66e","original_version_ids":["8525f8ad-f788-455c-b23d-6b62bfc67898"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"f7b63e19-fee5-4238-a31a-f115d1beb66e","title":"Nausea and Vomiting in Advanced Illness","specialty":"Palliative Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Palliative Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Last-days-of-life symptoms only; broader advanced-illness antiemetic selection needs another source.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Last-days-of-life symptoms only; broader advanced-illness antiemetic selection needs another source."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["8525f8ad-f788-455c-b23d-6b62bfc67898"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Nausea and vomiting arise from interacting gastrointestinal, vestibular, metabolic, intracranial, medication, and emotional inputs. Advanced illness can produce multiple simultaneous causes; symptom pattern and goals guide proportionate assessment. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Nausea and vomiting arise from interacting gastrointestinal, vestibular, metabolic, intracranial, medication, and emotional inputs. Advanced illness can produce multiple simultaneous causes","symptom pattern and goals guide proportionate assessment."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Nausea and Vomiting in Advanced Illness, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Bilious/feculent vomiting or severe distension","GI bleeding, severe dehydration, or electrolyte concern","New severe headache or raised intracranial pressure concern","Uncontrolled symptoms or inability to take essential medicines"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Medication adverse effect","distinguishingFeatures":"Temporal relation, dose change and polypharmacy may contribute."},{"condition":"Constipation or bowel obstruction","distinguishingFeatures":"Bowel history and abdominal findings guide evaluation."},{"condition":"Metabolic, vestibular, or intracranial cause","distinguishingFeatures":"Symptoms and focused exam identify targeted work-up."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Focused symptom, bowel and medication assessment","modalityTarget":"Focused symptom, bowel and medication assessment — Drug-related, gastrointestinal or central triggers","targetCondition":"Drug-related, gastrointestinal or central triggers","expectedFinding":"Timing, vomiting pattern, bowel function and recent medicine changes help identify the mechanism.","clinicalRationale":"Selects symptom treatment according to the likely cause and feasible administration route."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Glucose, electrolytes, calcium and creatinine when results change care","modalityTarget":"Glucose, electrolytes, calcium and creatinine when results change care — A metabolic contributor or complication of vomiting","targetCondition":"A metabolic contributor or complication of vomiting","expectedFinding":"Hypercalcaemia, dysglycaemia, kidney impairment or electrolyte loss may explain symptoms.","clinicalRationale":"Detects reversible causes and supports safe, proportionate symptom management."},{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"Targeted imaging if obstruction or another structural cause is suspected","modalityTarget":"Targeted imaging if obstruction or another structural cause is suspected — A structural cause amenable to intervention","targetCondition":"A structural cause amenable to intervention","expectedFinding":"Imaging may demonstrate obstruction or another focal lesion relevant to the symptoms.","clinicalRationale":"Use when the finding can change a goal-concordant intervention; avoid routine imaging without a decision."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Assess likely cause, including medicines and obstruction, alongside goals of care.","Individualise symptom treatment and seek specialist advice if symptoms persist or diagnosis is uncertain."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f68c7030-b134-4b46-85b0-2ed092d94f58","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.5; nausea and vomiting","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Last-days-of-life symptoms only; broader advanced-illness antiemetic selection needs another source. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Focused symptom, bowel and medication assessment","clinical_question":"Drug-related, gastrointestinal or central triggers","expected_finding":"Timing, vomiting pattern, bowel function and recent medicine changes help identify the mechanism.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Selects symptom treatment according to the likely cause and feasible administration route.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Glucose, electrolytes, calcium and creatinine when results change care","clinical_question":"A metabolic contributor or complication of vomiting","expected_finding":"Hypercalcaemia, dysglycaemia, kidney impairment or electrolyte loss may explain symptoms.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects reversible causes and supports safe, proportionate symptom management.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Targeted imaging if obstruction or another structural cause is suspected","clinical_question":"A structural cause amenable to intervention","expected_finding":"Imaging may demonstrate obstruction or another focal lesion relevant to the symptoms.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Use when the finding can change a goal-concordant intervention; avoid routine imaging without a decision.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f68c7030-b134-4b46-85b0-2ed092d94f58","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.5; nausea and vomiting","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Last-days-of-life symptoms only; broader advanced-illness antiemetic selection needs another source. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Assess likely cause, including medicines and obstruction, alongside goals of care.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Individualise symptom treatment and seek specialist advice if symptoms persist or diagnosis is uncertain.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f68c7030-b134-4b46-85b0-2ed092d94f58","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.5; nausea and vomiting","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Last-days-of-life symptoms only; broader advanced-illness antiemetic selection needs another source. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain nausea and vomiting in advanced illness in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Palliative Medicine","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"96362735-4fed-4dc9-9c7b-3a8d10d1cfbd","original_version_ids":["278c7fd1-d923-43aa-810f-7dd75bd95805"],"source_title":"Identifying and assessing overweight, obesity and central adiposity","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng246/chapter/Identifying-and-assessing-overweight-obesity-and-central-adiposity","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"96362735-4fed-4dc9-9c7b-3a8d10d1cfbd","title":"Obesity and Weight-Related Health","specialty":"Primary Care / Endocrinology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Chronic Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult assessment; medicine eligibility and surgery are separately specified chapters.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Adult assessment; medicine eligibility and surgery are separately specified chapters."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["278c7fd1-d923-43aa-810f-7dd75bd95805"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Energy regulation, genetics, environment, medicines, sleep, psychosocial factors, and endocrine disease interact. Excess adiposity can contribute to metabolic, respiratory, musculoskeletal, hepatic, and emotional burden. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Energy regulation, genetics, environment, medicines, sleep, psychosocial factors, and endocrine disease interact. Excess adiposity can contribute to metabolic, respiratory, musculoskeletal, hepatic, and emotional burden.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Obesity and Weight-Related Health, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Rapid unexplained weight gain with oedema","Severe mood symptoms or suicidal thinking","Possible eating disorder or extreme restriction","Sleep-related hypoventilation or acute cardiometabolic complication"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Medicine-associated weight gain","distinguishingFeatures":"Review temporal changes and suitable alternatives."},{"condition":"Endocrine disorder","distinguishingFeatures":"Investigate secondary causes when history/exam indicates."},{"condition":"Fluid retention","distinguishingFeatures":"Rapid gain with oedema suggests cardiac, renal, or hepatic illness."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Weight, height and blood-pressure measurement with consent","modalityTarget":"Weight, height and blood-pressure measurement with consent — Weight-related risk and elevated blood pressure","targetCondition":"Weight-related risk and elevated blood pressure","expectedFinding":"BMI and pressure provide risk measures but must be interpreted with body composition, ethnicity and the person's context.","clinicalRationale":"Establishes a respectful baseline and directs risk-focused care."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"HbA1c or fasting glucose and lipid profile when indicated","modalityTarget":"HbA1c or fasting glucose and lipid profile when indicated — Diabetes and dyslipidaemia","targetCondition":"Diabetes and dyslipidaemia","expectedFinding":"Abnormal glycaemia or lipids identifies cardiometabolic comorbidity.","clinicalRationale":"Finds conditions that influence treatment priorities and eligibility for interventions."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Sleep-apnoea, liver, mood and medication assessment","modalityTarget":"Sleep-apnoea, liver, mood and medication assessment — Associated disease or a medication contributor","targetCondition":"Associated disease or a medication contributor","expectedFinding":"Snoring/daytime sleepiness, hepatic clues, mood concerns or weight-promoting medicines direct targeted follow-up.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies complications and modifiable contributors; further testing follows the specific suspected condition."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Assess BMI, central adiposity, related conditions and the person's goals without stigma.","Offer appropriate behavioural and multidisciplinary support and verify eligibility for medicines or surgery in the current guidance and local formulary."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"1ce8f061-3da3-4f97-8f9b-8d021e0d6699","title":"Identifying and assessing overweight, obesity and central adiposity","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng246/chapter/Identifying-and-assessing-overweight-obesity-and-central-adiposity","locator":"Identifying and assessing overweight, obesity and central adiposity","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult assessment; medicine eligibility and surgery are separately specified chapters. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Weight, height and blood-pressure measurement with consent","clinical_question":"Weight-related risk and elevated blood pressure","expected_finding":"BMI and pressure provide risk measures but must be interpreted with body composition, ethnicity and the person's context.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Establishes a respectful baseline and directs risk-focused care.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"HbA1c or fasting glucose and lipid profile when indicated","clinical_question":"Diabetes and dyslipidaemia","expected_finding":"Abnormal glycaemia or lipids identifies cardiometabolic comorbidity.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Finds conditions that influence treatment priorities and eligibility for interventions.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Sleep-apnoea, liver, mood and medication assessment","clinical_question":"Associated disease or a medication contributor","expected_finding":"Snoring/daytime sleepiness, hepatic clues, mood concerns or weight-promoting medicines direct targeted follow-up.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies complications and modifiable contributors; further testing follows the specific suspected condition.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"1ce8f061-3da3-4f97-8f9b-8d021e0d6699","title":"Identifying and assessing overweight, obesity and central adiposity","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng246/chapter/Identifying-and-assessing-overweight-obesity-and-central-adiposity","locator":"Identifying and assessing overweight, obesity and central adiposity","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult assessment; medicine eligibility and surgery are separately specified chapters. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Assess BMI, central adiposity, related conditions and the person's goals without stigma.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Offer appropriate behavioural and multidisciplinary support and verify eligibility for medicines or surgery in the current guidance and local formulary.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"1ce8f061-3da3-4f97-8f9b-8d021e0d6699","title":"Identifying and assessing overweight, obesity and central adiposity","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng246/chapter/Identifying-and-assessing-overweight-obesity-and-central-adiposity","locator":"Identifying and assessing overweight, obesity and central adiposity","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult assessment; medicine eligibility and surgery are separately specified chapters. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain obesity and weight-related health in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary Care / Endocrinology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"44ad5ad7-8c67-4c70-8725-cd5ca7c34ce9","original_version_ids":["b7c14ee8-8368-486d-9a2f-46e8045b48c5"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng226/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"44ad5ad7-8c67-4c70-8725-cd5ca7c34ce9","title":"Osteoarthritis and Chronic Pain","specialty":"Rheumatology / Primary Care","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Chronic Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Osteoarthritis-specific care, not all chronic pain syndromes.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Osteoarthritis-specific care, not all chronic pain syndromes."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["b7c14ee8-8368-486d-9a2f-46e8045b48c5"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Joint tissue remodelling and low-grade inflammation interact with nociceptive processing, sleep, mood, and function. Pain intensity does not map perfectly to radiographic change; care should prioritise function and patient-defined goals. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Joint tissue remodelling and low-grade inflammation interact with nociceptive processing, sleep, mood, and function. Pain intensity does not map perfectly to radiographic change","care should prioritise function and patient-defined goals."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Osteoarthritis and Chronic Pain, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Hot swollen joint with fever","Acute inability to bear weight after trauma","Progressive neurological deficit or red-flag back pain","Unexplained weight loss or cancer/infection risk"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Inflammatory arthritis","distinguishingFeatures":"Prolonged stiffness, systemic signs, and multiple joints may indicate inflammation."},{"condition":"Septic arthritis","distinguishingFeatures":"Acute hot joint and systemic illness require urgent assessment."},{"condition":"Referred or neuropathic pain","distinguishingFeatures":"Distribution and neurological examination guide evaluation."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Focused joint and functional examination","modalityTarget":"Focused joint and functional examination — A mechanical joint-pain pattern and functional limitation","targetCondition":"A mechanical joint-pain pattern and functional limitation","expectedFinding":"Activity-related pain, restricted motion and function support the assessment; a hot swollen joint needs a different urgent differential.","clinicalRationale":"Establishes the clinical pattern and the effect on daily life."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"firstLineImaging","testName":"Joint radiograph when atypical features or an intervention require it","modalityTarget":"Joint radiograph when atypical features or an intervention require it — Structural disease or an alternative bony lesion","targetCondition":"Structural disease or an alternative bony lesion","expectedFinding":"Degenerative change may support the diagnosis, but imaging severity does not directly measure pain.","clinicalRationale":"Answers a specific diagnostic or planning question rather than routinely imaging typical uncomplicated symptoms."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Medication and comorbidity assessment","modalityTarget":"Medication and comorbidity assessment — Renal, gastrointestinal or cardiovascular risk from analgesic choices","targetCondition":"Renal, gastrointestinal or cardiovascular risk from analgesic choices","expectedFinding":"Relevant disease, interactions or previous adverse effects may change the pain plan.","clinicalRationale":"Supports safer treatment and targeted monitoring."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Use clinical diagnosis for typical osteoarthritis and avoid routine imaging unless atypical features suggest another diagnosis.","Prioritise tailored therapeutic exercise and weight management where relevant; choose analgesia according to joint, risks and response."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ffcf0b14-3df4-478a-8d9e-4f651582ca8a","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng226/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.3; 1.4","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Osteoarthritis-specific care, not all chronic pain syndromes. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Focused joint and functional examination","clinical_question":"A mechanical joint-pain pattern and functional limitation","expected_finding":"Activity-related pain, restricted motion and function support the assessment; a hot swollen joint needs a different urgent differential.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Establishes the clinical pattern and the effect on daily life.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Joint radiograph when atypical features or an intervention require it","clinical_question":"Structural disease or an alternative bony lesion","expected_finding":"Degenerative change may support the diagnosis, but imaging severity does not directly measure pain.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Answers a specific diagnostic or planning question rather than routinely imaging typical uncomplicated symptoms.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Medication and comorbidity assessment","clinical_question":"Renal, gastrointestinal or cardiovascular risk from analgesic choices","expected_finding":"Relevant disease, interactions or previous adverse effects may change the pain plan.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports safer treatment and targeted monitoring.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ffcf0b14-3df4-478a-8d9e-4f651582ca8a","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng226/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.3; 1.4","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Osteoarthritis-specific care, not all chronic pain syndromes. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Use clinical diagnosis for typical osteoarthritis and avoid routine imaging unless atypical features suggest another diagnosis.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Prioritise tailored therapeutic exercise and weight management where relevant; choose analgesia according to joint, risks and response.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ffcf0b14-3df4-478a-8d9e-4f651582ca8a","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng226/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.1; 1.3; 1.4","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Osteoarthritis-specific care, not all chronic pain syndromes. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain osteoarthritis and chronic pain in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Rheumatology / Primary Care","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"267bf607-b37b-4029-b76a-761cc3d9e3be","original_version_ids":["75ac6677-abc4-47c8-a3f6-5b88dcebd7f0"],"source_title":"Current osteoporosis guideline retrieval pending — audit only","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng259/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"Other","correction_status":"audit-only","content":{"id":"267bf607-b37b-4029-b76a-761cc3d9e3be","title":"Osteoporosis Risk Assessment and Fracture Prevention","specialty":"Primary Care / Endocrinology","authority":"Textbook","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Use current NG259 rather than superseded CG146; drug-treatment selection requires its own current evidence.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Use current NG259 rather than superseded CG146; drug-treatment selection requires its own current evidence.","Current primary guideline retrieval failed; this is an audit-only candidate, with no new guideline recommendations asserted."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["75ac6677-abc4-47c8-a3f6-5b88dcebd7f0"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Reduced bone strength reflects impaired bone mass, microarchitecture, or both, increasing fragility-fracture risk. Age, prior fracture, glucocorticoid exposure, low body weight, falls, and secondary disease shape risk and prevention. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Reduced bone strength reflects impaired bone mass, microarchitecture, or both, increasing fragility-fracture risk. Age, prior fracture, glucocorticoid exposure, low body weight, falls, and secondary disease shape risk and prevention.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Osteoporosis Risk Assessment and Fracture Prevention, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["New focal back pain after minimal trauma or suspected vertebral fracture","Acute hip pain or inability to bear weight after a fall","Possible secondary cause such as prolonged glucocorticoid exposure","High fall risk or unsafe home setting"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Osteomalacia","distinguishingFeatures":"May involve vitamin D or mineral abnormalities and bone pain."},{"condition":"Paget disease","distinguishingFeatures":"Often has characteristic focal remodelling and biochemical features."},{"condition":"Secondary osteoporosis","distinguishingFeatures":"Consider endocrine, renal, medication, or malabsorption causes."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Fracture-risk, falls and medication assessment","modalityTarget":"Fracture-risk, falls and medication assessment — Fragility fracture history and future fracture risk","targetCondition":"Fragility fracture history and future fracture risk","expectedFinding":"Prior low-trauma fractures, fall risk and relevant exposures inform the locally adopted risk estimate.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies who benefits from bone-health investigation and prevention."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"DXA when indicated","modalityTarget":"DXA when indicated — Low bone mineral density","targetCondition":"Low bone mineral density","expectedFinding":"Site-specific density scores are interpreted according to age and clinical context.","clinicalRationale":"Supports diagnosis and risk assessment; bone density alone does not capture all fracture risk."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Targeted calcium, renal, vitamin D or other cause-specific tests","modalityTarget":"Targeted calcium, renal, vitamin D or other cause-specific tests — A secondary cause or factor affecting treatment safety","targetCondition":"A secondary cause or factor affecting treatment safety","expectedFinding":"An identified abnormality directs further cause-specific assessment.","clinicalRationale":"Selects tests from the history and examination before finalising bone-protection treatment."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"assess-and-triage","title":"Assess urgency, stability, and the person’s priorities","timeframe":"At first contact and whenever the situation changes","actions":["Confirm the presenting concern, relevant timeline, baseline function, medicines, allergies, comorbidities, and the patient’s immediate priorities.","Assess the red flags above and use the current local escalation pathway if instability or rapid deterioration is present.","Explain uncertainty and involve the patient or appropriate decision-maker in a way suited to the setting."],"branches":[{"condition":"A red flag, instability, or rapid deterioration is present","actions":["Escalate immediately to the responsible senior or emergency team using the local pathway.","Stabilise and investigate in parallel; do not delay time-critical action for routine testing."]},{"condition":"The person is stable for a planned or longitudinal pathway","actions":["Proceed with focused assessment and shared planning.","Document the threshold for urgent reassessment."]}]},{"id":"confirm-and-stratify","title":"Confirm the working diagnosis and stratify risk","timeframe":"Promptly; adapt timing to acuity","actions":["Use the history, examination, and investigations listed above to confirm the likely process and assess important alternatives.","Interpret results using current national/local diagnostic criteria, age, pregnancy status, comorbidity, and prior results.","Record severity, uncertainty, and which findings would change the plan."],"branches":[{"condition":"The diagnosis remains uncertain or tests conflict with the clinical picture","actions":["Reassess the history and examination and seek senior or specialty advice.","Use targeted additional testing only when its result can change management."]},{"condition":"A high-risk complication or an alternative diagnosis is identified","actions":["Switch to the relevant urgent or specialty pathway.","Communicate the finding and handover responsibility clearly."]}]},{"id":"individualised-care","title":"Agree evidence-informed care and address the cause","timeframe":"According to acuity and current local protocol","actions":["Use the topic-specific focus in this record to agree immediate and longer-term priorities with the patient.","Select treatment only after checking current local guidance, formulary, contraindications, interactions, organ function, pregnancy considerations, and patient preference.","Treat reversible contributors and address access, communication, cultural, and functional barriers."],"branches":[{"condition":"Treatment is ineffective, poorly tolerated, or inconsistent with the patient’s goals","actions":["Reassess diagnosis, treatment burden, adherence barriers, and alternatives with the responsible specialist.","Document the shared decision and safety-net plan."]},{"condition":"The patient improves on the agreed plan","actions":["Continue the plan with monitoring proportional to risk.","Provide clear instructions for expected course and warning symptoms."]}]},{"id":"coordinate-and-follow-up","title":"Coordinate handover, education, and follow-up","timeframe":"Before transition and at the agreed review interval","actions":["Provide a written plan stating the working diagnosis, key findings, medicines or interventions, monitoring, and who owns each next step.","Use teach-back to check that the patient or caregiver understands warning symptoms, follow-up, and how to obtain help.","Close the loop on pending results, referrals, and screening or prevention actions."],"branches":[{"condition":"Safe care cannot be delivered in the current setting","actions":["Arrange a higher level of care or supported transfer and send a structured clinical handover.","Confirm transport, caregiver, and communication needs where relevant."]},{"condition":"The patient is ready for outpatient or continuing care","actions":["Confirm a feasible follow-up date and contact route.","Document when and how the plan should be reviewed or escalated."]}]}],"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain osteoporosis risk assessment and fracture prevention in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Primary Care / Endocrinology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"c52eac83-6f42-4d81-b132-40d59fa4544b","original_version_ids":["b901c360-f6de-411f-b923-df70dc5c9104"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng235/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"c52eac83-6f42-4d81-b132-40d59fa4544b","title":"Postpartum Haemorrhage Response","specialty":"Obstetrics / Anaesthesia","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Safe Birth","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Obstetric haemorrhage emergency; uterotonic contraindications and escalation require the full local protocol.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Obstetric haemorrhage emergency; uterotonic contraindications and escalation require the full local protocol."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["b901c360-f6de-411f-b923-df70dc5c9104"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Postpartum haemorrhage results from impaired uterine contraction, genital tract trauma, retained tissue, or coagulation failure. Blood loss can outpace visible estimation and lead to shock, coagulopathy, and organ injury. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Postpartum haemorrhage results from impaired uterine contraction, genital tract trauma, retained tissue, or coagulation failure. Blood loss can outpace visible estimation and lead to shock, coagulopathy, and organ injury.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Postpartum Haemorrhage Response, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Ongoing heavy bleeding or shock","Altered consciousness or collapse","Coagulopathy or rapidly falling haemoglobin","Suspected uterine rupture or retained placenta"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Genital tract trauma","distinguishingFeatures":"Inspect for lacerations when appropriate."},{"condition":"Retained placental tissue","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess placenta and uterine cavity per protocol."},{"condition":"Coagulopathy/uterine inversion","distinguishingFeatures":"Rare but time-critical alternate mechanisms."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Quantified blood loss and serial maternal observations","modalityTarget":"Quantified blood loss and serial maternal observations — Ongoing haemorrhage and circulatory compromise","targetCondition":"Ongoing haemorrhage and circulatory compromise","expectedFinding":"Continuing blood loss, tachycardia or falling pressure raises concern; physiological change may lag behind bleeding.","clinicalRationale":"Tracks severity and response while resuscitation and cause control proceed."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Full blood count, coagulation and fibrinogen","modalityTarget":"Full blood count, coagulation and fibrinogen — Anaemia, platelet deficiency and coagulopathy","targetCondition":"Anaemia, platelet deficiency and coagulopathy","expectedFinding":"Falling haemoglobin/platelets or abnormal coagulation/fibrinogen informs blood-product assessment; early haemoglobin can be misleading.","clinicalRationale":"Guides the haemorrhage/transfusion pathway without delaying immediate treatment."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Blood group and crossmatch","modalityTarget":"Blood group and crossmatch — Compatible blood products","targetCondition":"Compatible blood products","expectedFinding":"Compatibility testing enables appropriate transfusion support.","clinicalRationale":"Prepares urgently needed products through the local major-haemorrhage protocol."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Focused obstetric examination with ultrasound when useful","modalityTarget":"Focused obstetric examination with ultrasound when useful — Atony, trauma, retained tissue or another bleeding cause","targetCondition":"Atony, trauma, retained tissue or another bleeding cause","expectedFinding":"Uterine tone, genital trauma or retained tissue directs cause-specific intervention.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies the source; imaging must not delay action for clinically evident haemorrhage."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Activate obstetric haemorrhage support, resuscitate and assess the cause while monitoring blood loss and maternal condition.","Select uterotonics considering prior prophylaxis and contraindications; add tranexamic acid under the emergency protocol and escalate ongoing bleeding."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c1414a26-99a3-4d34-8533-c8954d5bffae","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng235/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.10.31–1.10.37; table 12","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Obstetric haemorrhage emergency; uterotonic contraindications and escalation require the full local protocol. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Quantified blood loss and serial maternal observations","clinical_question":"Ongoing haemorrhage and circulatory compromise","expected_finding":"Continuing blood loss, tachycardia or falling pressure raises concern; physiological change may lag behind bleeding.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Tracks severity and response while resuscitation and cause control proceed.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Full blood count, coagulation and fibrinogen","clinical_question":"Anaemia, platelet deficiency and coagulopathy","expected_finding":"Falling haemoglobin/platelets or abnormal coagulation/fibrinogen informs blood-product assessment; early haemoglobin can be misleading.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Guides the haemorrhage/transfusion pathway without delaying immediate treatment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Blood group and crossmatch","clinical_question":"Compatible blood products","expected_finding":"Compatibility testing enables appropriate transfusion support.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Prepares urgently needed products through the local major-haemorrhage protocol.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Focused obstetric examination with ultrasound when useful","clinical_question":"Atony, trauma, retained tissue or another bleeding cause","expected_finding":"Uterine tone, genital trauma or retained tissue directs cause-specific intervention.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies the source; imaging must not delay action for clinically evident haemorrhage.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c1414a26-99a3-4d34-8533-c8954d5bffae","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng235/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.10.31–1.10.37; table 12","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Obstetric haemorrhage emergency; uterotonic contraindications and escalation require the full local protocol. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Activate obstetric haemorrhage support, resuscitate and assess the cause while monitoring blood loss and maternal condition.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Select uterotonics considering prior prophylaxis and contraindications; add tranexamic acid under the emergency protocol and escalate ongoing bleeding.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"c1414a26-99a3-4d34-8533-c8954d5bffae","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng235/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.10.31–1.10.37; table 12","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Obstetric haemorrhage emergency; uterotonic contraindications and escalation require the full local protocol. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain postpartum haemorrhage response in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Obstetrics / Anaesthesia","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"040068a6-0d8f-4382-acf5-b28685eb6708","original_version_ids":["bc5f20b3-ff8b-4696-9d8e-7aee16a83196"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng247/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"040068a6-0d8f-4382-acf5-b28685eb6708","title":"Preconception Health and Risk Review","specialty":"Family Medicine / Obstetrics","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Nutrition and folate component only; diabetes and other conditions require their separate preconception pathways.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Nutrition and folate component only; diabetes and other conditions require their separate preconception pathways."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["bc5f20b3-ff8b-4696-9d8e-7aee16a83196"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Maternal health, chronic disease, medicines, nutrition, and environmental exposures can influence implantation, fetal development, and pregnancy outcomes. Preconception review provides an opportunity to optimise risks before conception. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Maternal health, chronic disease, medicines, nutrition, and environmental exposures can influence implantation, fetal development, and pregnancy outcomes. Preconception review provides an opportunity to optimise risks before conception.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Preconception Health and Risk Review, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Current pregnancy with high-risk medicine exposure","Poorly controlled diabetes, seizures, hypertension, or cardiac disease","Medication change that could destabilise serious illness","Intimate partner violence or safeguarding concern"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Infertility evaluation","distinguishingFeatures":"Different pathway if conception has not occurred after appropriate interval."},{"condition":"Unplanned pregnancy","distinguishingFeatures":"Needs timely, nonjudgemental medication and risk review."},{"condition":"Medication adverse effect","distinguishingFeatures":"Do not stop essential therapy abruptly without prescriber review."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Disease-control and medication review","modalityTarget":"Disease-control and medication review — Maternal conditions or medicines that may affect pregnancy","targetCondition":"Maternal conditions or medicines that may affect pregnancy","expectedFinding":"Suboptimal disease control or potentially harmful exposures require an individualised plan.","clinicalRationale":"Allows safer pregnancy preparation and specialist input before conception."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Blood pressure and risk-selected glycaemia assessment","modalityTarget":"Blood pressure and risk-selected glycaemia assessment — Unrecognised or poorly controlled cardiometabolic disease","targetCondition":"Unrecognised or poorly controlled cardiometabolic disease","expectedFinding":"Elevated pressure or glycaemia requires confirmation and optimisation.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies modifiable maternal risk before pregnancy."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Pregnancy test when clinically relevant and with consent","modalityTarget":"Pregnancy test when clinically relevant and with consent — An existing pregnancy","targetCondition":"An existing pregnancy","expectedFinding":"A positive result changes investigation, medicine and counselling decisions.","clinicalRationale":"Avoids treating the encounter as preconception when pregnancy has already begun."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Immunisation and risk-based infection/genetic history","modalityTarget":"Immunisation and risk-based infection/genetic history — Missing protection or a specific inherited/infectious risk","targetCondition":"Missing protection or a specific inherited/infectious risk","expectedFinding":"Records and relevant family/exposure history select any indicated further tests.","clinicalRationale":"Targets preventive care using current Saudi guidance instead of blanket testing."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Review nutrition, folic-acid eligibility, medicines and existing conditions before pregnancy.","Use condition-specific specialist planning, including NG3 for diabetes, rather than applying a single universal preconception treatment schedule."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"4337ecb4-ca38-4423-8197-31b791ed5432","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng247/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Folic acid supplementation","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Nutrition and folate component only; diabetes and other conditions require their separate preconception pathways. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Disease-control and medication review","clinical_question":"Maternal conditions or medicines that may affect pregnancy","expected_finding":"Suboptimal disease control or potentially harmful exposures require an individualised plan.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Allows safer pregnancy preparation and specialist input before conception.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Blood pressure and risk-selected glycaemia assessment","clinical_question":"Unrecognised or poorly controlled cardiometabolic disease","expected_finding":"Elevated pressure or glycaemia requires confirmation and optimisation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies modifiable maternal risk before pregnancy.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Pregnancy test when clinically relevant and with consent","clinical_question":"An existing pregnancy","expected_finding":"A positive result changes investigation, medicine and counselling decisions.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Avoids treating the encounter as preconception when pregnancy has already begun.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Immunisation and risk-based infection/genetic history","clinical_question":"Missing protection or a specific inherited/infectious risk","expected_finding":"Records and relevant family/exposure history select any indicated further tests.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Targets preventive care using current Saudi guidance instead of blanket testing.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"4337ecb4-ca38-4423-8197-31b791ed5432","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng247/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Folic acid supplementation","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Nutrition and folate component only; diabetes and other conditions require their separate preconception pathways. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Review nutrition, folic-acid eligibility, medicines and existing conditions before pregnancy.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use condition-specific specialist planning, including NG3 for diabetes, rather than applying a single universal preconception treatment schedule.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"4337ecb4-ca38-4423-8197-31b791ed5432","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng247/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Folic acid supplementation","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Nutrition and folate component only; diabetes and other conditions require their separate preconception pathways. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain preconception health and risk review in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Family Medicine / Obstetrics","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"db633270-3fb9-4b9e-97bb-4a54376ad9ab","original_version_ids":["b706ebe2-ea3a-4c73-99fa-9ddd2e0a568d"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng25/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"db633270-3fb9-4b9e-97bb-4a54376ad9ab","title":"Prelabour Rupture of Membranes","specialty":"Obstetrics","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Safe Birth","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Preterm rupture; term rupture requires NG235 and neonatal-infection guidance.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Preterm rupture; term rupture requires NG235 and neonatal-infection guidance."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["b706ebe2-ea3a-4c73-99fa-9ddd2e0a568d"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Membrane rupture before labour allows ascending infection and may precipitate birth; prematurity creates gestation-dependent neonatal risk. The balance between infection, labour, and neonatal maturity informs timing. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Membrane rupture before labour allows ascending infection and may precipitate birth","prematurity creates gestation-dependent neonatal risk. The balance between infection, labour, and neonatal maturity informs timing."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Prelabour Rupture of Membranes, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Fever, uterine tenderness, maternal/fetal tachycardia","Cord prolapse or abnormal presentation","Bleeding or suspected abruption","Reduced fetal movement or non-reassuring fetal status"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Urinary incontinence","distinguishingFeatures":"History and testing help distinguish fluid source."},{"condition":"Physiologic discharge/semen","distinguishingFeatures":"Speculum evaluation can clarify."},{"condition":"Threatened preterm labour","distinguishingFeatures":"Contractions/cervical change may coexist."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Sterile speculum examination and a validated membrane test when uncertain","modalityTarget":"Sterile speculum examination and a validated membrane test when uncertain — Amniotic-fluid leakage","targetCondition":"Amniotic-fluid leakage","expectedFinding":"Pooling or a positive validated test supports rupture in context; contamination and assay limitations may affect results.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms the diagnosis while avoiding unnecessary repeated digital examination."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Ultrasound when indicated","modalityTarget":"Ultrasound when indicated — Amniotic-fluid volume, presentation and growth","targetCondition":"Amniotic-fluid volume, presentation and growth","expectedFinding":"Reduced fluid may support the context but cannot independently confirm or exclude rupture.","clinicalRationale":"Assists pregnancy assessment and planning alongside examination and gestation."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Maternal observations and fetal heart assessment","modalityTarget":"Maternal observations and fetal heart assessment — Infection or fetal compromise","targetCondition":"Infection or fetal compromise","expectedFinding":"Fever, maternal/fetal tachycardia or a concerning fetal pattern requires urgent obstetric reassessment.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies complications that change the surveillance and delivery plan."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician 