eeded treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"26995ba0-e325-44a3-a579-c02e7656b14d","original_version_ids":["2a3c18e3-5189-4b72-847c-239e863dd5f8"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng25/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"26995ba0-e325-44a3-a579-c02e7656b14d","title":"Preterm Labour and Threatened Preterm Birth","specialty":"Obstetrics / Neonatology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Safe Birth","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Gestational-age-specific care; full dose and exclusion review remains required.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Gestational-age-specific care; full dose and exclusion review remains required."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["2a3c18e3-5189-4b72-847c-239e863dd5f8"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Preterm labour involves uterine activity with cervical remodelling before term and may arise spontaneously or from infection, placental disease, or maternal/fetal indication. Neonatal risk depends strongly on gestational age and available care. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Preterm labour involves uterine activity with cervical remodelling before term and may arise spontaneously or from infection, placental disease, or maternal/fetal indication. Neonatal risk depends strongly on gestational age and available care.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Preterm Labour and Threatened Preterm Birth, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Heavy bleeding, maternal instability, or suspected abruption","Fever, uterine tenderness, or foul fluid","Cord prolapse or fetal compromise","Advanced labour beyond local transfer capability"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Braxton Hicks contractions","distinguishingFeatures":"No progressive cervical change and symptoms may settle."},{"condition":"UTI or dehydration","distinguishingFeatures":"Can cause uterine irritability and requires assessment."},{"condition":"Placental abruption","distinguishingFeatures":"Pain, bleeding, uterine tone, or fetal concern changes urgency."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Contraction, cervical and gestation assessment","modalityTarget":"Contraction, cervical and gestation assessment — Labour-associated cervical change before term","targetCondition":"Labour-associated cervical change before term","expectedFinding":"Contractions with progressive cervical change support labour; isolated contractions are insufficient.","clinicalRationale":"Determines whether urgent preterm-birth planning is needed."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Transvaginal cervical length or a validated prediction test when indicated","modalityTarget":"Transvaginal cervical length or a validated prediction test when indicated — Risk of imminent preterm birth","targetCondition":"Risk of imminent preterm birth","expectedFinding":"A short cervix or test result is interpreted within the locally adopted gestation-specific algorithm.","clinicalRationale":"Refines risk when clinical diagnosis is uncertain; eligibility and interpretation follow the obstetric pathway."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Maternal observations, urine testing and membrane assessment when indicated","modalityTarget":"Maternal observations, urine testing and membrane assessment when indicated — Infection or membrane rupture contributing to symptoms","targetCondition":"Infection or membrane rupture contributing to symptoms","expectedFinding":"An infectious finding or fluid leakage directs a separate treatment pathway.","clinicalRationale":"Detects causes and complications that change management and the appropriateness of examination/testing."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Assess suspected labour and membrane status, using appropriate diagnostic testing and obstetric review.","Check gestational-age eligibility and contraindications for tocolysis, antenatal steroids and magnesium neuroprotection, and plan appropriate place of birth."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"6bfd445a-4481-48c0-81db-b4e6a225ac1a","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng25/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Diagnosis; tocolysis; corticosteroids; neuroprotection","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Gestational-age-specific care; full dose and exclusion review remains required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Contraction, cervical and gestation assessment","clinical_question":"Labour-associated cervical change before term","expected_finding":"Contractions with progressive cervical change support labour; isolated contractions are insuffic