nherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["e997052c-e9a4-4e61-bf65-daeede2d5a3c"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Progressive neurological disease can impair motor, bulbar, respiratory, cognitive, and communication function. Symptom planning and advance decisions should occur early while the person can communicate preferences. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Progressive neurological disease can impair motor, bulbar, respiratory, cognitive, and communication function. Symptom planning and advance decisions should occur early while the person can communicate preferences.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Progressive Neurological Disease Support, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Acute respiratory compromise or choking","Rapid loss of communication or decision capacity","Uncontrolled secretions, pain, or panic","Caregiver crisis or unsafe equipment/support gap"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Reversible infection","distinguishingFeatures":"May worsen weakness and respiratory symptoms."},{"condition":"Medication adverse effect","distinguishingFeatures":"Can affect alertness, secretions, or breathing."},{"condition":"Depression or adjustment distress","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess and support without assuming all distress is psychiatric."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Respiratory symptom assessment and specialist-selected function tests","modalityTarget":"Respiratory symptom assessment and specialist-selected function tests — Respiratory muscle weakness or ventilatory failure","targetCondition":"Respiratory muscle weakness or ventilatory failure","expectedFinding":"Declining respiratory function, orthopnoea or sleep-related symptoms prompt respiratory review.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies respiratory support needs before a crisis, consistent with the person's preferences."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Swallowing, nutrition and communication assessment","modalityTarget":"Swallowing, nutrition and communication assessment — Dysphagia, aspiration risk or loss of communication","targetCondition":"Dysphagia, aspiration risk or loss of communication","expectedFinding":"Unsafe swallowing, weight loss or communication barriers identify support needs.","clinicalRationale":"Guides feeding, communication aids and anticipatory planning."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Focused review for new reversible deterioration","modalityTarget":"Focused review for new reversible deterioration — Infection, medication effects or another superimposed problem","targetCondition":"Infection, medication effects or another superimposed problem","expectedFinding":"A new change outside the expected trajectory directs specific additional tests.","clinicalRationale":"Avoids assuming every decline is inevitable progression; investigate when the result changes goal-concordant care."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["For MND, coordinate communication, nutrition, mobility and respiratory assessment through the specialist MDT.","Discuss anticipatory and end-of-life preferences; obtain a disease-specific source for other neurological disorders."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"0b16103c-58e4-425a-8258-d7a8bbd73cc0","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng42/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Multidisciplinary care; nutrition; respiratory impairment","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Motor neurone disease only; this must not be generalised to every progressive neurological diagnosis. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Respiratory symptom as