disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Palliative Medicine / Neurology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"0fa54350-8904-4f17-a688-c1b27946690d","original_version_ids":["ab37b558-7bed-4b82-971d-3f2c03d64eb4"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng131/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"0fa54350-8904-4f17-a688-c1b27946690d","title":"Prostate Cancer Diagnosis and Treatment Planning","specialty":"Urology / Oncology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Planned Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Suspected and confirmed prostate cancer; current systemic options require oncology review.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Suspected and confirmed prostate cancer; current systemic options require oncology review."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["ab37b558-7bed-4b82-971d-3f2c03d64eb4"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Prostate adenocarcinoma has a broad spectrum from indolent localised disease to aggressive metastatic cancer. Age, pathology, stage, competing risks, and patient values shape the balance of surveillance and treatment. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Prostate adenocarcinoma has a broad spectrum from indolent localised disease to aggressive metastatic cancer. Age, pathology, stage, competing risks, and patient values shape the balance of surveillance and treatment.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Prostate Cancer Diagnosis and Treatment Planning, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Acute urinary retention or obstructive renal failure","Spinal pain with neurological deficit or cord compression concern","Bone pain with fracture risk","Fever after biopsy or sepsis"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Benign prostatic enlargement","distinguishingFeatures":"Can elevate PSA and cause urinary symptoms."},{"condition":"Prostatitis/UTI","distinguishingFeatures":"Inflammation affects PSA interpretation and timing."},{"condition":"Other malignancy or metastatic lesion","distinguishingFeatures":"Clinical pattern and imaging direct evaluation."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"PSA with history and examination","modalityTarget":"PSA with history and examination — A prostate-cancer signal in clinical context","targetCondition":"A prostate-cancer signal in clinical context","expectedFinding":"An elevated or changing PSA may warrant further assessment; benign enlargement and inflammation can also raise it.","clinicalRationale":"Supports risk assessment without using PSA alone to diagnose cancer."},{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"Prostate MRI and biopsy when indicated","modalityTarget":"Prostate MRI and biopsy when indicated — A suspicious lesion and histological diagnosis/grade","targetCondition":"A suspicious lesion and histological diagnosis/grade","expectedFinding":"MRI guides risk and biopsy strategy; tissue histology establishes tumour grade and diagnosis.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms disease and informs management before treatment selection."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"Risk-appropriate staging imaging","modalityTarget":"Risk-appropriate staging imaging — Nodal or distant spread","targetCondition":"Nodal or distant spread","expectedFinding":"The selected imaging study identifies disease extent according to the cancer-risk category.","clinicalRationale":"Prevents under- or over-staging and guides multidisciplinary treatment planning."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Discuss multiparametric MRI and biopsy in the context of PSA, examination, comorbidity and suitability for radical treatment.","Use risk-stratified shared decisions about surveillance or treatment, explaining urinary, bowel and sexual effects."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9b4e1f36-04e6-43fa-8ce4-60d29f03f81d","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng131/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; localised disease","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Suspected and confirmed prostate cancer; current systemic options require oncology review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"PSA with history and examination","clinical_question":"A prostate-cancer signal in clinical context","expected_finding":"An elevated or changing PSA may warrant further assessment; benign enlargement and inflammation can also raise it.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports risk assessment without using PSA alone to diagnose cancer.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Prostate MRI and biopsy when indicated","clinical_question":"A suspicious lesion and histological diagnosis/grade","expected_finding":"MRI guides risk and biopsy strategy; tissue histology establishes tumour grade and diagnosis.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Confirms disease and informs management before treatment selection.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Risk-appropriate staging imaging","clinical_question":"Nodal or distant spread","expected_finding":"The selected imaging study identifies disease extent according to the cancer-risk category.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Prevents under- or over-staging and guides multidisciplinary treatment planning.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9b4e1f36-04e6-43fa-8ce4-60d29f03f81d","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng131/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; localised disease","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Suspected and confirmed prostate cancer; current systemic options require oncology review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Discuss multiparametric MRI and biopsy in the context of PSA, examination, comorbidity and suitability for radical treatment.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Use risk-stratified shared decisions about surveillance or treatment, explaining urinary, bowel and sexual effects.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"9b4e1f36-04e6-43fa-8ce4-60d29f03f81d","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng131/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2; localised disease","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Suspected and confirmed prostate cancer; current systemic options require oncology review. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain prostate cancer diagnosis and treatment planning in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Urology / Oncology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"3436a68e-5207-48f6-b840-af4d87529129","original_version_ids":["dd4134e1-0579-4a83-a341-85767abdd880"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng201/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"3436a68e-5207-48f6-b840-af4d87529129","title":"Reduced Fetal Movements Assessment","specialty":"Obstetrics / Fetal Medicine","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Safe Birth","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Recognition and immediate maternity assessment; further CTG/ultrasound thresholds require specialist protocols.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Recognition and immediate maternity assessment; further CTG/ultrasound thresholds require specialist protocols."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["dd4134e1-0579-4a83-a341-85767abdd880"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Maternal perception reflects fetal activity and may change with fetal sleep, gestation, or maternal factors. A sustained reduction can signal placental insufficiency or fetal compromise, so timely assessment is important. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Maternal perception reflects fetal activity and may change with fetal sleep, gestation, or maternal factors. A sustained reduction can signal placental insufficiency or fetal compromise, so timely assessment is important.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Reduced Fetal Movements Assessment, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Absent movements or abnormal fetal heart tracing","Bleeding, pain, fluid loss, or maternal illness","Known growth restriction or placental disease","Recurrent presentation despite prior reassurance"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Normal sleep cycle or perception variation","distinguishingFeatures":"May explain some variation but does not replace assessment."},{"condition":"Maternal medication/sedation","distinguishingFeatures":"Can change perception but requires context."},{"condition":"Fetal compromise or growth restriction","distinguishingFeatures":"Needs prompt objective evaluation."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Prompt fetal heart assessment","modalityTarget":"Prompt fetal heart assessment — Fetal viability and immediate heart-rate concern","targetCondition":"Fetal viability and immediate heart-rate concern","expectedFinding":"A confirmed fetal heartbeat establishes viability at assessment; absent or abnormal findings require urgent obstetric evaluation.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies immediate risk; home Doppler or reassurance from one sound does not replace assessment."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Gestation-appropriate cardiotocography","modalityTarget":"Gestation-appropriate cardiotocography — A concerning fetal heart-rate pattern","targetCondition":"A concerning fetal heart-rate pattern","expectedFinding":"A non-reassuring pattern changes urgency; a reassuring trace does not exclude all placental or growth problems.","clinicalRationale":"Evaluates short-term fetal wellbeing through the locally adopted pregnancy pathway."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Growth, fluid and Doppler ultrasound when indicated","modalityTarget":"Growth, fluid and Doppler ultrasound when indicated — Growth restriction or placental dysfunction","targetCondition":"Growth restriction or placental dysfunction","expectedFinding":"Small size, reduced fluid or abnormal Doppler may explain risk despite a reassuring initial assessment.","clinicalRationale":"Investigates persistent/recurrent concern or relevant risk factors and guides senior follow-up."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Advise prompt contact with maternity services for concerns about reduced movements after 24 weeks.","Assess the woman and baby; do not replace assessment with a routine home movement-counting package."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"10d7b787-827f-4590-8cc5-2a59d22d6311","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng201/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2.34–1.2.35","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Recognition and immediate maternity assessment; further CTG/ultrasound thresholds require specialist protocols. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Prompt fetal heart assessment","clinical_question":"Fetal viability and immediate heart-rate concern","expected_finding":"A confirmed fetal heartbeat establishes viability at assessment; absent or abnormal findings require urgent obstetric evaluation.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies immediate risk; home Doppler or reassurance from one sound does not replace assessment.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Gestation-appropriate cardiotocography","clinical_question":"A concerning fetal heart-rate pattern","expected_finding":"A non-reassuring pattern changes urgency; a reassuring trace does not exclude all placental or growth problems.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Evaluates short-term fetal wellbeing through the locally adopted pregnancy pathway.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Growth, fluid and Doppler ultrasound when indicated","clinical_question":"Growth restriction or placental dysfunction","expected_finding":"Small size, reduced fluid or abnormal Doppler may explain risk despite a reassuring initial assessment.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Investigates persistent/recurrent concern or relevant risk factors and guides senior follow-up.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"10d7b787-827f-4590-8cc5-2a59d22d6311","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng201/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2.34–1.2.35","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Recognition and immediate maternity assessment; further CTG/ultrasound thresholds require specialist protocols. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Advise prompt contact with maternity services for concerns about reduced movements after 24 weeks.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Assess the woman and baby; do not replace assessment with a routine home movement-counting package.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"10d7b787-827f-4590-8cc5-2a59d22d6311","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng201/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.2.34–1.2.35","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Recognition and immediate maternity assessment; further CTG/ultrasound thresholds require specialist protocols. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain reduced fetal movements assessment in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Obstetrics / Fetal Medicine","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002","original_version_ids":["a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"],"source_title":"Managing suspected sepsis","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng253/chapter/Managing-suspected-sepsis","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002","title":"Sepsis","specialty":"Emergency Medicine, Internal Medicine and Critical Care","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-01-01","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"People aged 16 or over who are not pregnant or recently pregnant; NG254 and NG255 are separate populations.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","People aged 16 or over who are not pregnant or recently pregnant; NG254 and NG255 are separate populations."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Sepsis is life-threatening organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to infection. Endothelial injury, vasodilation, capillary leak, microvascular thrombosis and cellular metabolic dysfunction can impair tissue oxygen delivery and progress to shock and multiorgan failure.","keyMechanisms":["An uncontrolled inflammatory and immune response disrupts endothelial integrity and vascular tone.","Relative and absolute hypovolaemia reduce effective circulating volume.","Microcirculatory dysfunction and coagulation activation impair organ perfusion.","Myocardial depression and cellular oxygen-utilisation defects can persist despite apparently corrected blood pressure."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Fever, rigors or feeling unusually cold","New confusion, profound weakness or reduced urine output","Breathlessness, cough, dysuria, abdominal pain or another focal infection symptom","Rapid deterioration in a patient with recent infection, procedure or immunosuppression"],"physicalSigns":["Altered mental status","Tachypnoea, hypoxaemia or increased work of breathing","Hypotension, prolonged capillary refill, mottling or cool peripheries","Oliguria, tachycardia or abnormal temperature"],"redFlags":["Persistent hypotension or evidence of hypoperfusion after initial fluid resuscitation","New altered consciousness, rapidly increasing oxygen need or respiratory failure","Lactate elevation with clinical deterioration or oliguria","Purpura, necrotising soft-tissue features, meningism or a source needing immediate surgical control"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Cardiogenic shock","distinguishingFeatures":"Ischaemic symptoms, pulmonary congestion, elevated jugular venous pressure or cardiac imaging suggesting pump failure."},{"condition":"Hypovolaemic shock","distinguishingFeatures":"History of bleeding or fluid loss without a convincing infectious focus; response depends on correction of the volume deficit."},{"condition":"Anaphylaxis","distinguishingFeatures":"Abrupt onset after exposure with skin or mucosal findings, bronchospasm or gastrointestinal symptoms."},{"condition":"Pulmonary embolism","distinguishingFeatures":"Sudden dyspnoea or pleuritic pain, thromboembolic risk and right-heart strain without a clear infection syndrome."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Serum lactate with repeat trend","modalityTarget":"Serum lactate with repeat trend — Tissue hypoperfusion","targetCondition":"Tissue hypoperfusion","expectedFinding":"Elevation or failure to clear in a clinically deteriorating patient.","clinicalRationale":"Supports severity assessment and response monitoring but must be interpreted with the whole clinical picture."},{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Blood cultures and source-directed microbiology","modalityTarget":"Blood cultures and source-directed microbiology — Causative infection","targetCondition":"Causative infection","expectedFinding":"Growth or molecular detection of a plausible pathogen from blood or the suspected source.","clinicalRationale":"Enables antimicrobial narrowing and source-directed care; obtain before antibiotics only when this does not cause harmful delay."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Organ-function panel","modalityTarget":"Organ-function panel — Sepsis-associated organ dysfunction","targetCondition":"Sepsis-associated organ dysfunction","expectedFinding":"Acute kidney, liver, coagulation, haematological or gas-exchange abnormality.","clinicalRationale":"Defines severity, guides support and provides a baseline for trends."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Electrocardiogram and cardiac biomarkers when indicated","modalityTarget":"Electrocardiogram and cardiac biomarkers when indicated — Acute coronary syndrome or primary cardiac shock","targetCondition":"Acute coronary syndrome or primary cardiac shock","expectedFinding":"No primary ischaemic pattern explaining the haemodynamic state.","clinicalRationale":"Cardiac disease can mimic or coexist with sepsis and changes fluid and vasopressor decisions."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Source-directed imaging","modalityTarget":"Source-directed imaging — Non-infectious mimic or drainable focus","targetCondition":"Non-infectious mimic or drainable focus","expectedFinding":"Imaging identifies or excludes pneumonia, obstruction, perforation, abscess or another urgent source.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms anatomy and determines whether procedural source control is required."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Use the current risk-based sepsis pathway with clinical judgement, urgent senior review and timely antibiotics for high-risk illness.","When fluid resuscitation is indicated, NG253 starts with 250 ml crystalloid, reassesses each bolus and seeks senior advice if response is inadequate after 1000 ml; do not automatically apply this to pregnancy."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f803c093-e4c8-4c6f-8331-286bbe4d7065","title":"Managing suspected sepsis","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng253/chapter/Managing-suspected-sepsis","locator":"High-risk management; 1.8.4–1.8.9","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. People aged 16 or over who are not pregnant or recently pregnant; NG254 and NG255 are separate populations. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Serum lactate with repeat trend","clinical_question":"Tissue hypoperfusion","expected_finding":"Elevation or failure to clear in a clinically deteriorating patient.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Supports severity assessment and response monitoring but must be interpreted with the whole clinical picture.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Blood cultures and source-directed microbiology","clinical_question":"Causative infection","expected_finding":"Growth or molecular detection of a plausible pathogen from blood or the suspected source.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Enables antimicrobial narrowing and source-directed care; obtain before antibiotics only when this does not cause harmful delay.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Organ-function panel","clinical_question":"Sepsis-associated organ dysfunction","expected_finding":"Acute kidney, liver, coagulation, haematological or gas-exchange abnormality.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Defines severity, guides support and provides a baseline for trends.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Electrocardiogram and cardiac biomarkers when indicated","clinical_question":"Acute coronary syndrome or primary cardiac shock","expected_finding":"No primary ischaemic pattern explaining the haemodynamic state.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Cardiac disease can mimic or coexist with sepsis and changes fluid and vasopressor decisions.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Source-directed imaging","clinical_question":"Non-infectious mimic or drainable focus","expected_finding":"Imaging identifies or excludes pneumonia, obstruction, perforation, abscess or another urgent source.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Confirms anatomy and determines whether procedural source control is required.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f803c093-e4c8-4c6f-8331-286bbe4d7065","title":"Managing suspected sepsis","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng253/chapter/Managing-suspected-sepsis","locator":"High-risk management; 1.8.4–1.8.9","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. People aged 16 or over who are not pregnant or recently pregnant; NG254 and NG255 are separate populations. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Use the current risk-based sepsis pathway with clinical judgement, urgent senior review and timely antibiotics for high-risk illness.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"When fluid resuscitation is indicated, NG253 starts with 250 ml crystalloid, reassesses each bolus and seeks senior advice if response is inadequate after 1000 ml; do not automatically apply this to pregnancy.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"f803c093-e4c8-4c6f-8331-286bbe4d7065","title":"Managing suspected sepsis","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng253/chapter/Managing-suspected-sepsis","locator":"High-risk management; 1.8.4–1.8.9","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. People aged 16 or over who are not pregnant or recently pregnant; NG254 and NG255 are separate populations. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain the suspected source, organ effects and why treatment and monitoring are time critical.","On recovery, provide signs of recurrent infection or deterioration that require urgent assessment.","Discuss antimicrobial purpose, planned review and potential adverse effects."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Support nutrition, hydration and mobilisation during recovery according to swallowing and organ-function assessment.","Review indicated vaccination and infection-prevention measures after the acute episode.","Address smoking and other modifiable infection risks when clinically stable."],"mdtReferrals":["Critical care for shock, respiratory failure or escalating organ support","Source-specific surgical or procedural team","Microbiology or infectious diseases for complex infection or antimicrobial stewardship","Physiotherapy, dietetics and rehabilitation after prolonged or severe illness"],"dischargeCriteria":["Infection source and treatment plan are established with stable physiology.","Organ dysfunction has resolved or has a safe documented outpatient plan.","Oral therapy, monitoring, follow-up and explicit return precautions are feasible and understood."],"followUpPlan":"Arrange source-appropriate clinical review and results follow-up, reconcile antimicrobials and other medicines, screen for post-sepsis functional or psychological problems, and escalate persistent fatigue, breathlessness, cognitive change or recurrent fever."}}},{"guideline_id":"8091cd18-2256-40b7-8c6d-7557ac5e2fdf","original_version_ids":["81a6aa65-c80e-4a43-84b7-ce8dc5be7b03"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng17/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"8091cd18-2256-40b7-8c6d-7557ac5e2fdf","title":"Severe Hypoglycaemia","specialty":"Emergency Medicine / Endocrinology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Urgent Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Adult hypoglycaemia, with an acute local treatment protocol required.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Adult hypoglycaemia, with an acute local treatment protocol required."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["81a6aa65-c80e-4a43-84b7-ce8dc5be7b03"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Glucose delivery falls below cerebral demand; counter-regulatory responses may be blunted by recurrent events or autonomic dysfunction. Insulin, secretagogues, reduced intake, renal impairment, alcohol, and acute illness can cause prolonged or recurrent episodes. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Glucose delivery falls below cerebral demand","counter-regulatory responses may be blunted by recurrent events or autonomic dysfunction. Insulin, secretagogues, reduced intake, renal impairment, alcohol, and acute illness can cause prolonged or recurrent episodes."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Severe Hypoglycaemia, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Seizure, coma, or airway compromise","Recurrent low glucose after initial response","Persistent focal deficit after glucose correction","Suspected overdose, trauma, or inability to maintain glucose safely"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Stroke/TIA","distinguishingFeatures":"Persistent focal signs after euglycaemia need urgent neurological work-up."},{"condition":"Seizure disorder","distinguishingFeatures":"Consider if events persist after correction or history supports it."},{"condition":"Sepsis, adrenal/metabolic illness, or intoxication","distinguishingFeatures":"Consider when context or recovery is atypical."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Immediate bedside glucose with repeat measurement","modalityTarget":"Immediate bedside glucose with repeat measurement — Low glucose and response to correction","targetCondition":"Low glucose and response to correction","expectedFinding":"A low result supports hypoglycaemia; a repeat measurement checks recovery or recurrence.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms the reversible emergency and monitors treatment without delaying immediate care."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Medication, intake and renal/hepatic assessment","modalityTarget":"Medication, intake and renal/hepatic assessment — Drug accumulation, missed intake or impaired glucose regulation","targetCondition":"Drug accumulation, missed intake or impaired glucose regulation","expectedFinding":"Recent insulin/sulfonylurea exposure, poor intake or organ dysfunction may explain prolonged or recurrent episodes.","clinicalRationale":"Identifies the trigger and determines monitoring needs and recurrence prevention."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Specialist-directed critical-sample testing for unexplained recurrent episodes","modalityTarget":"Specialist-directed critical-sample testing for unexplained recurrent episodes — Endogenous or exogenous hyperinsulinaemia and other causes","targetCondition":"Endogenous or exogenous hyperinsulinaemia and other causes","expectedFinding":"Selected glucose, insulin-related and exposure assays require interpretation at the time of a documented episode.","clinicalRationale":"Investigates unexplained hypoglycaemia; sample collection must never delay emergency correction."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Treat promptly using the appropriate route for consciousness and swallowing safety; recheck glucose and clinical response.","Review recurrence risks, insulin or drug exposure and hypoglycaemia awareness; provide prevention education and follow-up."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"e8abb55b-ed40-4c5e-8f5f-1cf524e0cf42","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng17/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.9; hypoglycaemia management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult hypoglycaemia, with an acute local treatment protocol required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Immediate bedside glucose with repeat measurement","clinical_question":"Low glucose and response to correction","expected_finding":"A low result supports hypoglycaemia; a repeat measurement checks recovery or recurrence.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Confirms the reversible emergency and monitors treatment without delaying immediate care.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Medication, intake and renal/hepatic assessment","clinical_question":"Drug accumulation, missed intake or impaired glucose regulation","expected_finding":"Recent insulin/sulfonylurea exposure, poor intake or organ dysfunction may explain prolonged or recurrent episodes.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Identifies the trigger and determines monitoring needs and recurrence prevention.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Specialist-directed critical-sample testing for unexplained recurrent episodes","clinical_question":"Endogenous or exogenous hyperinsulinaemia and other causes","expected_finding":"Selected glucose, insulin-related and exposure assays require interpretation at the time of a documented episode.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Investigates unexplained hypoglycaemia; sample collection must never delay emergency correction.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"e8abb55b-ed40-4c5e-8f5f-1cf524e0cf42","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng17/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.9; hypoglycaemia management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult hypoglycaemia, with an acute local treatment protocol required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Treat promptly using the appropriate route for consciousness and swallowing safety; recheck glucose and clinical response.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Review recurrence risks, insulin or drug exposure and hypoglycaemia awareness; provide prevention education and follow-up.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"e8abb55b-ed40-4c5e-8f5f-1cf524e0cf42","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng17/chapter/recommendations","locator":"1.9; hypoglycaemia management","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Adult hypoglycaemia, with an acute local treatment protocol required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain severe hypoglycaemia in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Emergency Medicine / Endocrinology","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"e62a9981-ea21-4643-abb1-19f7ffc37789","original_version_ids":["67fd3602-4ad0-4065-8001-6b98f01f975b"],"source_title":"Treating tobacco dependence","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng209/chapter/Treating-tobacco-dependence","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"e62a9981-ea21-4643-abb1-19f7ffc37789","title":"Tobacco and Nicotine Cessation","specialty":"Family Medicine / Public Health","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Keep Well","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Tobacco cessation; pregnancy and age-specific restrictions require separate checks.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Tobacco cessation; pregnancy and age-specific restrictions require separate checks."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["67fd3602-4ad0-4065-8001-6b98f01f975b"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Nicotine dependence is reinforced by reward pathways, withdrawal avoidance, cues, and social context. Combustible tobacco causes major preventable disease; vaping is not risk-free and dual use may sustain exposure. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Nicotine dependence is reinforced by reward pathways, withdrawal avoidance, cues, and social context. Combustible tobacco causes major preventable disease","vaping is not risk-free and dual use may sustain exposure."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Tobacco and Nicotine Cessation, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Pregnancy requires tailored cessation support","Severe mood symptoms or suicidality","Possible acute nicotine poisoning","Concurrent substance use or unstable psychiatric illness"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Cannabis or other smoked products","distinguishingFeatures":"Clarify all inhaled substances and goals."},{"condition":"Nicotine replacement overuse","distinguishingFeatures":"Assess symptoms and product combination."},{"condition":"Respiratory or cardiac disease","distinguishingFeatures":"Treat symptoms while supporting cessation."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Structured tobacco-use and dependence assessment","modalityTarget":"Structured tobacco-use and dependence assessment — Nicotine dependence and withdrawal risk","targetCondition":"Nicotine dependence and withdrawal risk","expectedFinding":"Product use, frequency, time to first use and prior withdrawal define the dependence pattern.","clinicalRationale":"Matches behavioural support and treatment planning to the person's needs."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Pregnancy, mental-health and medication review","modalityTarget":"Pregnancy, mental-health and medication review — Factors affecting cessation treatment safety and follow-up","targetCondition":"Factors affecting cessation treatment safety and follow-up","expectedFinding":"Pregnancy, relevant illness, interactions or prior adverse effects may change the plan.","clinicalRationale":"Selects suitable support through current Saudi cessation services; routine laboratory testing is not needed for every cessation encounter."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Offer behavioural support and discuss suitable cessation aids with contraindication and local-licensing checks.","Agree a quit plan and follow-up, reviewing adherence, adverse effects and relapse support."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"eb6f2204-a29d-48f1-8aed-3cca4b345cc6","title":"Treating tobacco dependence","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng209/chapter/Treating-tobacco-dependence","locator":"Behavioural support; pharmacological support","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Tobacco cessation; pregnancy and age-specific restrictions require separate checks. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Structured tobacco-use and dependence assessment","clinical_question":"Nicotine dependence and withdrawal risk","expected_finding":"Product use, frequency, time to first use and prior withdrawal define the dependence pattern.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Matches behavioural support and treatment planning to the person's needs.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Pregnancy, mental-health and medication review","clinical_question":"Factors affecting cessation treatment safety and follow-up","expected_finding":"Pregnancy, relevant illness, interactions or prior adverse effects may change the plan.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Selects suitable support through current Saudi cessation services; routine laboratory testing is not needed for every cessation encounter.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"eb6f2204-a29d-48f1-8aed-3cca4b345cc6","title":"Treating tobacco dependence","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng209/chapter/Treating-tobacco-dependence","locator":"Behavioural support; pharmacological support","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Tobacco cessation; pregnancy and age-specific restrictions require separate checks. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Offer behavioural support and discuss suitable cessation aids with contraindication and local-licensing checks.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"Agree a quit plan and follow-up, reviewing adherence, adverse effects and relapse support.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"eb6f2204-a29d-48f1-8aed-3cca4b345cc6","title":"Treating tobacco dependence","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng209/chapter/Treating-tobacco-dependence","locator":"Behavioural support; pharmacological support","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Tobacco cessation; pregnancy and age-specific restrictions require separate checks. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain tobacco and nicotine cessation in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Family Medicine / Public Health","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"3f198bb7-8829-4e91-b35c-e46ad1e07eb5","original_version_ids":["44a7f25d-221b-4cd9-b487-45e5ce17b142"],"source_title":"Initial medicines","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng28/chapter/Initial-medicines","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"3f198bb7-8829-4e91-b35c-e46ad1e07eb5","title":"Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Longitudinal Care","specialty":"Endocrinology / Primary Care","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Chronic Care","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"February 2026 NICE update; local prescribing, sick-day rules and contraindications remain required.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","February 2026 NICE update; local prescribing, sick-day rules and contraindications remain required."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["44a7f25d-221b-4cd9-b487-45e5ce17b142"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Insulin resistance and progressive beta-cell dysfunction produce chronic hyperglycaemia. Vascular, renal, retinal, neural, and metabolic complications accrue over time, with risk shaped by blood pressure, lipids, kidney status, and social determinants. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Insulin resistance and progressive beta-cell dysfunction produce chronic hyperglycaemia. Vascular, renal, retinal, neural, and metabolic complications accrue over time, with risk shaped by blood pressure, lipids, kidney status, and social determinants.","Clinical expression and progression vary with baseline risk, comorbidity, treatment exposure, and access to timely care."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Longitudinal Care, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Ketosis or severe dehydration","Rapid unexplained weight loss or new severe hyperglycaemia","Foot ulcer with infection/ischaemia","Acute visual change or pregnancy with poor control"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Type 1 diabetes/LADA","distinguishingFeatures":"Ketosis, rapid insulin need, or autoimmune history may prompt reclassification."},{"condition":"Medicine-related hyperglycaemia","distinguishingFeatures":"Review glucocorticoids and other contributing drugs."},{"condition":"Secondary diabetes","distinguishingFeatures":"Pancreatic or endocrine context may warrant evaluation."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"HbA1c or an appropriate glucose-based measure","modalityTarget":"HbA1c or an appropriate glucose-based measure — Current glycaemic control","targetCondition":"Current glycaemic control","expectedFinding":"The result shows overall control in context; use glucose-based measures when HbA1c is unreliable.","clinicalRationale":"Guides shared treatment review while considering hypoglycaemia, frailty and individual goals."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Creatinine/eGFR and urine albumin-creatinine ratio","modalityTarget":"Creatinine/eGFR and urine albumin-creatinine ratio — Reduced filtration or albuminuria","targetCondition":"Reduced filtration or albuminuria","expectedFinding":"Persistent abnormalities identify diabetic or other kidney disease and modify risk.","clinicalRationale":"Detects renal complications and informs medication safety and monitoring."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Retinal assessment and foot-risk examination","modalityTarget":"Retinal assessment and foot-risk examination — Retinopathy, neuropathy, ischaemia or ulceration","targetCondition":"Retinopathy, neuropathy, ischaemia or ulceration","expectedFinding":"Retinal abnormalities, reduced protective sensation or abnormal pulses require tracked follow-up.","clinicalRationale":"Finds complications early and directs preventive or urgent specialist care."},{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Lipid profile and cardiovascular assessment","modalityTarget":"Lipid profile and cardiovascular assessment — Atherogenic risk and established vascular disease","targetCondition":"Atherogenic risk and established vascular disease","expectedFinding":"Lipid abnormalities and vascular history influence prevention priorities.","clinicalRationale":"Addresses cardiovascular risk alongside glucose control under the current Saudi diabetes pathway."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Choose initial treatment using the current comorbidity-specific recommendations and individual goals.","For adults without relevant comorbidity, the 2026 NICE branch offers modified-release metformin plus an SGLT2 inhibitor; verify renal, pregnancy and ketoacidosis precautions and local availability."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ee40a462-ffc8-433a-836d-eb734f52b0ee","title":"Initial medicines","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng28/chapter/Initial-medicines","locator":"1.13; comorbidity-specific initial medicines","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. February 2026 NICE update; local prescribing, sick-day rules and contraindications remain required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"HbA1c or an appropriate glucose-based measure","clinical_question":"Current glycaemic control","expected_finding":"The result shows overall control in context; use glucose-based measures when HbA1c is unreliable.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Guides shared treatment review while considering hypoglycaemia, frailty and individual goals.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Creatinine/eGFR and urine albumin-creatinine ratio","clinical_question":"Reduced filtration or albuminuria","expected_finding":"Persistent abnormalities identify diabetic or other kidney disease and modify risk.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Detects renal complications and informs medication safety and monitoring.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Retinal assessment and foot-risk examination","clinical_question":"Retinopathy, neuropathy, ischaemia or ulceration","expected_finding":"Retinal abnormalities, reduced protective sensation or abnormal pulses require tracked follow-up.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Finds complications early and directs preventive or urgent specialist care.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Lipid profile and cardiovascular assessment","clinical_question":"Atherogenic risk and established vascular disease","expected_finding":"Lipid abnormalities and vascular history influence prevention priorities.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Addresses cardiovascular risk alongside glucose control under the current Saudi diabetes pathway.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"}],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ee40a462-ffc8-433a-836d-eb734f52b0ee","title":"Initial medicines","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng28/chapter/Initial-medicines","locator":"1.13; comorbidity-specific initial medicines","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. February 2026 NICE update; local prescribing, sick-day rules and contraindications remain required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}],"Treatment_Plan":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Limited source correction","timeframe":"According to clinical acuity and the source pathway","actions":[{"instruction":"Choose initial treatment using the current comorbidity-specific recommendations and individual goals.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"},{"instruction":"For adults without relevant comorbidity, the 2026 NICE branch offers modified-release metformin plus an SGLT2 inhibitor; verify renal, pregnancy and ketoacidosis precautions and local availability.","timeframe":"Clinician must confirm timing for the specific patient"}],"Medicines_Doses":[],"branches":[],"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"ee40a462-ffc8-433a-836d-eb734f52b0ee","title":"Initial medicines","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng28/chapter/Initial-medicines","locator":"1.13; comorbidity-specific initial medicines","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. February 2026 NICE update; local prescribing, sick-day rules and contraindications remain required. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."}}]},"nonClinicalManagement":{"patientEducation":["Explain type 2 diabetes mellitus longitudinal care in plain language, including what is known, what remains uncertain, and how the plan will be reviewed.","Use teach-back for warning signs, medicines or monitoring, and the route to urgent help.","Invite questions and adapt written or interpreted information to the patient’s language, health literacy, and communication needs."],"lifestyleAndDiet":["Offer topic-relevant prevention or self-management support that is safe, feasible, culturally appropriate, and consistent with the person’s goals.","Avoid one-size-fits-all restrictions; individualise advice for pregnancy, frailty, kidney/heart disease, disability, and treatment burden."],"mdtReferrals":["Endocrinology / Primary Care","Primary care or the responsible continuity team","Pharmacist, nurse educator, dietitian, rehabilitation, mental-health, or social support when relevant to the case."],"dischargeCriteria":["Clinical status is appropriate for the next setting, and urgent complications have been excluded or addressed.","The patient or caregiver has an understandable plan, access to needed treatment/support, and a clear escalation route.","Pending investigations and referrals have a named owner and follow-up timeframe."],"followUpPlan":"Review the topic-specific focus, patient goals, symptoms and function at an interval matched to risk. Reconcile new results and treatment effects, close referrals, and revisit the plan if the condition, circumstances, or preferences change."}}},{"guideline_id":"cbd9f91f-e176-4601-9bf4-b4f2f7e96deb","original_version_ids":["73153c22-9308-4e4e-b0b4-a1692aeb76fd"],"source_title":"Recommendations","source_url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng89/chapter/recommendations","issuer":"NICE","correction_status":"limited-scope-correction","content":{"id":"cbd9f91f-e176-4601-9bf4-b4f2f7e96deb","title":"Venous Thromboembolism in Pregnancy and Postpartum","specialty":"Maternal-Fetal Medicine / Haematology","authority":"NICE","status":"under_review","version":"evidence-audit-2026-10-11-v1","lastReviewed":"2026-10-10","pillar":"Safe Birth","clinicalReviewStatus":"pending","evidenceAudit":{"checkedOn":"2026-10-11","status":"incomplete","scope":"Hospital thromboprophylaxis only; NG89 does not verify the complete diagnosis or treatment of pregnancy-associated VTE.","findings":["Full NICE compliance and original Medscape derivation have not been established.","Presentation contains generic template instructions rather than a verified topic-specific symptom description.","Management contains generic template steps; the correction supplies a limited topic-specific source branch.","The recorded source is a publisher/book catalogue link; it does not substantiate the detailed clinical claims.","Hospital thromboprophylaxis only; NG89 does not verify the complete diagnosis or treatment of pregnancy-associated VTE."],"unverifiedSections":["Inherited pathophysiology, presentation and differential detail","Investigation selection and interpretation outside the explicitly cited scope","Complete medicines, contraindications, dose adjustments and monitoring","Non-clinical care and local Saudi adaptation"],"medscapeStatus":"unavailable","originalVersionIds":["73153c22-9308-4e4e-b0b4-a1692aeb76fd"]},"pathophysiology":{"summary":"Pregnancy increases venous stasis and coagulation tendency while reducing fibrinolysis; risk remains elevated postpartum. Thromboembolism threatens maternal oxygenation and requires coordinated diagnostic and anticoagulation planning. This topic is educational and should be interpreted alongside current local pathways and patient-specific assessment.","keyMechanisms":["Pregnancy increases venous stasis and coagulation tendency while reducing fibrinolysis","risk remains elevated postpartum. Thromboembolism threatens maternal oxygenation and requires coordinated diagnostic and anticoagulation planning."]},"presentation":{"symptoms":["Evaluate the characteristic symptom pattern of Venous Thromboembolism in Pregnancy and Postpartum, including onset, evolution, severity, associated symptoms, precipitating factors, complications, and relevant negative findings.","Clarify onset, progression, associated symptoms, baseline function, medicines and the patient’s own priorities.","Ask about relevant risk factors and context described in the case; document important negative findings rather than assuming their absence."],"physicalSigns":["Record observations and a focused examination directed to the organ system and competing diagnoses in this topic.","Assess functional change, comorbidity, hydration/perfusion where relevant, and baseline status.","Use serial reassessment when the condition or treatment can change over hours or days."],"redFlags":["Syncope, hypoxaemia, shock, or severe chest pain","Rapidly progressive swelling or suspected phlegmasia","Major bleeding or thrombocytopenia","Labour or planned neuraxial procedure while anticoagulated"]},"differentials":[{"condition":"Physiologic dependent oedema","distinguishingFeatures":"Usually bilateral and gradual but does not exclude DVT."},{"condition":"Pneumonia or musculoskeletal pain","distinguishingFeatures":"Alternative causes of chest symptoms."},{"condition":"Amniotic fluid embolism","distinguishingFeatures":"Peripartum collapse is distinct and immediately critical."}],"investigations":{"ruleIn":[{"tier":"specializedAdjunctive","testName":"Compression ultrasound for suspected DVT","modalityTarget":"Compression ultrasound for suspected DVT — Venous thrombosis","targetCondition":"Venous thrombosis","expectedFinding":"A non-compressible vein supports DVT; persistent suspicion after a negative study requires the pregnancy-specific follow-up pathway.","clinicalRationale":"Provides first-line objective assessment of symptomatic leg-vein thrombosis."},{"tier":"advancedImaging","testName":"Pregnancy-adapted PE assessment and specialist-selected chest imaging","modalityTarget":"Pregnancy-adapted PE assessment and specialist-selected chest imaging — Pulmonary embolism","targetCondition":"Pulmonary embolism","expectedFinding":"The selected V/Q or CT pulmonary angiographic study is interpreted within the pregnancy diagnostic pathway.","clinicalRationale":"Confirms or excludes PE with an appropriate balance of clinical risk, radiation and contrast considerations."}],"ruleOut":[{"tier":"laboratory","testName":"Full blood count, creatinine and bleeding assessment","modalityTarget":"Full blood count, creatinine and bleeding assessment — Anaemia, thrombocytopenia, renal impairment or bleeding risk","targetCondition":"Anaemia, thrombocytopenia, renal impairment or bleeding risk","expectedFinding":"Abnormal platelets/haemoglobin or renal function may change anticoagulation and monitoring.","clinicalRationale":"Establishes treatment safety without delaying urgent care for a suspected high-risk thromboembolic event."}]},"clinicalManagement":[{"id":"source-scope-correction","title":"Topic-specific source correction — limited scope","timeframe":"Apply according to acuity and the cited guideline; clinician verification required","actions":["Assess pregnancy-specific thrombosis and bleeding risk for prophylaxis when hospitalised.","For suspected or confirmed VTE, obtain a dedicated obstetric diagnostic and therapeutic anticoagulation source and specialist review; do not import the nonpregnant DOAC pathway."]}],"medicationPlan":{"status":"local-protocol-required","regimens":[],"note":"UNREVIEWED DRAFT — NOT FOR CLINICAL USE. This version replaces the inherited prescribing list with a limited source comparison. It is not a complete prescribing protocol. Verify all doses, routes, contraindications, organ-function adjustments, interactions and monitoring before approval. Original medication content remains preserved in the previous versions."},"granularPathway":{"schema_version":1,"evidence":{"sources":[{"id":"a838fe14-221d-4fce-8a2b-a1011175ee47","title":"Recommendations","issuer":"NICE","edition":"Public recommendation/reference page retrieved 11 October 2026; retrieval is not clinical approval","url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng89/chapter/recommendations","locator":"Pregnant women and women who gave birth or had miscarriage or termination in the past 6 weeks","primary_source":true}],"selection_rationale":"Limited source comparison only. Hospital thromboprophylaxis only; NG89 does not verify the complete diagnosis or treatment of pregnancy-associated VTE. Inherited sections have not been re-verified; see the evidence audit. No full NICE compliance, original Medscape derivation or clinician approval is asserted."},"Investigations":[{"id":"inherited-investigations","title":"Inherited investigations — verification still required","timeframe":"Determine from the full disease-specific pathway before clinical approval","steps":[{"test":"Compression ultrasound for suspected DVT","clinical_question":"Venous thrombosis","expected_finding":"A non-compressible vein supports DVT; persistent suspicion after a negative study requires the pregnancy-specific follow-up pathway.","decision_rationale":"Inherited and not verified in this audit: Provides first-line objective assessment of symptomatic leg-vein thrombosis.","timeframe":"Not newly verified"},{"test":"Pregnancy-adapted PE assessment and specialist-selected